{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015jsSGffhFDhYcPJXDKMwSz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# DATA.md — the shape of your market data (generated from THIS snapshot at setup)\n2\t\n3\tEach day is one parquet file, `date=YYYY-MM-DD.parquet`, a full 1440-row minute grid\n4\twith columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`. `close` is the scored series.\n5\t`close` is the venue's 1-minute candle close (the last trade of that minute); the other\n6\tcolumns describe the same minute. For the Hyperliquid-routed assets each minute is\n7\taggregated from the venue's 1-second candles (first open, highest high, lowest low, last\n8\tclose), the same values as the venue's 1-minute candle.\n9\t`source`/`ingested_at`/`is_final` are ingestion provenance — ignore them. Semantics:\n10\t\n11\t- **`trade_count` 0** = no trade that minute: the venue prints a flat candle (open, high, low\n12\t  and close at the previous close, volume 0), and the validator scores against it. NOT market\n13\t  hours: these venues trade 24/7. Trade density varies by asset and era — see the table.\n14\t- **NaN close** = no price at all: before the market's first trade, or a hole in the feed.\n15\t- **Missing file** = before that market's first trade, or before the snapshot's first day. A\n16\t  context reaching back before an asset's first file starts with NaN days.\n17\t- Scoring drops NaN per prompt. Never interpolate: inventing prices in the gaps is how\n18\t  you fool your own validation.\n19\t\n20\tPer-asset coverage, measured from this snapshot (untraded% = share of minutes without a\n21\ttrade, flat or NaN, among the asset's real days; first/last 30d columns show density drift —\n22\tearly months of newer listings are genuinely thin, low realized volatility there is real):\n23\t\n24\t| asset | first day | last day | real days | untraded% total | untraded% first 30d | untraded% last 30d |\n25\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n26\t| AAPLX | 2025-11-21 | 2