{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SQ571ZFZ6dHhUpaExcsT7K","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"ChampionMiner: a generic Bittensor SN50 miner that serves one benchmark champion.\n\nSubclasses set `simulate_fn` and `context_days`, the champion's CONTEXT_DAYS — `unpack_champion.py`\ngenerates that subclass, and one that leaves `context_days` unset serves the default.\nStartup does not wait for data: a background thread warms each venue-routed minute store up, asset\nby asset, then keeps them all fresh, and an asset is served as soon as its own warm-up is done; its\ntoday's partition is refreshed after each later asset's warm-up. Each request slices the trailing\n`context_days` context — a crypto-1h one topped up with the bars that closed since the last refresh —\nand adapts the champion's output to the live validator contract. A second thread refreshes the event\ncalendar at startup and daily, and the champion finds it at `$SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR`, as in its\ncampaign. A calendar already stored on the volume, no older than `CALENDAR_MAX_AGE_SECONDS`, is\nserved until the first refresh replaces it.\n\nNo guards: an unservable asset, a data hole, or an exploding path crashes the request so it\nshows up in monitoring instead of silently degrading.\n\nDeliberately NO `from __future__ import annotations` here. bittensor's `axon.attach` discovers the\nrequest type by reading the first parameter's annotation off `forward_miner` and calling\n`issubclass()` on it. Under PEP 563 that annotation is the *string* `\"Simulation\"`, so attach dies\nwith `TypeError: issubclass() arg 1 must be a class` and the miner cannot start at all. Keep the\nannotations in this module evaluated.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport threading\nimport time\nfrom datetime import timedelta\nfrom typing import Callable\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom neurons.miner import Miner  # type: ignore[import-untyped]\nfrom synth.protocol import Simulation  # type: ignore[import-untyped]\n\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import MARKET_DATA_DIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar import build as calendar_build\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_DIR, CALENDAR_ENV, VIEW_FILE\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.minute_price_store import MinutePriceStore\nfrom synth_lib.serving.serve import (\n    FRESH_TAIL_TIME_LENGTH,\n    ContextCache,\n    FreshTail,\n    serve_request,\n    servable_assets,\n    start_time_of,\n    venue_store,\n    warm_up,\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# The champion reads its volatility off the most recent bars, so the age of the newest bar at\n# request time is a scoring cost, not just a cosmetic one. Each refresh fetches only the partitions\n# that can still change — today's, and a past day not yet settled — so it runs every minute.\n#\n# It does not run on the request path. The one venue call there is FreshTail's, for crypto-1h prompts\n# only: no retries, a short timeout, and the stored context when it fails.\nREFRESH_SECONDS = 60\n# The served calendar reaches this far back, for a champion that measures the time since an event.\nCALENDAR_HISTORY_DAYS = 45\nCALENDAR_REFRESH_SECONDS = 24 * 3600\n# A stored calendar at most this old is served from startup, while the first refresh runs.\nCALENDAR_MAX_AGE_SECONDS = CALENDAR_REFRESH_SECONDS\n# Without one, how long after startup the assets wait for the first calendar refresh.\nCALENDAR_WAIT_SECONDS = 10 * 60\n\n\nclass ChampionMiner(Miner):\n    \"\"\"Serves one champion's simulate() over all venue-routed competition assets.\"\"\"\n\n    simulate_fn: Callable | None = None\n    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\n\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)\n        if type(self).simulate_fn is None:\n            raise TypeError(\"subclass must set simulate_fn (see synth_lib/serving/unpack_champion.py)\")\n        self._start(servable_assets())\n\n    def _start(self, assets: list[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Binds the stores and starts the background thread. Returns before any venue call, so the\n        axon comes up while the data is still being fetched.\"\"\"\n        self._stores: dict[str, MinutePriceStore] = {asset: venue_store(asset) for asset in assets}\n        self._tails: dict[str, FreshTail] = {asset: FreshTail(asset) for asset in assets}\n        self._contexts = ContextCache()\n        # An asset joins once its whole warm-up window is in: a partly warmed store can end days back.\n        self._ready: set[str] = set()\n        self._calendar_root = MARKET_DATA_DIR\n        view = self._calendar_root / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE\n        os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV] = str(view.resolve())\n        self._calendar_ready = threading.Event()\n        if view.exists():\n            age = time.time() - view.stat().st_mtime\n            if age <= CALENDAR_MAX_AGE_SECONDS:\n                logger.info(\"serving the calendar stored %.1f h ago until the first refresh\", age / 3600)\n                self._calendar_ready.set()\n        threading.Thread(target=self._refresh_calendar_daily, daemon=True).start()\n        threading.Thread(target=self._warm_up_then_refresh, daemon=True).start()\n        logger.info(\"CONTEXT_DAYS %d; warming up %d assets in the background\", self.context_days, len(assets))\n\n    def _warm_up_then_refresh(self) -> None:\n        calendar_deadline = time.monotonic() + CALENDAR_WAIT_SECONDS\n        for asset in self._stores:\n            warm_up([asset], self.context_days)\n            self._calendar_ready.wait(max(0.0, calendar_deadline - time.monotonic()))\n            # The assets already served stay fresh while the others warm up.\n            self._refresh(list(self._ready), days=1)\n            self._ready.add(asset)\n        logger.info(\"warm-up complete; refreshing every %d s\", REFRESH_SECONDS)\n        self._background_refresh()\n\n    def _refresh_once(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"One pass over every store: refresh_recent(days=context_days + 1) covers today-(context_days + 1)\n        through today, and fetches only today and the days not yet settled.\"\"\"\n        self._refresh(list(self._stores), self.context_days + 1)\n\n    def _refresh(self, assets: list[str], days: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"refresh_recent(days) on each asset's store, then marks the refresh for the cached contexts. A\n        venue outage must not stop the others being refreshed.\"\"\"\n        for asset in assets:\n            try:\n                self._stores[asset].refresh_recent(days=days)\n            except Exception as exc:\n                logger.warning(\"refresh failed for %s: %s\", asset, exc)\n        self._contexts.store_refreshed()\n\n    def _refresh_calendar(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"One update of the calendar: a source that fails keeps its rows, and the champion keeps the last view.\"\"\"\n        now = pd.Timestamp.now(tz=\"UTC\")\n        today = now.date()\n        try:\n            calendar_build.update(\n                self._calendar_root,\n                today - timedelta(days=CALENDAR_HISTORY_DAYS),\n                today + timedelta(days=calendar_build.DAYS_AHEAD),\n                now,\n            )\n        except Exception as exc:\n            logger.warning(\"calendar refresh failed: %s\", exc)\n\n    def _refresh_calendar_daily(self) -> None:\n        while True:\n            self._refresh_calendar()\n            self._calendar_ready.set()\n            time.sleep(CALENDAR_REFRESH_SECONDS)\n\n    def _background_refresh(self) -> None:\n        while True:\n            self._refresh_once()\n            time.sleep(REFRESH_SECONDS)\n\n    async def forward_miner(self, synapse: Simulation) -> Simulation:\n        simulation_input = synapse.simulation_input\n        store = self._stores[simulation_input.asset]\n        if simulation_input.asset not in self._ready:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"{simulation_input.asset} is still warming up\")\n        tail = None\n        if simulation_input.time_length == FRESH_TAIL_TIME_LENGTH:\n            # Only the venue call leaves the event loop: champions keep module state, so simulate()\n            # must not run on two threads at once.\n            fresh_tail = self._tails[simulation_input.asset]\n            tail = await asyncio.to_thread(fresh_tail.bars, start_time_of(simulation_input))\n        synapse.simulation_output = serve_request(\n            type(self).simulate_fn,\n            store,\n            simulation_input,\n            tail=tail,\n            context_days=self.context_days,\n            contexts=self._contexts,\n        )\n        return synapse\n\"\"\"Generate predictions from a modeling.py over a prompt grid — the reusable evaluation core.\n\nDELIBERATELY SELF-CONTAINED: imports nothing from synth_lib, only numpy/pandas/stdlib. It is\ncopied into a champion's clone and executed inside a --network none sandbox whose venv holds only\nthe champion's own pins, so a synth_lib import here would break every verdict.\nThat is what lets it serve three duties with one implementation:\n  - the verdict runner copies this single file into a cloned champion workspace and runs it\n    inside the --network none sandbox (synth_lib/benchmark/verdict/run_verdict.py);\n  - the CI contract gate runs it on the host against any miner exposing simulate();\n  - an operator can run it standalone against any modeling.py.\n\nNo-lookahead guarantee: for each prompt at time t the model receives only what a miner answering\nthat prompt could have held. The validator issues a prompt BEFORE the start_time it scores from\n(ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS), and the store labels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t\ncloses at t + 60s and its close is the first point the prompt is scored against. Ending the context\nat t would therefore hand the model that exact value. The context ends one bar before the issuance\ninstead. The model's sole market input is that DataFrame; simulate() takes no data root.\n\nPredictions land one file per day, under\n`<out>/<asset>/<time_length>_<time_increment>/date=<YYYY-MM-DD>.npy` — float32, shaped\n(prompts, simulations, steps) — beside a `.json` naming the prompt start_times it holds, the\nchampion's CONTEXT_DAYS and `context_head_nan_minutes`, the most minutes one of the day's contexts\nruns before its first real close. A day whose file already covers every requested start_time is\nskipped, so pointing --out-dir at a directory that survives the run makes a re-score reuse the paths\ninstead of regenerating them, with the contexts they were generated from.\n\nUsage:\n  python generate_predictions.py --modeling agent/modeling.py --asset BTC \\\\\n      --window-start 2026-07-30 --window-end 2026-08-03 \\\\\n      --data-root market_data --out-dir predictions \\\\\n      --time-increment 300 --time-length 86400 --cadence-minutes 60\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom types import ModuleType\nfrom typing import Callable\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# The champion's context length: `CONTEXT_DAYS` in its modeling.py, a plain int within these bounds,\n# and this default when the module does not set it.\nDEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS = 7\nCONTEXT_DAYS_BOUNDS = (3, 30)\n# Duplicated from synth_lib.preparation.config rather than imported: this file runs inside a\n# champion's own venv, which does not have synth_lib.\nOHLCV_COLUMNS = [\"open\", \"high\", \"low\", \"close\", \"volume\", \"trade_count\"]\n# The validator's real serving size (PromptConfig.num_simulations). Empirical CRPS is biased\n# upward for small N, so scoring at fewer paths than the field unfairly penalizes the candidate.\nDEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS = 1000\nSTORE_SUBDIR = \"prices\"\n# How far before a prompt's start_time the validator issues it, per format — measured from\n# `validator_requests.request_time - start_time`. A miner answers within seconds of issuance, so\n# nothing that closes after this instant can be in its hands.\nISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS = {3_600: 60, 86_400: 120}\n# The store's bar width. A bar labelled b covers [b, b+BAR_SECONDS), so its close is known only at\n# b + BAR_SECONDS; the newest bar a miner holds at time c is the one labelled c - BAR_SECONDS.\nBAR_SECONDS = 60\n\n\ndef context_end(start: pd.Timestamp, time_length: int, issuance_lead: int | None = None) -> pd.Timestamp:\n    \"\"\"Label of the last bar a miner answering the prompt at `start` could have held.\"\"\"\n    lead = ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS.get(time_length, 0) if issuance_lead is None else issuance_lead\n    return start - pd.Timedelta(seconds=lead + BAR_SECONDS)\n\n\ndef context_slice(\n    frame: pd.DataFrame, start: pd.Timestamp, time_length: int, context_days: int, issuance_lead: int | None = None\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"The context of the prompt at `start`: the bars from `context_days` before it to `context_end`.\"\"\"\n    return frame.loc[start - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days) : context_end(start, time_length, issuance_lead)]\n\n\ndef nan_head_minutes(context: pd.DataFrame) -> int:\n    \"\"\"How many minutes the context runs before its first real close.\"\"\"\n    real = context[\"close\"].notna().to_numpy()\n    return int(real.argmax()) if real.any() else len(real)\n\n\ndef context_days_of(module: ModuleType) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The champion's `CONTEXT_DAYS`, or the default when its module does not set it.\"\"\"\n    value = getattr(module, \"CONTEXT_DAYS\", DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS)\n    low, high = CONTEXT_DAYS_BOUNDS\n    if type(value) is not int or not low <= value <= high:\n        raise ValueError(f\"CONTEXT_DAYS must be a plain int from {low} to {high} in modeling.py, got {value!r}\")\n    return value\n\n\n# What simulate() receives as context_prices: the minute OHLCV frame, or the Series of closes (NaN\n# kept) of the contract before OHLCV, for a champion written against that one.\nCONTEXT_MODES = (\"ohlcv\", \"close\")\n\n\n# float32 is what the validator stores miner predictions as, so the field's CRPS was computed at\n# this precision too. It also quarters the cache: a day of crypto-1h is 35 MB instead of 170.\nPATH_DTYPE = \"float32\"\n\n\ndef day_files(out_dir: Path, asset: str, time_length: int, time_increment: int, day: str) -> tuple[Path, Path]:\n    \"\"\"The (paths, index) pair for one day of one prompt format.\"\"\"\n    root = out_dir / asset / f\"{time_length}_{time_increment}\"\n    return root / f\"date={day}.npy\", root / f\"date={day}.json\"\n\n\ndef covered_start_times(index_path: Path, paths_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Prompt start_times the day file already holds, or nothing when it has none.\n\n    Both halves must be present. build_prediction_index skips an index whose .npy is missing, so\n    treating that state as covered here would skip generation for a day nothing can then score.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (index_path.exists() and paths_path.exists()):\n        return set()\n    try:\n        return set(json.loads(index_path.read_text())[\"start_times\"])\n    except (ValueError, KeyError):\n        return set()  # truncated by an interrupted write; regenerate the day\n\n\ndef load_module(modeling_path: Path) -> ModuleType:\n    # A champion imports the modules beside it by name, as when its folder is the script's own.\n    folder = str(modeling_path.resolve().parent)\n    if folder not in sys.path:\n        sys.path.insert(0, folder)\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(f\"candidate_{modeling_path.parent.name}\", modeling_path)\n    assert spec is not None and spec.loader is not None  # always true for a .py file path\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    return module\n\n\ndef load_simulate(modeling_path: Path) -> Callable:\n    return load_module(modeling_path).simulate\n\n\ndef store_root(data_root: Path, asset: str) -> Path:\n    root = data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n    if not root.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"no minute store for {asset}: {root} does not exist\")\n    return root\n\n\ndef load_minute_prices(data_root: Path, asset: str, start: pd.Timestamp, end: pd.Timestamp) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Minute OHLCV over [start, end] from daily partitions.\n\n    The days before the asset's first partition, before the market's first trade or the store's first\n    day, are NaN on every minute, as in a live context. A missing partition after it raises: a silent\n    hole here would shrink every context that spans it without anyone noticing.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(data_root, asset)\n    stored = (date.fromisoformat(p.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\")) for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\"))\n    first_day = min(stored, default=start.date())\n    frames = []\n    day = max(start.date(), first_day)\n    while day <= end.date():\n        path = root / f\"date={day.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n        if not path.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"missing partition {path}\")\n        try:\n            frames.append(pd.read_parquet(path, columns=[\"timestamp\", *OHLCV_COLUMNS]))\n        except ValueError as exc:  # pyarrow's ArrowInvalid, on a column the file lacks\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{path} predates the OHLCV columns. Re-ingest with --force-refresh: ingest_day \"\n                f\"skips settled partitions that already exist.\"\n            ) from exc\n        day += timedelta(days=1)\n    if not frames:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\n            f\"no partition for {asset} from {start.date()} to {end.date()}: its first is {first_day}\"\n        )\n    frame = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n    frame[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(frame[\"timestamp\"], utc=True)\n    frame = frame.set_index(\"timestamp\").sort_index()\n    if start.date() < first_day:\n        head = pd.date_range(\n            pd.Timestamp(start.date(), tz=\"UTC\"), frame.index[0], freq=\"1min\", inclusive=\"left\", name=\"timestamp\"\n        )\n        frame = pd.concat([pd.DataFrame(np.nan, index=head, columns=OHLCV_COLUMNS), frame])\n    return frame.loc[start:end]\n\n\ndef prompt_grid(\n    window_start: pd.Timestamp,\n    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n    cadence_minutes: int,\n    prompt_times: list[pd.Timestamp] | None = None,\n) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n    \"\"\"Prompts in [start, end). Filtered with `t < window_end` rather than [:-1] so a window_end\n    not aligned to the cadence does not drop the last valid prompt.\n\n    `prompt_times` replaces the even grid with an explicit list — the start_times the validator\n    actually prompted at, which sit at arbitrary minutes.\"\"\"\n    grid = (\n        prompt_times\n        if prompt_times is not None\n        else pd.date_range(window_start, window_end, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", tz=\"UTC\")\n    )\n    return [t for t in grid if window_start <= t < window_end]\n\n\ndef generate_day(\n    simulate_fn: Callable,\n    asset: str,\n    day: str,\n    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n    price_frame: pd.DataFrame,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    time_increment: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    num_simulations: int,\n    issuance_lead: int | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Generate one day's prompts and write the pair. Returns how many were generated, 0 if the\n    day was already covered.\n\n    A day is written whole: if anything is missing it is all regenerated, so a file always holds\n    exactly the start_times its index names and an interrupted run cannot leave a half-day behind.\n    \"\"\"\n    paths_file, index_file = day_files(out_dir, asset, time_length, time_increment, day)\n    wanted = [t.isoformat() for t in times]\n    if not set(wanted) - covered_start_times(index_file, paths_file):\n        return 0\n\n    runs = []\n    head = 0\n    for t in times:\n        # THE no-lookahead line: the context stops at the last bar the prompt's issuance allows,\n        # never at t — the bar labelled t closes after the prompt starts.\n        context = context_slice(price_frame, t, time_length, context_days, issuance_lead)\n        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n        if context_mode == \"close\":\n            context = context[\"close\"]\n        out = simulate_fn(\n            asset=asset,\n            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n            context_prices=context,\n        )\n        runs.append(np.asarray(out[2:], dtype=PATH_DTYPE))\n\n    paths_file.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    stacked = np.stack(runs)\n    np.save(paths_file, stacked)\n    index_file.write_text(\n        json.dumps(\n            {\n                \"start_times\": wanted,\n                \"asset\": asset,\n                \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n                \"time_length\": time_length,\n                \"num_simulations\": int(stacked.shape[1]),\n                \"num_steps\": int(stacked.shape[2]),\n                \"context_days\": context_days,\n                \"context_head_nan_minutes\": head,\n            }\n        )\n    )\n    return len(times)\n\n\ndef generate(\n    simulate_fn: Callable,\n    asset: str,\n    window_start: pd.Timestamp,\n    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n    price_frame: pd.DataFrame,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    cadence_minutes: int,\n    time_increment: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    num_simulations: int = DEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS,\n    prompt_times: list[pd.Timestamp] | None = None,\n    issuance_lead: int | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS,\n) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Returns (generated, reused) prompt counts.\"\"\"\n    by_day: dict[str, list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n    for t in prompt_grid(window_start, window_end, cadence_minutes, prompt_times):\n        by_day.setdefault(t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"), []).append(t)\n\n    generated = reused = 0\n    for day, times in sorted(by_day.items()):\n        made = generate_day(\n            simulate_fn,\n            asset,\n            day,\n            times,\n            price_frame,\n            out_dir,\n            time_increment,\n            time_length,\n            num_simulations,\n            issuance_lead,\n            context_mode,\n            context_days,\n        )\n        generated += made\n        reused += 0 if made else len(times)\n    return generated, reused\n\n\ndef _utc(value: str) -> pd.Timestamp:\n    ts = pd.Timestamp(value)\n    return ts.tz_localize(\"UTC\") if ts.tzinfo is None else ts.tz_convert(\"UTC\")\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--modeling\", required=True, type=Path)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-start\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-end\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data-root\", required=True, type=Path)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out-dir\", required=True, type=Path)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--cadence-minutes\", type=int, required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--num-simulations\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS)\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--issuance-lead-seconds\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=f\"override how far before start_time the prompt is issued (default per format: \"\n        f\"{ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS})\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--context\",\n        choices=CONTEXT_MODES,\n        default=\"ohlcv\",\n        help=\"context_prices as the minute OHLCV frame, or as the Series of closes a champion written \"\n        \"before the OHLCV context expects\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--prompt-times\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"JSON list of ISO start_times to generate at, instead of the --cadence-minutes grid\",\n    )\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    start, end = _utc(args.window_start), _utc(args.window_end)\n    prompt_times = None\n    if args.prompt_times is not None:\n        prompt_times = [_utc(t) for t in json.loads(args.prompt_times.read_text())]\n    module = load_module(args.modeling)\n    days = context_days_of(module)\n    prices = load_minute_prices(args.data_root, args.asset, start - pd.Timedelta(days=days), end)\n    generated, reused = generate(\n        module.simulate,\n        args.asset,\n        start,\n        end,\n        prices,\n        args.out_dir,\n        cadence_minutes=args.cadence_minutes,\n        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n        time_length=args.time_length,\n        num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n        prompt_times=prompt_times,\n        issuance_lead=args.issuance_lead_seconds,\n        context_mode=args.context,\n        context_days=days,\n    )\n    print(f\"{args.asset} tl={args.time_length}: {generated} predictions ({reused} reused), CONTEXT_DAYS {days}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"2798ef8e-7446-4f12-8f29-5a0f8f97bed4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:14:58.152Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"ChampionMiner: a generic Bittensor SN50 miner that serves one benchmark champion.\n\nSubclasses set `simulate_fn` and `context_days`, the champion's CONTEXT_DAYS — `unpack_champion.py`\ngenerates that subclass, and one that leaves `context_days` unset serves the default.\nStartup does not wait for data: a background thread warms each venue-routed minute store up, asset\nby asset, then keeps them all fresh, and an asset is served as soon as its own warm-up is done; its\ntoday's partition is refreshed after each later asset's warm-up. Each request slices the trailing\n`context_days` context — a crypto-1h one topped up with the bars that closed since the last refresh —\nand adapts the champion's output to the live validator contract. A second thread refreshes the event\ncalendar at startup and daily, and the champion finds it at `$SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR`, as in its\ncampaign. A calendar already stored on the volume, no older than `CALENDAR_MAX_AGE_SECONDS`, is\nserved until the first refresh replaces it.\n\nNo guards: an unservable asset, a data hole, or an exploding path crashes the request so it\nshows up in monitoring instead of silently degrading.\n\nDeliberately NO `from __future__ import annotations` here. bittensor's `axon.attach` discovers the\nrequest type by reading the first parameter's annotation off `forward_miner` and calling\n`issubclass()` on it. Under PEP 563 that annotation is the *string* `\"Simulation\"`, so attach dies\nwith `TypeError: issubclass() arg 1 must be a class` and the miner cannot start at all. Keep the\nannotations in this module evaluated.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport logging\nimport os\nimport threading\nimport time\nfrom datetime import timedelta\nfrom typing import Callable\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom neurons.miner import Miner  # type: ignore[import-untyped]\nfrom synth.protocol import Simulation  # type: ignore[import-untyped]\n\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import MARKET_DATA_DIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar import build as calendar_build\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_DIR, CALENDAR_ENV, VIEW_FILE\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.minute_price_store import MinutePriceStore\nfrom synth_lib.serving.serve import (\n    FRESH_TAIL_TIME_LENGTH,\n    ContextCache,\n    FreshTail,\n    serve_request,\n    servable_assets,\n    start_time_of,\n    venue_store,\n    warm_up,\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# The champion reads its volatility off the most recent bars, so the age of the newest bar at\n# request time is a scoring cost, not just a cosmetic one. Each refresh fetches only the partitions\n# that can still change — today's, and a past day not yet settled — so it runs every minute.\n#\n# It does not run on the request path. The one venue call there is FreshTail's, for crypto-1h prompts\n# only: no retries, a short timeout, and the stored context when it fails.\nREFRESH_SECONDS = 60\n# The served calendar reaches this far back, for a champion that measures the time since an event.\nCALENDAR_HISTORY_DAYS = 45\nCALENDAR_REFRESH_SECONDS = 24 * 3600\n# A stored calendar at most this old is served from startup, while the first refresh runs.\nCALENDAR_MAX_AGE_SECONDS = CALENDAR_REFRESH_SECONDS\n# Without one, how long after startup the assets wait for the first calendar refresh.\nCALENDAR_WAIT_SECONDS = 10 * 60\n\n\nclass ChampionMiner(Miner):\n    \"\"\"Serves one champion's simulate() over all venue-routed competition assets.\"\"\"\n\n    simulate_fn: Callable | None = None\n    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\n\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)\n        if type(self).simulate_fn is None:\n            raise TypeError(\"subclass must set simulate_fn (see synth_lib/serving/unpack_champion.py)\")\n        self._start(servable_assets())\n\n    def _start(self, assets: list[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Binds the stores and starts the background thread. Returns before any venue call, so the\n        axon comes up while the data is still being fetched.\"\"\"\n        self._stores: dict[str, MinutePriceStore] = {asset: venue_store(asset) for asset in assets}\n        self._tails: dict[str, FreshTail] = {asset: FreshTail(asset) for asset in assets}\n        self._contexts = ContextCache()\n        # An asset joins once its whole warm-up window is in: a partly warmed store can end days back.\n        self._ready: set[str] = set()\n        self._calendar_root = MARKET_DATA_DIR\n        view = self._calendar_root / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE\n        os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV] = str(view.resolve())\n        self._calendar_ready = threading.Event()\n        if view.exists():\n            age = time.time() - view.stat().st_mtime\n            if age <= CALENDAR_MAX_AGE_SECONDS:\n                logger.info(\"serving the calendar stored %.1f h ago until the first refresh\", age / 3600)\n                self._calendar_ready.set()\n        threading.Thread(target=self._refresh_calendar_daily, daemon=True).start()\n        threading.Thread(target=self._warm_up_then_refresh, daemon=True).start()\n        logger.info(\"CONTEXT_DAYS %d; warming up %d assets in the background\", self.context_days, len(assets))\n\n    def _warm_up_then_refresh(self) -> None:\n        calendar_deadline = time.monotonic() + CALENDAR_WAIT_SECONDS\n        for asset in self._stores:\n            warm_up([asset], self.context_days)\n            self._calendar_ready.wait(max(0.0, calendar_deadline - time.monotonic()))\n            # The assets already served stay fresh while the others warm up.\n            self._refresh(list(self._ready), days=1)\n            self._ready.add(asset)\n        logger.info(\"warm-up complete; refreshing every %d s\", REFRESH_SECONDS)\n        self._background_refresh()\n\n    def _refresh_once(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"One pass over every store: refresh_recent(days=context_days + 1) covers today-(context_days + 1)\n        through today, and fetches only today and the days not yet settled.\"\"\"\n        self._refresh(list(self._stores), self.context_days + 1)\n\n    def _refresh(self, assets: list[str], days: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"refresh_recent(days) on each asset's store, then marks the refresh for the cached contexts. A\n        venue outage must not stop the others being refreshed.\"\"\"\n        for asset in assets:\n            try:\n                self._stores[asset].refresh_recent(days=days)\n            except Exception as exc:\n                logger.warning(\"refresh failed for %s: %s\", asset, exc)\n        self._contexts.store_refreshed()\n\n    def _refresh_calendar(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"One update of the calendar: a source that fails keeps its rows, and the champion keeps the last view.\"\"\"\n        now = pd.Timestamp.now(tz=\"UTC\")\n        today = now.date()\n        try:\n            calendar_build.update(\n                self._calendar_root,\n                today - timedelta(days=CALENDAR_HISTORY_DAYS),\n                today + timedelta(days=calendar_build.DAYS_AHEAD),\n                now,\n            )\n        except Exception as exc:\n            logger.warning(\"calendar refresh failed: %s\", exc)\n\n    def _refresh_calendar_daily(self) -> None:\n        while True:\n            self._refresh_calendar()\n            self._calendar_ready.set()\n            time.sleep(CALENDAR_REFRESH_SECONDS)\n\n    def _background_refresh(self) -> None:\n        while True:\n            self._refresh_once()\n            time.sleep(REFRESH_SECONDS)\n\n    async def forward_miner(self, synapse: Simulation) -> Simulation:\n        simulation_input = synapse.simulation_input\n        store = self._stores[simulation_input.asset]\n        if simulation_input.asset not in self._ready:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"{simulation_input.asset} is still warming up\")\n        tail = None\n        if simulation_input.time_length == FRESH_TAIL_TIME_LENGTH:\n            # Only the venue call leaves the event loop: champions keep module state, so simulate()\n            # must not run on two threads at once.\n            fresh_tail = self._tails[simulation_input.asset]\n            tail = await asyncio.to_thread(fresh_tail.bars, start_time_of(simulation_input))\n        synapse.simulation_output = serve_request(\n            type(self).simulate_fn,\n            store,\n            simulation_input,\n            tail=tail,\n            context_days=self.context_days,\n            contexts=self._contexts,\n        )\n        return synapse\n\"\"\"Generate predictions from a modeling.py over a prompt grid — the reusable evaluation core.\n\nDELIBERATELY SELF-CONTAINED: imports nothing from synth_lib, only numpy/pandas/stdlib. It is\ncopied into a champion's clone and executed inside a --network none sandbox whose venv holds only\nthe champion's own pins, so a synth_lib import here would break every verdict.\nThat is what lets it serve three duties with one implementation:\n  - the verdict runner copies this single file into a cloned champion workspace and runs it\n    inside the --network none sandbox (synth_lib/benchmark/verdict/run_verdict.py);\n  - the CI contract gate runs it on the host against any miner exposing simulate();\n  - an operator can run it standalone against any modeling.py.\n\nNo-lookahead guarantee: for each prompt at time t the model receives only what a miner answering\nthat prompt could have held. The validator issues a prompt BEFORE the start_time it scores from\n(ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS), and the store labels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t\ncloses at t + 60s and its close is the first point the prompt is scored against. Ending the context\nat t would therefore hand the model that exact value. The context ends one bar before the issuance\ninstead. The model's sole market input is that DataFrame; simulate() takes no data root.\n\nPredictions land one file per day, under\n`<out>/<asset>/<time_length>_<time_increment>/date=<YYYY-MM-DD>.npy` — float32, shaped\n(prompts, simulations, steps) — beside a `.json` naming the prompt start_times it holds, the\nchampion's CONTEXT_DAYS and `context_head_nan_minutes`, the most minutes one of the day's contexts\nruns before its first real close. A day whose file already covers every requested start_time is\nskipped, so pointing --out-dir at a directory that survives the run makes a re-score reuse the paths\ninstead of regenerating them, with the contexts they were generated from.\n\nUsage:\n  python generate_predictions.py --modeling agent/modeling.py --asset BTC \\\\\n      --window-start 2026-07-30 --window-end 2026-08-03 \\\\\n      --data-root market_data --out-dir predictions \\\\\n      --time-increment 300 --time-length 86400 --cadence-minutes 60\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom types import ModuleType\nfrom typing import Callable\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# The champion's context length: `CONTEXT_DAYS` in its modeling.py, a plain int within these bounds,\n# and this default when the module does not set it.\nDEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS = 7\nCONTEXT_DAYS_BOUNDS = (3, 30)\n# Duplicated from synth_lib.preparation.config rather than imported: this file runs inside a\n# champion's own venv, which does not have synth_lib.\nOHLCV_COLUMNS = [\"open\", \"high\", \"low\", \"close\", \"volume\", \"trade_count\"]\n# The validator's real serving size (PromptConfig.num_simulations). Empirical CRPS is biased\n# upward for small N, so scoring at fewer paths than the field unfairly penalizes the candidate.\nDEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS = 1000\nSTORE_SUBDIR = \"prices\"\n# How far before a prompt's start_time the validator issues it, per format — measured from\n# `validator_requests.request_time - start_time`. A miner answers within seconds of issuance, so\n# nothing that closes after this instant can be in its hands.\nISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS = {3_600: 60, 86_400: 120}\n# The store's bar width. A bar labelled b covers [b, b+BAR_SECONDS), so its close is known only at\n# b + BAR_SECONDS; the newest bar a miner holds at time c is the one labelled c - BAR_SECONDS.\nBAR_SECONDS = 60\n\n\ndef context_end(start: pd.Timestamp, time_length: int, issuance_lead: int | None = None) -> pd.Timestamp:\n    \"\"\"Label of the last bar a miner answering the prompt at `start` could have held.\"\"\"\n    lead = ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS.get(time_length, 0) if issuance_lead is None else issuance_lead\n    return start - pd.Timedelta(seconds=lead + BAR_SECONDS)\n\n\ndef context_slice(\n    frame: pd.DataFrame, start: pd.Timestamp, time_length: int, context_days: int, issuance_lead: int | None = None\n) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"The context of the prompt at `start`: the bars from `context_days` before it to `context_end`.\"\"\"\n    return frame.loc[start - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days) : context_end(start, time_length, issuance_lead)]\n\n\ndef nan_head_minutes(context: pd.DataFrame) -> int:\n    \"\"\"How many minutes the context runs before its first real close.\"\"\"\n    real = context[\"close\"].notna().to_numpy()\n    return int(real.argmax()) if real.any() else len(real)\n\n\ndef context_days_of(module: ModuleType) -> int:\n    \"\"\"The champion's `CONTEXT_DAYS`, or the default when its module does not set it.\"\"\"\n    value = getattr(module, \"CONTEXT_DAYS\", DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS)\n    low, high = CONTEXT_DAYS_BOUNDS\n    if type(value) is not int or not low <= value <= high:\n        raise ValueError(f\"CONTEXT_DAYS must be a plain int from {low} to {high} in modeling.py, got {value!r}\")\n    return value\n\n\n# What simulate() receives as context_prices: the minute OHLCV frame, or the Series of closes (NaN\n# kept) of the contract before OHLCV, for a champion written against that one.\nCONTEXT_MODES = (\"ohlcv\", \"close\")\n\n\n# float32 is what the validator stores miner predictions as, so the field's CRPS was computed at\n# this precision too. It also quarters the cache: a day of crypto-1h is 35 MB instead of 170.\nPATH_DTYPE = \"float32\"\n\n\ndef day_files(out_dir: Path, asset: str, time_length: int, time_increment: int, day: str) -> tuple[Path, Path]:\n    \"\"\"The (paths, index) pair for one day of one prompt format.\"\"\"\n    root = out_dir / asset / f\"{time_length}_{time_increment}\"\n    return root / f\"date={day}.npy\", root / f\"date={day}.json\"\n\n\ndef covered_start_times(index_path: Path, paths_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Prompt start_times the day file already holds, or nothing when it has none.\n\n    Both halves must be present. build_prediction_index skips an index whose .npy is missing, so\n    treating that state as covered here would skip generation for a day nothing can then score.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (index_path.exists() and paths_path.exists()):\n        return set()\n    try:\n        return set(json.loads(index_path.read_text())[\"start_times\"])\n    except (ValueError, KeyError):\n        return set()  # truncated by an interrupted write; regenerate the day\n\n\ndef load_module(modeling_path: Path) -> ModuleType:\n    # A champion imports the modules beside it by name, as when its folder is the script's own.\n    folder = str(modeling_path.resolve().parent)\n    if folder not in sys.path:\n        sys.path.insert(0, folder)\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(f\"candidate_{modeling_path.parent.name}\", modeling_path)\n    assert spec is not None and spec.loader is not None  # always true for a .py file path\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    return module\n\n\ndef load_simulate(modeling_path: Path) -> Callable:\n    return load_module(modeling_path).simulate\n\n\ndef store_root(data_root: Path, asset: str) -> Path:\n    root = data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n    if not root.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"no minute store for {asset}: {root} does not exist\")\n    return root\n\n\ndef load_minute_prices(data_root: Path, asset: str, start: pd.Timestamp, end: pd.Timestamp) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Minute OHLCV over [start, end] from daily partitions.\n\n    The days before the asset's first partition, before the market's first trade or the store's first\n    day, are NaN on every minute, as in a live context. A missing partition after it raises: a silent\n    hole here would shrink every context that spans it without anyone noticing.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(data_root, asset)\n    stored = (date.fromisoformat(p.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\")) for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\"))\n    first_day = min(stored, default=start.date())\n    frames = []\n    day = max(start.date(), first_day)\n    while day <= end.date():\n        path = root / f\"date={day.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n        if not path.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"missing partition {path}\")\n        try:\n            frames.append(pd.read_parquet(path, columns=[\"timestamp\", *OHLCV_COLUMNS]))\n        except ValueError as exc:  # pyarrow's ArrowInvalid, on a column the file lacks\n            raise ValueError(\n                f\"{path} predates the OHLCV columns. Re-ingest with --force-refresh: ingest_day \"\n                f\"skips settled partitions that already exist.\"\n            ) from exc\n        day += timedelta(days=1)\n    if not frames:\n        raise FileNotFoundError(\n            f\"no partition for {asset} from {start.date()} to {end.date()}: its first is {first_day}\"\n        )\n    frame = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n    frame[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(frame[\"timestamp\"], utc=True)\n    frame = frame.set_index(\"timestamp\").sort_index()\n    if start.date() < first_day:\n        head = pd.date_range(\n            pd.Timestamp(start.date(), tz=\"UTC\"), frame.index[0], freq=\"1min\", inclusive=\"left\", name=\"timestamp\"\n        )\n        frame = pd.concat([pd.DataFrame(np.nan, index=head, columns=OHLCV_COLUMNS), frame])\n    return frame.loc[start:end]\n\n\ndef prompt_grid(\n    window_start: pd.Timestamp,\n    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n    cadence_minutes: int,\n    prompt_times: list[pd.Timestamp] | None = None,\n) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n    \"\"\"Prompts in [start, end). Filtered with `t < window_end` rather than [:-1] so a window_end\n    not aligned to the cadence does not drop the last valid prompt.\n\n    `prompt_times` replaces the even grid with an explicit list — the start_times the validator\n    actually prompted at, which sit at arbitrary minutes.\"\"\"\n    grid = (\n        prompt_times\n        if prompt_times is not None\n        else pd.date_range(window_start, window_end, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", tz=\"UTC\")\n    )\n    return [t for t in grid if window_start <= t < window_end]\n\n\ndef generate_day(\n    simulate_fn: Callable,\n    asset: str,\n    day: str,\n    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n    price_frame: pd.DataFrame,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    time_increment: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    num_simulations: int,\n    issuance_lead: int | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Generate one day's prompts and write the pair. Returns how many were generated, 0 if the\n    day was already covered.\n\n    A day is written whole: if anything is missing it is all regenerated, so a file always holds\n    exactly the start_times its index names and an interrupted run cannot leave a half-day behind.\n    \"\"\"\n    paths_file, index_file = day_files(out_dir, asset, time_length, time_increment, day)\n    wanted = [t.isoformat() for t in times]\n    if not set(wanted) - covered_start_times(index_file, paths_file):\n        return 0\n\n    runs = []\n    head = 0\n    for t in times:\n        # THE no-lookahead line: the context stops at the last bar the prompt's issuance allows,\n        # never at t — the bar labelled t closes after the prompt starts.\n        context = context_slice(price_frame, t, time_length, context_days, issuance_lead)\n        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n        if context_mode == \"close\":\n            context = context[\"close\"]\n        out = simulate_fn(\n            asset=asset,\n            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n            context_prices=context,\n        )\n        runs.append(np.asarray(out[2:], dtype=PATH_DTYPE))\n\n    paths_file.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    stacked = np.stack(runs)\n    np.save(paths_file, stacked)\n    index_file.write_text(\n        json.dumps(\n            {\n                \"start_times\": wanted,\n                \"asset\": asset,\n                \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n                \"time_length\": time_length,\n                \"num_simulations\": int(stacked.shape[1]),\n                \"num_steps\": int(stacked.shape[2]),\n                \"context_days\": context_days,\n                \"context_head_nan_minutes\": head,\n            }\n        )\n    )\n    return len(times)\n\n\ndef generate(\n    simulate_fn: Callable,\n    asset: str,\n    window_start: pd.Timestamp,\n    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n    price_frame: pd.DataFrame,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    cadence_minutes: int,\n    time_increment: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    num_simulations: int = DEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS,\n    prompt_times: list[pd.Timestamp] | None = None,\n    issuance_lead: int | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS,\n) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Returns (generated, reused) prompt counts.\"\"\"\n    by_day: dict[str, list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n    for t in prompt_grid(window_start, window_end, cadence_minutes, prompt_times):\n        by_day.setdefault(t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"), []).append(t)\n\n    generated = reused = 0\n    for day, times in sorted(by_day.items()):\n        made = generate_day(\n            simulate_fn,\n            asset,\n            day,\n            times,\n            price_frame,\n            out_dir,\n            time_increment,\n            time_length,\n            num_simulations,\n            issuance_lead,\n            context_mode,\n            context_days,\n        )\n        generated += made\n        reused += 0 if made else len(times)\n    return generated, reused\n\n\ndef _utc(value: str) -> pd.Timestamp:\n    ts = pd.Timestamp(value)\n    return ts.tz_localize(\"UTC\") if ts.tzinfo is None else ts.tz_convert(\"UTC\")\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--modeling\", required=True, type=Path)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-start\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-end\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data-root\", required=True, type=Path)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out-dir\", required=True, type=Path)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--cadence-minutes\", type=int, required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--num-simulations\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS)\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--issuance-lead-seconds\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=f\"override how far before start_time the prompt is issued (default per format: \"\n        f\"{ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS})\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--context\",\n        choices=CONTEXT_MODES,\n        default=\"ohlcv\",\n        help=\"context_prices as the minute OHLCV frame, or as the Series of closes a champion written \"\n        \"before the OHLCV context expects\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--prompt-times\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"JSON list of ISO start_times to generate at, instead of the --cadence-minutes grid\",\n    )\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    start, end = _utc(args.window_start), _utc(args.window_end)\n    prompt_times = None\n    if args.prompt_times is not None:\n        prompt_times = [_utc(t) for t in json.loads(args.prompt_times.read_text())]\n    module = load_module(args.modeling)\n    days = context_days_of(module)\n    prices = load_minute_prices(args.data_root, args.asset, start - pd.Timedelta(days=days), end)\n    generated, reused = generate(\n        module.simulate,\n        args.asset,\n        start,\n        end,\n        prices,\n        args.out_dir,\n        cadence_minutes=args.cadence_minutes,\n        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n        time_length=args.time_length,\n        num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n        prompt_times=prompt_times,\n        issuance_lead=args.issuance_lead_seconds,\n        context_mode=args.context,\n        context_days=days,\n    )\n    print(f\"{args.asset} tl={args.time_length}: {generated} predictions ({reused} reused), CONTEXT_DAYS {days}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SQ571ZFZ6dHhUpaExcsT7K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
