{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FmdnMYiE6MjWRySSdFq4aJ","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (38.2KB). Full output saved to: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad/tool-results/bkfxn1o7m.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n\"\"\"Verdict runner: score archived champions, in the sandbox.\n\nFor each leg under campaign_results/<campaign>/ that has a CHAMPION + workspace.bundle:\n  1. `git clone` the bundle and check out CHAMPION.sha — the scored code is provably the\n     nominated code, not whatever the workspace drifted to after nomination.\n  2. Copy in generate_predictions.py (self-contained by design).\n  3. Phase 1 (network=bridge): `uv sync` in the clone — bundles are git-only, the venv must be\n     built, and that needs the network. It fetches only pinned packages, never prices.\n  4. Phase 2 (network=none): one sandbox run per (competition, asset) generating predictions.\n     The data root is mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data; the model itself only ever\n     receives the pre-prompt context (see generate_predictions.py). Predictions are\n     written to a cache mounted at /workspace/predictions that outlives the workspace, one file\n     per day, so a re-score of a window already generated skips straight to scoring.\n  5. On the host: evaluate_candidate() against the offline bundle -> per-competition rank +\n     simulated emissions -> Score = 100 x mean over competitions of reward_vs_top (see\n     evaluate.reward_metrics; the unweighted mean mirrors the subnet's 1/3-per-competition\n     emission split, and the softmaxed reward_weight makes top positions worth more, which a\n     rank percentile would flatten). Field uids that changed hands are split as live does, from\n     registrations read from the Synth API once per window and kept in local files: the\n     window's offline bundle and each verdict. A re-score reads those first. Late joiners are\n     backfilled from each minute's first-saved prompt, read the same way into the bundle.\n  6. Write campaign_results/<campaign>/<leg>/verdict-<tag>/ — the verdict.json, the\n     per-competition rank-evolution charts, the per-prompt CRPS frames and the recomputed field\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"404fa730-8358-46b5-8ab1-524b061d9a16","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:15:41.771Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Verdict runner: score archived champions, in the sandbox.\n\nFor each leg under campaign_results/<campaign>/ that has a CHAMPION + workspace.bundle:\n  1. `git clone` the bundle and check out CHAMPION.sha — the scored code is provably the\n     nominated code, not whatever the workspace drifted to after nomination.\n  2. Copy in generate_predictions.py (self-contained by design).\n  3. Phase 1 (network=bridge): `uv sync` in the clone — bundles are git-only, the venv must be\n     built, and that needs the network. It fetches only pinned packages, never prices.\n  4. Phase 2 (network=none): one sandbox run per (competition, asset) generating predictions.\n     The data root is mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data; the model itself only ever\n     receives the pre-prompt context (see generate_predictions.py). Predictions are\n     written to a cache mounted at /workspace/predictions that outlives the workspace, one file\n     per day, so a re-score of a window already generated skips straight to scoring.\n  5. On the host: evaluate_candidate() against the offline bundle -> per-competition rank +\n     simulated emissions -> Score = 100 x mean over competitions of reward_vs_top (see\n     evaluate.reward_metrics; the unweighted mean mirrors the subnet's 1/3-per-competition\n     emission split, and the softmaxed reward_weight makes top positions worth more, which a\n     rank percentile would flatten). Field uids that changed hands are split as live does, from\n     registrations read from the Synth API once per window and kept in local files: the\n     window's offline bundle and each verdict. A re-score reads those first. Late joiners are\n     backfilled from each minute's first-saved prompt, read the same way into the bundle.\n  6. Write campaign_results/<campaign>/<leg>/verdict-<tag>/ — the verdict.json, the\n     per-competition rank-evolution charts, the per-prompt CRPS frames and the recomputed field\n     rewards. One directory per verdict, so a re-score under --tag cannot overwrite the artifacts\n     of the verdict it is compared against.\n\nThe synth_default baseline runs on the HOST (trusted repo code; note its known caveat below).\n\nUsage (on the box, after ingesting prices up to window_end + 1 day):\n  export LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=...   # not needed here, but the offline bundle build needs network,\n                                  # and so does the first run of a window (registrations)\n  uv run python -m synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict --campaign <name> \\\\\n      --window-start <YYYY-MM-DD> --window-end <YYYY-MM-DD>\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores, get_registrations, get_scores_save_order\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.scoring import Registrations, SaveOrder\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark import workspace\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import CONTEXT_MODES, DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.nomination import parse_champion\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.campaign import PACKAGED_BASELINE, baseline_modeling_path\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.sandbox.run_sandbox import DEFAULT_IMAGE, image_identity, sandbox_cmd\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.manifest import sha256_file\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.evaluate import COMPETITIONS, evaluate_candidate, prepare_offline_bundle\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_DIR, CALENDAR_ENV, VIEW_FILE\n\nGENERATE_SCRIPT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / \"generate_predictions.py\"\nSANDBOX_IMAGE = DEFAULT_IMAGE\nSANDBOX_MEMORY_GB = 12\nSANDBOX_CPUS = 12\n# Prompt grid density per format: hourly for the 24h competitions, 10-minute for crypto-1h. It is\n# the density the validator scores at — one request per asset per hour for the 24h competitions,\n# one per 10 minutes for crypto-1h — but not the phase: the kept request sits at an arbitrary\n# minute inside its bucket, so a grid prompt is up to half a cadence from the one the field\n# answered. --live-prompts replaces the grid with the real start_times.\nCADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n# Written into the workspace for --live-prompts; the generator reads one file per (asset, format).\nPROMPT_TIMES_DIR = \"prompt_times\"\n# A prompt's paths depend on the champion's code and on the seed it was generated with, so both\n# are in the cache path: nothing else distinguishes two runs of the same window.\nDEFAULT_PREDICTIONS_CACHE = Path(\"predictions_cache\")\n# Beside the scores and rewards in the window's offline bundle (prepare_offline_bundle).\nREGISTRATIONS_FILE = \"registrations.json\"\nSAVE_ORDER_FILE = \"scores_save_order.json\"\n\n# Constitution rule 7: a champion that uses randomness seeds every generator from this, and it\n# is set only here, at evaluation. Absent during a campaign, so an agent's own runs vary.\nSEED_ENV = \"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\"\n# Python salts string hashing per process, so a champion that derives its own seed from hash() —\n# which rule 7 does not reach, and campaign-3's champion does — draws different paths on every\n# run. Pinning this makes those champions reproducible too. Must be set before the interpreter\n# starts, which is why it travels as an env var rather than being set in the generator.\nHASH_SEED_ENV = \"PYTHONHASHSEED\"\nDEFAULT_SEED = 0\n\n\ndef generation_env(seed: int) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"What a generation process needs to be reproducible.\"\"\"\n    return {SEED_ENV: str(seed), HASH_SEED_ENV: str(seed % 2**32)}\n\n\ndef generation_start(window_start: str, time_length: int, lead_in: bool) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Where generation begins for a competition, given the scoring window's start.\n\n    The window scores every prompt whose `scored_time` falls inside it, but a prompt is scored one\n    horizon after it starts — so the earliest scored prompts began BEFORE the window. Generating\n    only from `window_start` leaves those without a prediction, and the validator's moving average\n    then treats the candidate as a miner that joined late: `prepare_df_for_moving_average` backfills\n    every earlier timestamp with the worst score in the field. The candidate eats a full horizon of\n    worst-score rounds it never had the chance to answer.\n\n    Leading generation in by one horizon makes the candidate's first `scored_time` equal the\n    field's, so it is never classified as new. Lengthening the window does not substitute for this:\n    it dilutes the backfilled rounds without removing them.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = pd.Timestamp(window_start, tz=\"UTC\")\n    if lead_in:\n        start -= pd.Timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n    return start.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef live_prompt_starts(window: tuple[str, str], lead_in: bool) -> dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]]:\n    \"\"\"The start_times the validator actually scored, per (asset, time_length).\n\n    Read from the offline bundle, which is built first: `scored_time - time_length` is the prompt's\n    own start, and the bundle already holds only the density-tapered set the validator kept — one\n    request per asset per hour for the 24h competitions, one per 10 minutes for crypto-1h. The\n    issued set behind it is ten times larger and was never scored.\n    \"\"\"\n    out: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        start = pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)).to_pydatetime()\n        end = pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime()\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            # The scores are keyed on scored_time, so ask from one horizon after the first prompt.\n            scores = get_miner_scores(\n                start + timedelta(seconds=comp.time_length), end, asset, comp.time_length, comp.time_increment\n            )\n            starts = [] if scores.empty else sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n            out[(asset, comp.time_length)] = [t for t in starts if start <= t.to_pydatetime() < end]\n            print(f\"  {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {len(out[(asset, comp.time_length)])} prompts\", flush=True)\n    return out\n\n\ndef write_prompt_times(root: Path, prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"One JSON list of start_times per (asset, time_length), named as the generator expects.\"\"\"\n    directory = root / PROMPT_TIMES_DIR\n    directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for (asset, time_length), starts in prompt_starts.items():\n        path = directory / f\"{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n        path.write_text(json.dumps([pd.Timestamp(t).isoformat() for t in starts]))\n\n\ndef run(cmd: list[str], what: str, env: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> None:\n    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, env={**os.environ, **env} if env else None)\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        tail = (result.stdout + result.stderr).decode(errors=\"replace\")[-2000:]\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{what} failed (rc={result.returncode}):\\n{tail}\")\n\n\ndef docker_limits() -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"SANDBOX_CPUS/MEMORY capped to what the local daemon actually has — a laptop's Docker\n    Desktop VM is often smaller than the host, and docker hard-errors on an over-ask.\"\"\"\n    result = subprocess.run([\"docker\", \"info\", \"--format\", \"{{.NCPU}} {{.MemTotal}}\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        return SANDBOX_CPUS, SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB\n    ncpu, mem_bytes = result.stdout.split()\n    return min(SANDBOX_CPUS, int(ncpu)), min(SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB, int(mem_bytes) // 1024**3)\n\n\ndef baseline_identity(modeling: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Short content hash of the baseline's source, so changing it cannot reuse its cache.\"\"\"\n    return hashlib.sha256(modeling.read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n\n\ndef predictions_cache(\n    root: Path,\n    champion: str,\n    seed: int,\n    live_prompts: bool,\n    lead_in: bool,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    calendar_sha: str | None = None,\n) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where one champion's generated paths live, across runs.\n\n    Everything that decides WHICH prompts get generated is in the path. Two runs that disagree on\n    any of it answer the same window at different instants, and scoring matches the nearest\n    prediction within half an hour — so a shared tree would serve one run the other's predictions,\n    silently reproducing the behaviour the differing flag exists to measure.\n    \"\"\"\n    mode = \"live-prompts\" if live_prompts else \"cadence-grid\"\n    if not lead_in:\n        mode += \"-no-lead-in\"\n    if context_mode != \"ohlcv\":\n        mode += f\"-{context_mode}\"\n    if calendar_sha is not None:\n        mode += f\"-calendar-{calendar_sha[:12]}\"\n    return root / champion / f\"seed={seed}\" / mode\n\n\ndef sandbox(\n    workspace: Path,\n    data_root: Path,\n    home: Path,\n    inner: str,\n    network: str,\n    gpus: bool,\n    cpus: int = SANDBOX_CPUS,\n    memory_gb: int = SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB,\n    env: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n    predictions: Path | None = None,\n) -> list[str]:\n    return sandbox_cmd(\n        workspace=workspace,\n        snapshot=data_root,  # mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data\n        home=home,\n        image=SANDBOX_IMAGE,\n        memory_gb=memory_gb,\n        cpus=cpus,\n        network=network,\n        env=env or {},\n        inner_cmd=inner,\n        gpus=gpus,\n        predictions=predictions,\n    )\n\n\ndef clone_champion(bundle: Path, sha: str, dest: Path) -> None:\n    run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"-q\", str(bundle), str(dest)], f\"clone {bundle}\")\n    run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(dest), \"checkout\", \"-q\", sha], f\"checkout {sha}\")\n\n\ndef generate_all(\n    workspace: Path,\n    data_root: Path,\n    home: Path,\n    window: tuple[str, str],\n    gpus: bool,\n    limits: tuple[int, int],\n    seed: int,\n    lead_in: bool = True,\n    prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] | None = None,\n    cache: Path | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    calendar: Path | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"One --network none sandbox run per (competition, asset).\n\n    The sandbox inherits nothing from the host, so the seed, the prompt start_times and the calendar\n    have to be handed to it explicitly — the latter two as files in the workspace, since it has no\n    network. The calendar is the campaign's, frozen at its cutoff, not the one in the data root.\"\"\"\n    if not GENERATE_SCRIPT.exists():  # packaging regression: it must ship with the package\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"generation core missing at {GENERATE_SCRIPT}\")\n    shutil.copy(GENERATE_SCRIPT, workspace / \"generate_predictions.py\")\n    if prompt_starts is not None:\n        write_prompt_times(workspace, prompt_starts)\n    env = generation_env(seed)\n    if calendar is not None:\n        (workspace / CALENDAR_DIR).mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n        shutil.copy(calendar, workspace / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE)\n        env[CALENDAR_ENV] = f\"/workspace/{CALENDAR_DIR}/{VIEW_FILE}\"\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            inner = (\n                \"uv run python generate_predictions.py\"\n                \" --modeling agent/modeling.py\"\n                f\" --asset {asset}\"\n                f\" --window-start {generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)}\"\n                f\" --window-end {window[1]}\"\n                \" --data-root /workspace/market_data --out-dir predictions\"\n                f\" --cadence-minutes {CADENCE_MINUTES[comp.time_length]}\"\n                f\" --time-increment {comp.time_increment} --time-length {comp.time_length}\"\n            )\n            if prompt_starts is not None:\n                inner += f\" --prompt-times {PROMPT_TIMES_DIR}/{asset}_{comp.time_length}.json\"\n            if context_mode != \"ohlcv\":\n                inner += f\" --context {context_mode}\"\n            try:\n                run(\n                    sandbox(\n                        workspace,\n                        data_root,\n                        home,\n                        inner,\n                        network=\"none\",\n                        gpus=gpus,\n                        cpus=limits[0],\n                        memory_gb=limits[1],\n                        env=env,\n                        predictions=cache,\n                    ),\n                    f\"generate {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\",\n                )\n            except RuntimeError as exc:\n                # Per-asset fault isolation, mirroring evaluate_candidate: a dead asset (real\n                # case: SPYX — feed retired mid-July, no prices in any post-cutoff window) must\n                # not sink the leg. No predictions -> the asset lands in assets_failed at scoring.\n                print(f\"  SKIP {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {str(exc).splitlines()[-1]}\", flush=True)\n                continue\n            print(f\"  generated {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef reported_context_days(predictions: Path) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"The CONTEXT_DAYS every (competition, asset) run reported in its day indexes, None when there is\n    no index. An index written before the field reads as the default.\"\"\"\n    reported = {\n        json.loads(index.read_text()).get(\"context_days\", DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS)\n        for index in predictions.glob(\"*/*/date=*.json\")\n    }\n    if len(reported) > 1:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"the generation runs under {predictions} report different CONTEXT_DAYS: {sorted(reported)}\")\n    return reported.pop() if reported else None\n\n\ndef context_heads(predictions: Path, window: tuple[str, str], lead_in: bool) -> dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Per asset with a context of the window that did not start on a real close, the most minutes one\n    ran before its first, from the day indexes of the window's generation days. An index written\n    before the field reads as 0.\"\"\"\n    first = min(pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window[0], c.time_length, lead_in)) for c in COMPETITIONS)\n    end = pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\")\n    heads: dict[str, int] = {}\n    for index in predictions.glob(\"*/*/date=*.json\"):\n        day = pd.Timestamp(index.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\"), tz=\"UTC\")\n        if day < first.normalize() or day >= end:\n            continue\n        minutes = json.loads(index.read_text()).get(\"context_head_nan_minutes\", 0)\n        asset = index.parent.parent.name\n        if minutes:\n            heads[asset] = max(heads.get(asset, 0), minutes)\n    return dict(sorted(heads.items()))\n\n\ndef stores_starting_late(\n    data_root: Path, window_start: str, context_days: int, lead_in: bool\n) -> dict[str, tuple[date, date]]:\n    \"\"\"Per asset whose first partition in `data_root` is after the day its first context begins: that\n    day, and the first partition's.\"\"\"\n    begins: dict[str, date] = {}\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        start = pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window_start, comp.time_length, lead_in))\n        day = (start - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days)).date()\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            begins[asset] = min(begins.get(asset, day), day)\n    late = {}\n    for asset, day in begins.items():\n        stored = (data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\").glob(\"date=*.parquet\")\n        first = min((date.fromisoformat(p.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\")) for p in stored), default=None)\n        if first is not None and first > day:\n            late[asset] = (day, first)\n    return late\n\n\ndef generate_baseline(\n    modeling: Path,\n    data_root: Path,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    window: tuple[str, str],\n    seed: int,\n    lead_in: bool = True,\n    prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Host-side, trusted repo code. Known caveat: the subnet's default generator ignores\n    context_prices and anchors on a price it fetches ITSELF — for past prompts that anchor may be\n    wrong, so read the baseline's verdict with suspicion and drop it from the article if broken.\"\"\"\n    if prompt_starts is not None:\n        write_prompt_times(out_dir.parent, prompt_starts)\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            times = out_dir.parent / PROMPT_TIMES_DIR / f\"{asset}_{comp.time_length}.json\"\n            try:\n                run(\n                    [\n                        \"uv\",\n                        \"run\",\n                        \"python\",\n                        str(GENERATE_SCRIPT),\n                        *(\"--modeling\", str(modeling)),\n                        *(\"--asset\", asset),\n                        *(\"--window-start\", generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)),\n                        *(\"--window-end\", window[1]),\n                        *(\"--data-root\", str(data_root), \"--out-dir\", str(out_dir)),\n                        *(\"--cadence-minutes\", str(CADENCE_MINUTES[comp.time_length])),\n                        *(\"--time-increment\", str(comp.time_increment), \"--time-length\", str(comp.time_length)),\n                        *((\"--prompt-times\", str(times)) if prompt_starts is not None else ()),\n                    ],\n                    f\"baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\",\n                    env=generation_env(seed),\n                )\n            except RuntimeError as exc:\n                print(f\"  SKIP baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {str(exc).splitlines()[-1]}\", flush=True)\n                continue\n            print(f\"  baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef registration_span(window: tuple[str, str], simulate_registration: datetime | None) -> tuple[datetime, datetime]:\n    \"\"\"The span whose registrations can split the scored data: from one horizon before the window\n    (and a competition window earlier with a simulated registration) to the window's end.\"\"\"\n    start = pd.Timestamp(window[0], tz=\"UTC\") - pd.Timedelta(seconds=max(c.time_length for c in COMPETITIONS))\n    if simulate_registration is not None:\n        start -= pd.Timedelta(days=max(c.window_days for c in COMPETITIONS))\n    return start.to_pydatetime(), pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime()\n\n\ndef registrations_record(span: tuple[datetime, datetime], rows: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The field's registrations over `span` (`get_registrations` rows), as kept beside a window's\n    bundle and in its verdicts.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"since\": span[0].isoformat(),\n        \"until\": span[1].isoformat(),\n        \"rows\": [\n            {\"miner_uid\": int(row.miner_uid), \"hotkey\": row.hotkey, \"created_at\": row.created_at.isoformat()}\n            for row in rows.itertuples()\n        ],\n    }\n\n\ndef registrations_from(record: dict) -> dict[int, list[datetime]]:\n    \"\"\"uid -> the registration times of its occupants in a `registrations_record`, ascending.\"\"\"\n    out: dict[int, list[datetime]] = {}\n    for row in record[\"rows\"]:\n        out.setdefault(int(row[\"miner_uid\"]), []).append(datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"created_at\"]))\n    return {uid: sorted(times) for uid, times in out.items()}\n\n\ndef _covers(record: dict, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> bool:\n    return (record.get(\"since\"), record.get(\"until\")) == (span[0].isoformat(), span[1].isoformat())\n\n\ndef recorded_registrations(campaign_dir: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"The registrations record any of the campaign's verdicts holds for `span`, or None.\"\"\"\n    for path in sorted(campaign_dir.glob(\"**/verdict*/verdict.json\")):\n        record = json.loads(path.read_text()).get(\"registrations\") or {}\n        if _covers(record, span):\n            return record\n    return None\n\n\ndef window_registrations(bundle: Path, campaign_dir: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The field's registrations record for `span`, from local files before the API: the window's\n    offline bundle, then the campaign's verdicts. Written into the bundle when it lacked it.\"\"\"\n    cached = bundle / REGISTRATIONS_FILE\n    if cached.exists() and _covers(record := json.loads(cached.read_text()), span):\n        return record\n    record = recorded_registrations(campaign_dir, span)\n    if record is None:\n        print(\"reading the field's uid registrations from the Synth API...\", flush=True)\n        record = registrations_record(span, get_registrations(*span))\n    cached.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return record\n\n\ndef window_save_order(bundle: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict[int, SaveOrder]:\n    \"\"\"time_length -> the validator's save order over `span` (`get_scores_save_order`), from the\n    window's offline bundle before the API. Written into the bundle when it lacked it.\"\"\"\n    cached = bundle / SAVE_ORDER_FILE\n    if cached.exists() and _covers(record := json.loads(cached.read_text()), span):\n        orders = record[\"orders\"]\n    else:\n        print(\"reading the validator's save order from the Synth API...\", flush=True)\n        orders = {\n            str(time_length): [\n                {\"scored_time\": t.isoformat(), \"assets\": assets}\n                for t, assets in get_scores_save_order(*span, time_length).items()\n            ]\n            for time_length in sorted({c.time_length for c in COMPETITIONS})\n        }\n        record = {\"since\": span[0].isoformat(), \"until\": span[1].isoformat(), \"orders\": orders}\n        cached.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return {int(tl): {pd.Timestamp(row[\"scored_time\"]): row[\"assets\"] for row in rows} for tl, rows in orders.items()}\n\n\ndef engine_rev() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"The synth-lib commit this host scores with, or None when it was not installed from git.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return workspace._host_synth_lib_rev()\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return None\n\n\ndef score(\n    name: str,\n    predictions: Path,\n    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n    window_days: int,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    simulate_registration: datetime | None = None,\n    registrations: Registrations | None = None,\n    save_order: Mapping[int, SaveOrder] | None = None,\n) -> dict:\n    result = evaluate_candidate(\n        name,\n        predictions,\n        window_end,\n        window_days,\n        out_dir,\n        simulate_registration,\n        registrations,\n        save_order,\n        match_tolerance_minutes=CADENCE_MINUTES,\n    )\n    mrt = result[\"mean_reward_vs_top\"]\n    result[\"score\"] = round(100 * mrt, 1) if mrt is not None else None\n    ranks = [c[\"rank\"] for c in result[\"per_competition\"].values() if c[\"rank\"] is not None]\n    # Crude by design (field sizes differ per competition) but requested for cross-window\n    # comparisons: the Score is softmax-top-weighted and near-zero for everyone off the podium,\n    # while the mean rank still moves in the mid-field.\n    result[\"mean_competition_rank\"] = round(sum(ranks) / len(ranks), 1) if ranks else None\n    return result\n\n\ndef verdict_payload(\n    result: dict,\n    sha: str | None,\n    window: tuple[str, str],\n    seed: int,\n    simulate_registration: datetime | None,\n    live_prompts: bool,\n    registrations: dict | None = None,\n    engine: str | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    calendar: dict | None = None,\n    context_days: int | None = None,\n    context_head_nan_minutes: dict[str, int] | None = None,\n) -> dict:\n    return {\n        \"score\": result[\"score\"],\n        \"mean_competition_rank\": result[\"mean_competition_rank\"],\n        \"score_definition\": \"100 x mean over competitions of min(1, candidate_total_reward /\"\n        \" top_other_miner_total_reward) (validator reward_weight summed over the window; bounded\"\n        \" 0-100: 0 = earned nothing, 100 = matched or beat the field's best in every competition;\"\n        \" per-competition beats_field flags when the cap binds)\",\n        \"mean_reward_vs_top\": result[\"mean_reward_vs_top\"],\n        \"mean_competition_percentile\": result[\"mean_competition_percentile\"],\n        \"per_competition\": result[\"per_competition\"],\n        \"window\": {\n            \"start\": window[0],\n            \"end\": window[1],\n            \"note\": \"pseudo-out-of-sample: after the \"\n            \"data cutoff, but agents had live field-API access during their runs\",\n        },\n        \"champion_sha\": sha,\n        \"sandbox_image\": image_identity(SANDBOX_IMAGE),\n        \"cadence_minutes\": CADENCE_MINUTES,\n        \"num_simulations\": 1000,\n        # What a stochastic champion was seeded with. Without it \"seeded\" is unverifiable and\n        # a re-score of this window cannot reproduce the number above.\n        \"seed\": seed,\n        # A Score with a simulated registration includes the onboarding backfill every real\n        # miner pays once. It answers a different question from the steady-state Score and the\n        # two must never be read as the same number.\n        \"simulate_registration\": simulate_registration.isoformat() if simulate_registration else None,\n        # False means the candidate answered a cadence grid and cadence_minutes describes it; True\n        # means it answered the validator's own scored start_times and the grid was not used.\n        \"live_prompts\": live_prompts,\n        # Field uids registered inside the scored span (registrations_record); a re-score of the\n        # same span reads them back instead of the API.\n        \"registrations\": registrations,\n        # The synth-lib commit that scored this verdict; None for an install not made from git.\n        \"engine_rev\": engine,\n        # What simulate() received as context_prices (generate_predictions.CONTEXT_MODES).\n        \"context_prices\": context_mode,\n        # How many days of it: the champion's CONTEXT_DAYS, as its generation runs reported it.\n        \"context_days\": context_days,\n        # Per asset whose contexts did not all start on a real close, the most minutes one ran before it.\n        \"context_head_nan_minutes\": context_head_nan_minutes,\n        # The event calendar the champion was handed: the one its campaign's agents saw, or None.\n        \"calendar\": calendar,\n    }\n\n\ndef main() -> None:  # noqa: C901 — a linear operator script; splitting it would obscure the order\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--campaign\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-start\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-end\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--results-dir\", type=Path, default=Path(\"campaign_results\"))\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data-root\", type=Path, default=Path(\"market_data\"))\n    ap.add_argument(\"--legs\", nargs=\"*\", default=None, help=\"default: every leg with a CHAMPION\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--tag\",\n        default=None,\n        help=\"write into verdict-<tag>/ instead of verdict/ — use for extra windows (in-sample \"\n        \"diagnostics) so they never overwrite the pre-registered window's canonical verdict\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"rescore legs whose verdict.json already exists\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--skip-baseline\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--no-lead-in\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"generate only inside the window, as before the lead-in fix: the first horizon of \"\n        \"scored prompts then has no prediction and the candidate is backfilled at the field's \"\n        \"worst score. For reproducing an old verdict, not for scoring a new one.\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--baseline-module\",\n        default=PACKAGED_BASELINE,\n        help=\"dotted module path or file path exposing simulate() (default: the packaged control)\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--simulate-registration\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"score the champion as a miner that registered on --window-start: the prompts issued \"\n        \"before that day are dropped, so its first score lands a horizon later and the validator's \"\n        \"moving average treats it as a late joiner, backfilling the preceding window at the field's \"\n        \"worst score. This is what a champion earns in its first days live, and it is NOT comparable \"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/root/.claude/projects/-workspace/b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad/tool-results/bkfxn1o7m.txt","persistedOutputSize":39155},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FmdnMYiE6MjWRySSdFq4aJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011CgwCixn4Q4m8N8gwdXWzi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U7TN9QYCM2KpBhfQ9493xq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/root/.claude/projects/-workspace/b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad/tool-results/bkfxn1o7m.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4741,"cache_read_input_tokens":96134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4741,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"1358b2e0-ac3b-4e79-8457-089801e30c86","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:15:45.729Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U7TN9QYCM2KpBhfQ9493xq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Verdict runner: score archived champions, in the sandbox.\n2\t\n3\tFor each leg under campaign_results/<campaign>/ that has a CHAMPION + workspace.bundle:\n4\t  1. `git clone` the bundle and check out CHAMPION.sha — the scored code is provably the\n5\t     nominated code, not whatever the workspace drifted to after nomination.\n6\t  2. Copy in generate_predictions.py (self-contained by design).\n7\t  3. Phase 1 (network=bridge): `uv sync` in the clone — bundles are git-only, the venv must be\n8\t     built, and that needs the network. It fetches only pinned packages, never prices.\n9\t  4. Phase 2 (network=none): one sandbox run per (competition, asset) generating predictions.\n10\t     The data root is mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data; the model itself only ever\n11\t     receives the pre-prompt context (see generate_predictions.py). Predictions are\n12\t     written to a cache mounted at /workspace/predictions that outlives the workspace, one file\n13\t     per day, so a re-score of a window already generated skips straight to scoring.\n14\t  5. On the host: evaluate_candidate() against the offline bundle -> per-competition rank +\n15\t     simulated emissions -> Score = 100 x mean over competitions of reward_vs_top (see\n16\t     evaluate.reward_metrics; the unweighted mean mirrors the subnet's 1/3-per-competition\n17\t     emission split, and the softmaxed reward_weight makes top positions worth more, which a\n18\t     rank percentile would flatten). Field uids that changed hands are split as live does, from\n19\t     registrations read from the Synth API once per window and kept in local files: the\n20\t     window's offline bundle and each verdict. A re-score reads those first. Late joiners are\n21\t     backfilled from each minute's first-saved prompt, read the same way into the bundle.\n22\t  6. Write campaign_results/<campaign>/<leg>/verdict-<tag>/ — the verdict.json, the\n23\t     per-competition rank-evolution charts, the per-prompt CRPS frames and the recomputed field\n24\t     rewards. One directory per verdict, so a re-score under --tag cannot overwrite the artifacts\n25\t     of the verdict it is compared against.\n26\t\n27\tThe synth_default baseline runs on the HOST (trusted repo code; note its known caveat below).\n28\t\n29\tUsage (on the box, after ingesting prices up to window_end + 1 day):\n30\t  export LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=...   # not needed here, but the offline bundle build needs network,\n31\t                                  # and so does the first run of a window (registrations)\n32\t  uv run python -m synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict --campaign <name> \\\\\n33\t      --window-start <YYYY-MM-DD> --window-end <YYYY-MM-DD>\n34\t\"\"\"\n35\t\n36\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n37\t\n38\timport argparse\n39\timport hashlib\n40\timport json\n41\timport os\n42\timport shutil\n43\timport subprocess\n44\timport tempfile\n45\tfrom collections.abc import Mapping\n46\tfrom datetime import date, datetime, timedelta\n47\tfrom pathlib import Path\n48\t\n49\timport pandas as pd\n50\t\n51\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores, get_registrations, get_scores_save_order\n52\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.scoring import Registrations, SaveOrder\n53\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark import workspace\n54\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import CONTEXT_MODES, DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\n55\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.nomination import parse_champion\n56\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.campaign import PACKAGED_BASELINE, baseline_modeling_path\n57\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.sandbox.run_sandbox import DEFAULT_IMAGE, image_identity, sandbox_cmd\n58\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.manifest import sha256_file\n59\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.evaluate import COMPETITIONS, evaluate_candidate, prepare_offline_bundle\n60\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\n61\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_DIR, CALENDAR_ENV, VIEW_FILE\n62\t\n63\tGENERATE_SCRIPT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / \"generate_predictions.py\"\n64\tSANDBOX_IMAGE = DEFAULT_IMAGE\n65\tSANDBOX_MEMORY_GB = 12\n66\tSANDBOX_CPUS = 12\n67\t# Prompt grid density per format: hourly for the 24h competitions, 10-minute for crypto-1h. It is\n68\t# the density the validator scores at — one request per asset per hour for the 24h competitions,\n69\t# one per 10 minutes for crypto-1h — but not the phase: the kept request sits at an arbitrary\n70\t# minute inside its bucket, so a grid prompt is up to half a cadence from the one the field\n71\t# answered. --live-prompts replaces the grid with the real start_times.\n72\tCADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n73\t# Written into the workspace for --live-prompts; the generator reads one file per (asset, format).\n74\tPROMPT_TIMES_DIR = \"prompt_times\"\n75\t# A prompt's paths depend on the champion's code and on the seed it was generated with, so both\n76\t# are in the cache path: nothing else distinguishes two runs of the same window.\n77\tDEFAULT_PREDICTIONS_CACHE = Path(\"predictions_cache\")\n78\t# Beside the scores and rewards in the window's offline bundle (prepare_offline_bundle).\n79\tREGISTRATIONS_FILE = \"registrations.json\"\n80\tSAVE_ORDER_FILE = \"scores_save_order.json\"\n81\t\n82\t# Constitution rule 7: a champion that uses randomness seeds every generator from this, and it\n83\t# is set only here, at evaluation. Absent during a campaign, so an agent's own runs vary.\n84\tSEED_ENV = \"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\"\n85\t# Python salts string hashing per process, so a champion that derives its own seed from hash() —\n86\t# which rule 7 does not reach, and campaign-3's champion does — draws different paths on every\n87\t# run. Pinning this makes those champions reproducible too. Must be set before the interpreter\n88\t# starts, which is why it travels as an env var rather than being set in the generator.\n89\tHASH_SEED_ENV = \"PYTHONHASHSEED\"\n90\tDEFAULT_SEED = 0\n91\t\n92\t\n93\tdef generation_env(seed: int) -> dict[str, str]:\n94\t    \"\"\"What a generation process needs to be reproducible.\"\"\"\n95\t    return {SEED_ENV: str(seed), HASH_SEED_ENV: str(seed % 2**32)}\n96\t\n97\t\n98\tdef generation_start(window_start: str, time_length: int, lead_in: bool) -> str:\n99\t    \"\"\"Where generation begins for a competition, given the scoring window's start.\n100\t\n101\t    The window scores every prompt whose `scored_time` falls inside it, but a prompt is scored one\n102\t    horizon after it starts — so the earliest scored prompts began BEFORE the window. Generating\n103\t    only from `window_start` leaves those without a prediction, and the validator's moving average\n104\t    then treats the candidate as a miner that joined late: `prepare_df_for_moving_average` backfills\n105\t    every earlier timestamp with the worst score in the field. The candidate eats a full horizon of\n106\t    worst-score rounds it never had the chance to answer.\n107\t\n108\t    Leading generation in by one horizon makes the candidate's first `scored_time` equal the\n109\t    field's, so it is never classified as new. Lengthening the window does not substitute for this:\n110\t    it dilutes the backfilled rounds without removing them.\n111\t    \"\"\"\n112\t    start = pd.Timestamp(window_start, tz=\"UTC\")\n113\t    if lead_in:\n114\t        start -= pd.Timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n115\t    return start.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n116\t\n117\t\n118\tdef live_prompt_starts(window: tuple[str, str], lead_in: bool) -> dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]]:\n119\t    \"\"\"The start_times the validator actually scored, per (asset, time_length).\n120\t\n121\t    Read from the offline bundle, which is built first: `scored_time - time_length` is the prompt's\n122\t    own start, and the bundle already holds only the density-tapered set the validator kept — one\n123\t    request per asset per hour for the 24h competitions, one per 10 minutes for crypto-1h. The\n124\t    issued set behind it is ten times larger and was never scored.\n125\t    \"\"\"\n126\t    out: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n127\t    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n128\t        start = pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)).to_pydatetime()\n129\t        end = pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime()\n130\t        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n131\t            # The scores are keyed on scored_time, so ask from one horizon after the first prompt.\n132\t            scores = get_miner_scores(\n133\t                start + timedelta(seconds=comp.time_length), end, asset, comp.time_length, comp.time_increment\n134\t            )\n135\t            starts = [] if scores.empty else sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n136\t            out[(asset, comp.time_length)] = [t for t in starts if start <= t.to_pydatetime() < end]\n137\t            print(f\"  {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {len(out[(asset, comp.time_length)])} prompts\", flush=True)\n138\t    return out\n139\t\n140\t\n141\tdef write_prompt_times(root: Path, prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]]) -> None:\n142\t    \"\"\"One JSON list of start_times per (asset, time_length), named as the generator expects.\"\"\"\n143\t    directory = root / PROMPT_TIMES_DIR\n144\t    directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n145\t    for (asset, time_length), starts in prompt_starts.items():\n146\t        path = directory / f\"{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n147\t        path.write_text(json.dumps([pd.Timestamp(t).isoformat() for t in starts]))\n148\t\n149\t\n150\tdef run(cmd: list[str], what: str, env: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> None:\n151\t    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, env={**os.environ, **env} if env else None)\n152\t    if result.returncode != 0:\n153\t        tail = (result.stdout + result.stderr).decode(errors=\"replace\")[-2000:]\n154\t        raise RuntimeError(f\"{what} failed (rc={result.returncode}):\\n{tail}\")\n155\t\n156\t\n157\tdef docker_limits() -> tuple[int, int]:\n158\t    \"\"\"SANDBOX_CPUS/MEMORY capped to what the local daemon actually has — a laptop's Docker\n159\t    Desktop VM is often smaller than the host, and docker hard-errors on an over-ask.\"\"\"\n160\t    result = subprocess.run([\"docker\", \"info\", \"--format\", \"{{.NCPU}} {{.MemTotal}}\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n161\t    if result.returncode != 0:\n162\t        return SANDBOX_CPUS, SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB\n163\t    ncpu, mem_bytes = result.stdout.split()\n164\t    return min(SANDBOX_CPUS, int(ncpu)), min(SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB, int(mem_bytes) // 1024**3)\n165\t\n166\t\n167\tdef baseline_identity(modeling: Path) -> str:\n168\t    \"\"\"Short content hash of the baseline's source, so changing it cannot reuse its cache.\"\"\"\n169\t    return hashlib.sha256(modeling.read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n170\t\n171\t\n172\tdef predictions_cache(\n173\t    root: Path,\n174\t    champion: str,\n175\t    seed: int,\n176\t    live_prompts: bool,\n177\t    lead_in: bool,\n178\t    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n179\t    calendar_sha: str | None = None,\n180\t) -> Path:\n181\t    \"\"\"Where one champion's generated paths live, across runs.\n182\t\n183\t    Everything that decides WHICH prompts get generated is in the path. Two runs that disagree on\n184\t    any of it answer the same window at different instants, and scoring matches the nearest\n185\t    prediction within half an hour — so a shared tree would serve one run the other's predictions,\n186\t    silently reproducing the behaviour the differing flag exists to measure.\n187\t    \"\"\"\n188\t    mode = \"live-prompts\" if live_prompts else \"cadence-grid\"\n189\t    if not lead_in:\n190\t        mode += \"-no-lead-in\"\n191\t    if context_mode != \"ohlcv\":\n192\t        mode += f\"-{context_mode}\"\n193\t    if calendar_sha is not None:\n194\t        mode += f\"-calendar-{calendar_sha[:12]}\"\n195\t    return root / champion / f\"seed={seed}\" / mode\n196\t\n197\t\n198\tdef sandbox(\n199\t    workspace: Path,\n200\t    data_root: Path,\n201\t    home: Path,\n202\t    inner: str,\n203\t    network: str,\n204\t    gpus: bool,\n205\t    cpus: int = SANDBOX_CPUS,\n206\t    memory_gb: int = SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB,\n207\t    env: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n208\t    predictions: Path | None = None,\n209\t) -> list[str]:\n210\t    return sandbox_cmd(\n211\t        workspace=workspace,\n212\t        snapshot=data_root,  # mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data\n213\t        home=home,\n214\t        image=SANDBOX_IMAGE,\n215\t        memory_gb=memory_gb,\n216\t        cpus=cpus,\n217\t        network=network,\n218\t        env=env or {},\n219\t        inner_cmd=inner,\n220\t        gpus=gpus,\n221\t        predictions=predictions,\n222\t    )\n223\t\n224\t\n225\tdef clone_champion(bundle: Path, sha: str, dest: Path) -> None:\n226\t    run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"-q\", str(bundle), str(dest)], f\"clone {bundle}\")\n227\t    run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(dest), \"checkout\", \"-q\", sha], f\"checkout {sha}\")\n228\t\n229\t\n230\tdef generate_all(\n231\t    workspace: Path,\n232\t    data_root: Path,\n233\t    home: Path,\n234\t    window: tuple[str, str],\n235\t    gpus: bool,\n236\t    limits: tuple[int, int],\n237\t    seed: int,\n238\t    lead_in: bool = True,\n239\t    prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] | None = None,\n240\t    cache: Path | None = None,\n241\t    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n242\t    calendar: Path | None = None,\n243\t) -> None:\n244\t    \"\"\"One --network none sandbox run per (competition, asset).\n245\t\n246\t    The sandbox inherits nothing from the host, so the seed, the prompt start_times and the calendar\n247\t    have to be handed to it explicitly — the latter two as files in the workspace, since it has no\n248\t    network. The calendar is the campaign's, frozen at its cutoff, not the one in the data root.\"\"\"\n249\t    if not GENERATE_SCRIPT.exists():  # packaging regression: it must ship with the package\n250\t        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"generation core missing at {GENERATE_SCRIPT}\")\n251\t    shutil.copy(GENERATE_SCRIPT, workspace / \"generate_predictions.py\")\n252\t    if prompt_starts is not None:\n253\t        write_prompt_times(workspace, prompt_starts)\n254\t    env = generation_env(seed)\n255\t    if calendar is not None:\n256\t        (workspace / CALENDAR_DIR).mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n257\t        shutil.copy(calendar, workspace / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE)\n258\t        env[CALENDAR_ENV] = f\"/workspace/{CALENDAR_DIR}/{VIEW_FILE}\"\n259\t    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n260\t        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n261\t            inner = (\n262\t                \"uv run python generate_predictions.py\"\n263\t                \" --modeling agent/modeling.py\"\n264\t                f\" --asset {asset}\"\n265\t                f\" --window-start {generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)}\"\n266\t                f\" --window-end {window[1]}\"\n267\t                \" --data-root /workspace/market_data --out-dir predictions\"\n268\t                f\" --cadence-minutes {CADENCE_MINUTES[comp.time_length]}\"\n269\t                f\" --time-increment {comp.time_increment} --time-length {comp.time_length}\"\n270\t            )\n271\t            if prompt_starts is not None:\n272\t                inner += f\" --prompt-times {PROMPT_TIMES_DIR}/{asset}_{comp.time_length}.json\"\n273\t            if context_mode != \"ohlcv\":\n274\t                inner += f\" --context {context_mode}\"\n275\t            try:\n276\t                run(\n277\t                    sandbox(\n278\t                        workspace,\n279\t                        data_root,\n280\t                        home,\n281\t                        inner,\n282\t                        network=\"none\",\n283\t                        gpus=gpus,\n284\t                        cpus=limits[0],\n285\t                        memory_gb=limits[1],\n286\t                        env=env,\n287\t                        predictions=cache,\n288\t                    ),\n289\t                    f\"generate {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\",\n290\t                )\n291\t            except RuntimeError as exc:\n292\t                # Per-asset fault isolation, mirroring evaluate_candidate: a dead asset (real\n293\t                # case: SPYX — feed retired mid-July, no prices in any post-cutoff window) must\n294\t                # not sink the leg. No predictions -> the asset lands in assets_failed at scoring.\n295\t                print(f\"  SKIP {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {str(exc).splitlines()[-1]}\", flush=True)\n296\t                continue\n297\t            print(f\"  generated {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\", flush=True)\n298\t\n299\t\n300\tdef reported_context_days(predictions: Path) -> int | None:\n301\t    \"\"\"The CONTEXT_DAYS every (competition, asset) run reported in its day indexes, None when there is\n302\t    no index. An index written before the field reads as the default.\"\"\"\n303\t    reported = {\n304\t        json.loads(index.read_text()).get(\"context_days\", DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS)\n305\t        for index in predictions.glob(\"*/*/date=*.json\")\n306\t    }\n307\t    if len(reported) > 1:\n308\t        raise RuntimeError(f\"the generation runs under {predictions} report different CONTEXT_DAYS: {sorted(reported)}\")\n309\t    return reported.pop() if reported else None\n310\t\n311\t\n312\tdef context_heads(predictions: Path, window: tuple[str, str], lead_in: bool) -> dict[str, int]:\n313\t    \"\"\"Per asset with a context of the window that did not start on a real close, the most minutes one\n314\t    ran before its first, from the day indexes of the window's generation days. An index written\n315\t    before the field reads as 0.\"\"\"\n316\t    first = min(pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window[0], c.time_length, lead_in)) for c in COMPETITIONS)\n317\t    end = pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\")\n318\t    heads: dict[str, int] = {}\n319\t    for index in predictions.glob(\"*/*/date=*.json\"):\n320\t        day = pd.Timestamp(index.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\"), tz=\"UTC\")\n321\t        if day < first.normalize() or day >= end:\n322\t            continue\n323\t        minutes = json.loads(index.read_text()).get(\"context_head_nan_minutes\", 0)\n324\t        asset = index.parent.parent.name\n325\t        if minutes:\n326\t            heads[asset] = max(heads.get(asset, 0), minutes)\n327\t    return dict(sorted(heads.items()))\n328\t\n329\t\n330\tdef stores_starting_late(\n331\t    data_root: Path, window_start: str, context_days: int, lead_in: bool\n332\t) -> dict[str, tuple[date, date]]:\n333\t    \"\"\"Per asset whose first partition in `data_root` is after the day its first context begins: that\n334\t    day, and the first partition's.\"\"\"\n335\t    begins: dict[str, date] = {}\n336\t    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n337\t        start = pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window_start, comp.time_length, lead_in))\n338\t        day = (start - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days)).date()\n339\t        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n340\t            begins[asset] = min(begins.get(asset, day), day)\n341\t    late = {}\n342\t    for asset, day in begins.items():\n343\t        stored = (data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\").glob(\"date=*.parquet\")\n344\t        first = min((date.fromisoformat(p.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\")) for p in stored), default=None)\n345\t        if first is not None and first > day:\n346\t            late[asset] = (day, first)\n347\t    return late\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tdef generate_baseline(\n351\t    modeling: Path,\n352\t    data_root: Path,\n353\t    out_dir: Path,\n354\t    window: tuple[str, str],\n355\t    seed: int,\n356\t    lead_in: bool = True,\n357\t    prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] | None = None,\n358\t) -> None:\n359\t    \"\"\"Host-side, trusted repo code. Known caveat: the subnet's default generator ignores\n360\t    context_prices and anchors on a price it fetches ITSELF — for past prompts that anchor may be\n361\t    wrong, so read the baseline's verdict with suspicion and drop it from the article if broken.\"\"\"\n362\t    if prompt_starts is not None:\n363\t        write_prompt_times(out_dir.parent, prompt_starts)\n364\t    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n365\t    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n366\t        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n367\t            times = out_dir.parent / PROMPT_TIMES_DIR / f\"{asset}_{comp.time_length}.json\"\n368\t            try:\n369\t                run(\n370\t                    [\n371\t                        \"uv\",\n372\t                        \"run\",\n373\t                        \"python\",\n374\t                        str(GENERATE_SCRIPT),\n375\t                        *(\"--modeling\", str(modeling)),\n376\t                        *(\"--asset\", asset),\n377\t                        *(\"--window-start\", generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)),\n378\t                        *(\"--window-end\", window[1]),\n379\t                        *(\"--data-root\", str(data_root), \"--out-dir\", str(out_dir)),\n380\t                        *(\"--cadence-minutes\", str(CADENCE_MINUTES[comp.time_length])),\n381\t                        *(\"--time-increment\", str(comp.time_increment), \"--time-length\", str(comp.time_length)),\n382\t                        *((\"--prompt-times\", str(times)) if prompt_starts is not None else ()),\n383\t                    ],\n384\t                    f\"baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\",\n385\t                    env=generation_env(seed),\n386\t                )\n387\t            except RuntimeError as exc:\n388\t                print(f\"  SKIP baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {str(exc).splitlines()[-1]}\", flush=True)\n389\t                continue\n390\t            print(f\"  baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\", flush=True)\n391\t\n392\t\n393\tdef registration_span(window: tuple[str, str], simulate_registration: datetime | None) -> tuple[datetime, datetime]:\n394\t    \"\"\"The span whose registrations can split the scored data: from one horizon before the window\n395\t    (and a competition window earlier with a simulated registration) to the window's end.\"\"\"\n396\t    start = pd.Timestamp(window[0], tz=\"UTC\") - pd.Timedelta(seconds=max(c.time_length for c in COMPETITIONS))\n397\t    if simulate_registration is not None:\n398\t        start -= pd.Timedelta(days=max(c.window_days for c in COMPETITIONS))\n399\t    return start.to_pydatetime(), pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime()\n400\t\n401\t\n402\tdef registrations_record(span: tuple[datetime, datetime], rows: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n403\t    \"\"\"The field's registrations over `span` (`get_registrations` rows), as kept beside a window's\n404\t    bundle and in its verdicts.\"\"\"\n405\t    return {\n406\t        \"since\": span[0].isoformat(),\n407\t        \"until\": span[1].isoformat(),\n408\t        \"rows\": [\n409\t            {\"miner_uid\": int(row.miner_uid), \"hotkey\": row.hotkey, \"created_at\": row.created_at.isoformat()}\n410\t            for row in rows.itertuples()\n411\t        ],\n412\t    }\n413\t\n414\t\n415\tdef registrations_from(record: dict) -> dict[int, list[datetime]]:\n416\t    \"\"\"uid -> the registration times of its occupants in a `registrations_record`, ascending.\"\"\"\n417\t    out: dict[int, list[datetime]] = {}\n418\t    for row in record[\"rows\"]:\n419\t        out.setdefault(int(row[\"miner_uid\"]), []).append(datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"created_at\"]))\n420\t    return {uid: sorted(times) for uid, times in out.items()}\n421\t\n422\t\n423\tdef _covers(record: dict, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> bool:\n424\t    return (record.get(\"since\"), record.get(\"until\")) == (span[0].isoformat(), span[1].isoformat())\n425\t\n426\t\n427\tdef recorded_registrations(campaign_dir: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict | None:\n428\t    \"\"\"The registrations record any of the campaign's verdicts holds for `span`, or None.\"\"\"\n429\t    for path in sorted(campaign_dir.glob(\"**/verdict*/verdict.json\")):\n430\t        record = json.loads(path.read_text()).get(\"registrations\") or {}\n431\t        if _covers(record, span):\n432\t            return record\n433\t    return None\n434\t\n435\t\n436\tdef window_registrations(bundle: Path, campaign_dir: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict:\n437\t    \"\"\"The field's registrations record for `span`, from local files before the API: the window's\n438\t    offline bundle, then the campaign's verdicts. Written into the bundle when it lacked it.\"\"\"\n439\t    cached = bundle / REGISTRATIONS_FILE\n440\t    if cached.exists() and _covers(record := json.loads(cached.read_text()), span):\n441\t        return record\n442\t    record = recorded_registrations(campaign_dir, span)\n443\t    if record is None:\n444\t        print(\"reading the field's uid registrations from the Synth API...\", flush=True)\n445\t        record = registrations_record(span, get_registrations(*span))\n446\t    cached.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n447\t    return record\n448\t\n449\t\n450\tdef window_save_order(bundle: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict[int, SaveOrder]:\n451\t    \"\"\"time_length -> the validator's save order over `span` (`get_scores_save_order`), from the\n452\t    window's offline bundle before the API. Written into the bundle when it lacked it.\"\"\"\n453\t    cached = bundle / SAVE_ORDER_FILE\n454\t    if cached.exists() and _covers(record := json.loads(cached.read_text()), span):\n455\t        orders = record[\"orders\"]\n456\t    else:\n457\t        print(\"reading the validator's save order from the Synth API...\", flush=True)\n458\t        orders = {\n459\t            str(time_length): [\n460\t                {\"scored_time\": t.isoformat(), \"assets\": assets}\n461\t                for t, assets in get_scores_save_order(*span, time_length).items()\n462\t            ]\n463\t            for time_length in sorted({c.time_length for c in COMPETITIONS})\n464\t        }\n465\t        record = {\"since\": span[0].isoformat(), \"until\": span[1].isoformat(), \"orders\": orders}\n466\t        cached.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n467\t    return {int(tl): {pd.Timestamp(row[\"scored_time\"]): row[\"assets\"] for row in rows} for tl, rows in orders.items()}\n468\t\n469\t\n470\tdef engine_rev() -> str | None:\n471\t    \"\"\"The synth-lib commit this host scores with, or None when it was not installed from git.\"\"\"\n472\t    try:\n473\t        return workspace._host_synth_lib_rev()\n474\t    except RuntimeError:\n475\t        return None\n476\t\n477\t\n478\tdef score(\n479\t    name: str,\n480\t    predictions: Path,\n481\t    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n482\t    window_days: int,\n483\t    out_dir: Path,\n484\t    simulate_registration: datetime | None = None,\n485\t    registrations: Registrations | None = None,\n486\t    save_order: Mapping[int, SaveOrder] | None = None,\n487\t) -> dict:\n488\t    result = evaluate_candidate(\n489\t        name,\n490\t        predictions,\n491\t        window_end,\n492\t        window_days,\n493\t        out_dir,\n494\t        simulate_registration,\n495\t        registrations,\n496\t        save_order,\n497\t        match_tolerance_minutes=CADENCE_MINUTES,\n498\t    )\n499\t    mrt = result[\"mean_reward_vs_top\"]\n500\t    result[\"score\"] = round(100 * mrt, 1) if mrt is not None else None\n501\t    ranks = [c[\"rank\"] for c in result[\"per_competition\"].values() if c[\"rank\"] is not None]\n502\t    # Crude by design (field sizes differ per competition) but requested for cross-window\n503\t    # comparisons: the Score is softmax-top-weighted and near-zero for everyone off the podium,\n504\t    # while the mean rank still moves in the mid-field.\n505\t    result[\"mean_competition_rank\"] = round(sum(ranks) / len(ranks), 1) if ranks else None\n506\t    return result\n507\t\n508\t\n509\tdef verdict_payload(\n510\t    result: dict,\n511\t    sha: str | None,\n512\t    window: tuple[str, str],\n513\t    seed: int,\n514\t    simulate_registration: datetime | None,\n515\t    live_prompts: bool,\n516\t    registrations: dict | None = None,\n517\t    engine: str | None = None,\n518\t    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n519\t    calendar: dict | None = None,\n520\t    context_days: int | None = None,\n521\t    context_head_nan_minutes: dict[str, int] | None = None,\n522\t) -> dict:\n523\t    return {\n524\t        \"score\": result[\"score\"],\n525\t        \"mean_competition_rank\": result[\"mean_competition_rank\"],\n526\t        \"score_definition\": \"100 x mean over competitions of min(1, candidate_total_reward /\"\n527\t        \" top_other_miner_total_reward) (validator reward_weight summed over the window; bounded\"\n528\t        \" 0-100: 0 = earned nothing, 100 = matched or beat the field's best in every competition;\"\n529\t        \" per-competition beats_field flags when the cap binds)\",\n530\t        \"mean_reward_vs_top\": result[\"mean_reward_vs_top\"],\n531\t        \"mean_competition_percentile\": result[\"mean_competition_percentile\"],\n532\t        \"per_competition\": result[\"per_competition\"],\n533\t        \"window\": {\n534\t            \"start\": window[0],\n535\t            \"end\": window[1],\n536\t            \"note\": \"pseudo-out-of-sample: after the \"\n537\t            \"data cutoff, but agents had live field-API access during their runs\",\n538\t        },\n539\t        \"champion_sha\": sha,\n540\t        \"sandbox_image\": image_identity(SANDBOX_IMAGE),\n541\t        \"cadence_minutes\": CADENCE_MINUTES,\n542\t        \"num_simulations\": 1000,\n543\t        # What a stochastic champion was seeded with. Without it \"seeded\" is unverifiable and\n544\t        # a re-score of this window cannot reproduce the number above.\n545\t        \"seed\": seed,\n546\t        # A Score with a simulated registration includes the onboarding backfill every real\n547\t        # miner pays once. It answers a different question from the steady-state Score and the\n548\t        # two must never be read as the same number.\n549\t        \"simulate_registration\": simulate_registration.isoformat() if simulate_registration else None,\n550\t        # False means the candidate answered a cadence grid and cadence_minutes describes it; True\n551\t        # means it answered the validator's own scored start_times and the grid was not used.\n552\t        \"live_prompts\": live_prompts,\n553\t        # Field uids registered inside the scored span (registrations_record); a re-score of the\n554\t        # same span reads them back instead of the API.\n555\t        \"registrations\": registrations,\n556\t        # The synth-lib commit that scored this verdict; None for an install not made from git.\n557\t        \"engine_rev\": engine,\n558\t        # What simulate() received as context_prices (generate_predictions.CONTEXT_MODES).\n559\t        \"context_prices\": context_mode,\n560\t        # How many days of it: the champion's CONTEXT_DAYS, as its generation runs reported it.\n561\t        \"context_days\": context_days,\n562\t        # Per asset whose contexts did not all start on a real close, the most minutes one ran before it.\n563\t        \"context_head_nan_minutes\": context_head_nan_minutes,\n564\t        # The event calendar the champion was handed: the one its campaign's agents saw, or None.\n565\t        \"calendar\": calendar,\n566\t    }\n567\t\n568\t\n569\tdef main() -> None:  # noqa: C901 — a linear operator script; splitting it would obscure the order\n570\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n571\t    ap.add_argument(\"--campaign\", required=True)\n572\t    ap.add_argument(\"--window-start\", required=True)\n573\t    ap.add_argument(\"--window-end\", required=True)\n574\t    ap.add_argument(\"--results-dir\", type=Path, default=Path(\"campaign_results\"))\n575\t    ap.add_argument(\"--data-root\", type=Path, default=Path(\"market_data\"))\n576\t    ap.add_argument(\"--legs\", nargs=\"*\", default=None, help=\"default: every leg with a CHAMPION\")\n577\t    ap.add_argument(\n578\t        \"--tag\",\n579\t        default=None,\n580\t        help=\"write into verdict-<tag>/ instead of verdict/ — use for extra windows (in-sample \"\n581\t        \"diagnostics) so they never overwrite the pre-registered window's canonical verdict\",\n582\t    )\n583\t    ap.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"rescore legs whose verdict.json already exists\")\n584\t    ap.add_argument(\"--skip-baseline\", action=\"store_true\")\n585\t    ap.add_argument(\n586\t        \"--no-lead-in\",\n587\t        action=\"store_true\",\n588\t        help=\"generate only inside the window, as before the lead-in fix: the first horizon of \"\n589\t        \"scored prompts then has no prediction and the candidate is backfilled at the field's \"\n590\t        \"worst score. For reproducing an old verdict, not for scoring a new one.\",\n591\t    )\n592\t    ap.add_argument(\n593\t        \"--baseline-module\",\n594\t        default=PACKAGED_BASELINE,\n595\t        help=\"dotted module path or file path exposing simulate() (default: the packaged control)\",\n596\t    )\n597\t    ap.add_argument(\n598\t        \"--simulate-registration\",\n599\t        action=\"store_true\",\n600\t        help=\"score the champion as a miner that registered on --window-start: the prompts issued \"\n601\t        \"before that day are dropped, so its first score lands a horizon later and the validator's \"\n602\t        \"moving average treats it as a late joiner, backfilling the preceding window at the field's \"\n603\t        \"worst score. This is what a champion earns in its first days live, and it is NOT comparable \"\n604\t        \"to a Score without it — give it its own --tag.\",\n605\t    )\n606\t    ap.add_argument(\n607\t        \"--live-prompts\",\n608\t        action=\"store_true\",\n609\t        help=\"generate at the start_times the validator actually scored, instead of an even cadence \"\n610\t        \"grid. Same number of prompts, different minutes: the kept request sits at an arbitrary \"\n611\t        \"minute in its bucket, so without this the candidate answers up to half a cadence away from \"\n612\t        \"the prompt the field answered and is scored against that prompt's realized path.\",\n613\t    )\n614\t    ap.add_argument(\n615\t        \"--seed\",\n616\t        type=int,\n617\t        default=DEFAULT_SEED,\n618\t        help=f\"value of {SEED_ENV} for generation, recorded in the verdict. Constitution rule 7 \"\n619\t        \"has a stochastic champion seed every generator from it, so a re-score reproduces\",\n620\t    )\n621\t    ap.add_argument(\n622\t        \"--predictions-cache\",\n623\t        type=Path,\n624\t        default=DEFAULT_PREDICTIONS_CACHE,\n625\t        help=\"where generated paths are kept between runs, under <sha>/seed=<n>/<prompt mode>. A day already \"\n626\t        \"covering every prompt of a re-score is reused instead of regenerated. Roughly 5 GB per \"\n627\t        \"champion per 10-day window, so prune it rather than letting it grow\",\n628\t    )\n629\t    ap.add_argument(\n630\t        \"--context\",\n631\t        choices=CONTEXT_MODES,\n632\t        default=\"ohlcv\",\n633\t        help=\"what the champion's simulate() receives as context_prices: the minute OHLCV frame, or \"\n634\t        \"'close', the Series of minute closes (NaN kept) of the contract before OHLCV, for a champion \"\n635\t        \"written against it\",\n636\t    )\n637\t    ap.add_argument(\"--no-gpu\", action=\"store_true\")\n638\t    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-work\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep clones + predictions for inspection\")\n639\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n640\t\n641\t    campaign_dir = args.results_dir / args.campaign\n642\t    window = (args.window_start, args.window_end)\n643\t    window_end = pd.Timestamp(args.window_end, tz=\"UTC\")\n644\t    window_days = (date.fromisoformat(args.window_end) - date.fromisoformat(args.window_start)).days\n645\t    data_root = args.data_root.resolve()\n646\t\n647\t    # The registration day is the window's first: the champion is deployed as the window opens.\n648\t    sim_reg = pd.Timestamp(args.window_start, tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime() if args.simulate_registration else None\n649\t    print(\"building the offline scores bundle for the scoring window (network, resumable)...\", flush=True)\n650\t    bundle = prepare_offline_bundle(window_end, window_days, simulate_registration=sim_reg)\n651\t    prompt_starts = None\n652\t    if args.live_prompts:\n653\t        print(\"reading the validator's scored prompt start_times from the bundle...\", flush=True)\n654\t        prompt_starts = live_prompt_starts(window, lead_in=not args.no_lead_in)\n655\t\n656\t    span = registration_span(window, sim_reg)\n657\t    record = window_registrations(bundle, campaign_dir, span)\n658\t    registrations = registrations_from(record)\n659\t    save_order = window_save_order(bundle, span)\n660\t    print(f\"{len(record['rows'])} field registrations in {span[0]:%Y-%m-%d} -> {span[1]:%Y-%m-%d}\", flush=True)\n661\t    engine = engine_rev()\n662\t    calendar = campaign_dir / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE\n663\t    calendar_sha = sha256_file(calendar) if calendar.exists() else None\n664\t    calendar_record = (\n665\t        {\"sha256\": calendar_sha, \"events\": len(pd.read_parquet(calendar))} if calendar_sha is not None else None\n666\t    )\n667\t    if calendar_record is not None:\n668\t        print(f\"calendar: {calendar_record['events']} events, sha256 {calendar_sha[:12]}\", flush=True)\n669\t\n670\t    legs = args.legs or sorted(p.name for p in campaign_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir() and (p / \"CHAMPION\").exists())\n671\t    work = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f\"verdict-{args.campaign}-\"))\n672\t    limits = docker_limits()\n673\t    if limits != (SANDBOX_CPUS, SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB):\n674\t        print(f\"docker daemon smaller than the reference box: sandboxes capped at {limits[0]} cpus / {limits[1]} GB\")\n675\t    print(f\"legs: {legs}; work dir: {work}\", flush=True)\n676\t\n677\t    verdict_name = f\"verdict-{args.tag}\" if args.tag else \"verdict\"\n678\t    for leg in legs:\n679\t        verdict_dir = campaign_dir / leg / verdict_name\n680\t        out = verdict_dir / \"verdict.json\"\n681\t        if out.exists() and not args.force:\n682\t            print(f\"[{leg}] {out} already exists — SKIPPING (pass --force to rescore)\", flush=True)\n683\t            continue\n684\t        champion = parse_champion(campaign_dir / leg / \"CHAMPION\")\n685\t        clone = work / leg\n686\t        home = work / f\"{leg}-home\"\n687\t        home.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n688\t        print(f\"[{leg}] clone @ {champion.sha}\", flush=True)\n689\t        clone_champion(campaign_dir / leg / \"workspace.bundle\", champion.sha, clone)\n690\t        print(f\"[{leg}] phase 1: uv sync (network)\", flush=True)\n691\t        run(\n692\t            sandbox(\n693\t                clone, data_root, home, \"uv sync\", network=\"bridge\", gpus=False, cpus=limits[0], memory_gb=limits[1]\n694\t            ),\n695\t            f\"{leg} uv sync\",\n696\t        )\n697\t        print(f\"[{leg}] phase 2: generation (--network none)\", flush=True)\n698\t        cache = predictions_cache(\n699\t            args.predictions_cache,\n700\t            champion.sha,\n701\t            args.seed,\n702\t            args.live_prompts,\n703\t            not args.no_lead_in,\n704\t            args.context,\n705\t            calendar_sha,\n706\t        )\n707\t        generate_all(\n708\t            clone,\n709\t            data_root,\n710\t            home,\n711\t            window,\n712\t            gpus=not args.no_gpu,\n713\t            limits=limits,\n714\t            seed=args.seed,\n715\t            lead_in=not args.no_lead_in,\n716\t            prompt_starts=prompt_starts,\n717\t            cache=cache,\n718\t            context_mode=args.context,\n719\t            calendar=calendar if calendar_sha is not None else None,\n720\t        )\n721\t        context_days = reported_context_days(cache)\n722\t        heads = context_heads(cache, window, not args.no_lead_in)\n723\t        for asset, minutes in heads.items():\n724\t            print(\n725\t                f\"[{leg}] {asset}: contexts start with up to {minutes} NaN minutes ({minutes / 1440:.1f} days)\",\n726\t                flush=True,\n727\t            )\n728\t        if context_days is not None:\n729\t            late = stores_starting_late(data_root, args.window_start, context_days, not args.no_lead_in)\n730\t            for asset, (begins, first) in late.items():\n731\t                print(\n732\t                    f\"[{leg}] WARNING: {asset}'s first partition in {data_root} is {first}, after {begins}, where \"\n733\t                    f\"its first context begins. If the market traded before {first}, ingest those days and delete \"\n734\t                    f\"{cache / asset}, whose day files keep the truncated contexts they were generated with.\",\n735\t                    flush=True,\n736\t                )\n737\t        print(f\"[{leg}] scoring (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days})\", flush=True)\n738\t        result = score(leg, cache, window_end, window_days, verdict_dir, sim_reg, registrations, save_order)\n739\t        payload = verdict_payload(\n740\t            result,\n741\t            champion.sha,\n742\t            window,\n743\t            args.seed,\n744\t            sim_reg,\n745\t            args.live_prompts,\n746\t            record,\n747\t            engine,\n748\t            args.context,\n749\t            calendar_record,\n750\t            context_days,\n751\t            heads,\n752\t        )\n753\t        verdict_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n754\t        out.write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n755\t        print(f\"[{leg}] score={result['score']} mean_rank={result['mean_competition_rank']} -> {out}\", flush=True)\n756\t        if not args.keep_work:\n757\t            shutil.rmtree(clone, ignore_errors=True)\n758\t\n759\t    baseline_dir = campaign_dir / \"baselines\" / \"synth_default\" / verdict_name\n760\t    baseline_out = baseline_dir / \"verdict.json\"\n761\t    if not args.skip_baseline and baseline_out.exists() and not args.force:\n762\t        print(f\"[baseline] {baseline_out} already exists — SKIPPING (pass --force to rescore)\", flush=True)\n763\t    elif not args.skip_baseline:\n764\t        baseline_modeling = baseline_modeling_path(args.baseline_module)\n765\t        predictions = predictions_cache(\n766\t            args.predictions_cache, \"synth_default\", args.seed, args.live_prompts, not args.no_lead_in\n767\t        )\n768\t        print(\"[baseline] generating (host)\", flush=True)\n769\t        generate_baseline(\n770\t            baseline_modeling,\n771\t            data_root,\n772\t            predictions,\n773\t            window,\n774\t            seed=args.seed,\n775\t            lead_in=not args.no_lead_in,\n776\t            prompt_starts=prompt_starts,\n777\t        )\n778\t        result = score(\n779\t            \"synth_default\", predictions, window_end, window_days, baseline_dir, sim_reg, registrations, save_order\n780\t        )\n781\t        payload = verdict_payload(\n782\t            result,\n783\t            None,\n784\t            window,\n785\t            args.seed,\n786\t            sim_reg,\n787\t            args.live_prompts,\n788\t            record,\n789\t            engine,\n790\t            context_days=reported_context_days(predictions),\n791\t            context_head_nan_minutes=context_heads(predictions, window, not args.no_lead_in),\n792\t        )\n793\t        baseline_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n794\t        baseline_out.write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n795\t        print(\n796\t            f\"[baseline] score={result['score']} mean_rank={result['mean_competition_rank']} -> {baseline_out}\",\n797\t            flush=True,\n798\t        )\n799\t\n800\t    if not args.keep_work:\n801\t        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n802\t\n803\t\n804\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n805\t    main()\n806\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"2d74c0d9-579e-450b-9751-46ba59814761","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:15:45.930Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/root/.claude/projects/-workspace/b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad/tool-results/bkfxn1o7m.txt","content":"\"\"\"Verdict runner: score archived champions, in the sandbox.\n\nFor each leg under campaign_results/<campaign>/ that has a CHAMPION + workspace.bundle:\n  1. `git clone` the bundle and check out CHAMPION.sha — the scored code is provably the\n     nominated code, not whatever the workspace drifted to after nomination.\n  2. Copy in generate_predictions.py (self-contained by design).\n  3. Phase 1 (network=bridge): `uv sync` in the clone — bundles are git-only, the venv must be\n     built, and that needs the network. It fetches only pinned packages, never prices.\n  4. Phase 2 (network=none): one sandbox run per (competition, asset) generating predictions.\n     The data root is mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data; the model itself only ever\n     receives the pre-prompt context (see generate_predictions.py). Predictions are\n     written to a cache mounted at /workspace/predictions that outlives the workspace, one file\n     per day, so a re-score of a window already generated skips straight to scoring.\n  5. On the host: evaluate_candidate() against the offline bundle -> per-competition rank +\n     simulated emissions -> Score = 100 x mean over competitions of reward_vs_top (see\n     evaluate.reward_metrics; the unweighted mean mirrors the subnet's 1/3-per-competition\n     emission split, and the softmaxed reward_weight makes top positions worth more, which a\n     rank percentile would flatten). Field uids that changed hands are split as live does, from\n     registrations read from the Synth API once per window and kept in local files: the\n     window's offline bundle and each verdict. A re-score reads those first. Late joiners are\n     backfilled from each minute's first-saved prompt, read the same way into the bundle.\n  6. Write campaign_results/<campaign>/<leg>/verdict-<tag>/ — the verdict.json, the\n     per-competition rank-evolution charts, the per-prompt CRPS frames and the recomputed field\n     rewards. One directory per verdict, so a re-score under --tag cannot overwrite the artifacts\n     of the verdict it is compared against.\n\nThe synth_default baseline runs on the HOST (trusted repo code; note its known caveat below).\n\nUsage (on the box, after ingesting prices up to window_end + 1 day):\n  export LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=...   # not needed here, but the offline bundle build needs network,\n                                  # and so does the first run of a window (registrations)\n  uv run python -m synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict --campaign <name> \\\\\n      --window-start <YYYY-MM-DD> --window-end <YYYY-MM-DD>\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\nfrom collections.abc import Mapping\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores, get_registrations, get_scores_save_order\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.scoring import Registrations, SaveOrder\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark import workspace\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import CONTEXT_MODES, DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.nomination import parse_champion\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.campaign import PACKAGED_BASELINE, baseline_modeling_path\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.sandbox.run_sandbox import DEFAULT_IMAGE, image_identity, sandbox_cmd\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.manifest import sha256_file\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.evaluate import COMPETITIONS, evaluate_candidate, prepare_offline_bundle\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_DIR, CALENDAR_ENV, VIEW_FILE\n\nGENERATE_SCRIPT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / \"generate_predictions.py\"\nSANDBOX_IMAGE = DEFAULT_IMAGE\nSANDBOX_MEMORY_GB = 12\nSANDBOX_CPUS = 12\n# Prompt grid density per format: hourly for the 24h competitions, 10-minute for crypto-1h. It is\n# the density the validator scores at — one request per asset per hour for the 24h competitions,\n# one per 10 minutes for crypto-1h — but not the phase: the kept request sits at an arbitrary\n# minute inside its bucket, so a grid prompt is up to half a cadence from the one the field\n# answered. --live-prompts replaces the grid with the real start_times.\nCADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n# Written into the workspace for --live-prompts; the generator reads one file per (asset, format).\nPROMPT_TIMES_DIR = \"prompt_times\"\n# A prompt's paths depend on the champion's code and on the seed it was generated with, so both\n# are in the cache path: nothing else distinguishes two runs of the same window.\nDEFAULT_PREDICTIONS_CACHE = Path(\"predictions_cache\")\n# Beside the scores and rewards in the window's offline bundle (prepare_offline_bundle).\nREGISTRATIONS_FILE = \"registrations.json\"\nSAVE_ORDER_FILE = \"scores_save_order.json\"\n\n# Constitution rule 7: a champion that uses randomness seeds every generator from this, and it\n# is set only here, at evaluation. Absent during a campaign, so an agent's own runs vary.\nSEED_ENV = \"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\"\n# Python salts string hashing per process, so a champion that derives its own seed from hash() —\n# which rule 7 does not reach, and campaign-3's champion does — draws different paths on every\n# run. Pinning this makes those champions reproducible too. Must be set before the interpreter\n# starts, which is why it travels as an env var rather than being set in the generator.\nHASH_SEED_ENV = \"PYTHONHASHSEED\"\nDEFAULT_SEED = 0\n\n\ndef generation_env(seed: int) -> dict[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"What a generation process needs to be reproducible.\"\"\"\n    return {SEED_ENV: str(seed), HASH_SEED_ENV: str(seed % 2**32)}\n\n\ndef generation_start(window_start: str, time_length: int, lead_in: bool) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Where generation begins for a competition, given the scoring window's start.\n\n    The window scores every prompt whose `scored_time` falls inside it, but a prompt is scored one\n    horizon after it starts — so the earliest scored prompts began BEFORE the window. Generating\n    only from `window_start` leaves those without a prediction, and the validator's moving average\n    then treats the candidate as a miner that joined late: `prepare_df_for_moving_average` backfills\n    every earlier timestamp with the worst score in the field. The candidate eats a full horizon of\n    worst-score rounds it never had the chance to answer.\n\n    Leading generation in by one horizon makes the candidate's first `scored_time` equal the\n    field's, so it is never classified as new. Lengthening the window does not substitute for this:\n    it dilutes the backfilled rounds without removing them.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = pd.Timestamp(window_start, tz=\"UTC\")\n    if lead_in:\n        start -= pd.Timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n    return start.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef live_prompt_starts(window: tuple[str, str], lead_in: bool) -> dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]]:\n    \"\"\"The start_times the validator actually scored, per (asset, time_length).\n\n    Read from the offline bundle, which is built first: `scored_time - time_length` is the prompt's\n    own start, and the bundle already holds only the density-tapered set the validator kept — one\n    request per asset per hour for the 24h competitions, one per 10 minutes for crypto-1h. The\n    issued set behind it is ten times larger and was never scored.\n    \"\"\"\n    out: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        start = pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)).to_pydatetime()\n        end = pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime()\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            # The scores are keyed on scored_time, so ask from one horizon after the first prompt.\n            scores = get_miner_scores(\n                start + timedelta(seconds=comp.time_length), end, asset, comp.time_length, comp.time_increment\n            )\n            starts = [] if scores.empty else sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n            out[(asset, comp.time_length)] = [t for t in starts if start <= t.to_pydatetime() < end]\n            print(f\"  {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {len(out[(asset, comp.time_length)])} prompts\", flush=True)\n    return out\n\n\ndef write_prompt_times(root: Path, prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"One JSON list of start_times per (asset, time_length), named as the generator expects.\"\"\"\n    directory = root / PROMPT_TIMES_DIR\n    directory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for (asset, time_length), starts in prompt_starts.items():\n        path = directory / f\"{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n        path.write_text(json.dumps([pd.Timestamp(t).isoformat() for t in starts]))\n\n\ndef run(cmd: list[str], what: str, env: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> None:\n    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, env={**os.environ, **env} if env else None)\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        tail = (result.stdout + result.stderr).decode(errors=\"replace\")[-2000:]\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{what} failed (rc={result.returncode}):\\n{tail}\")\n\n\ndef docker_limits() -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"SANDBOX_CPUS/MEMORY capped to what the local daemon actually has — a laptop's Docker\n    Desktop VM is often smaller than the host, and docker hard-errors on an over-ask.\"\"\"\n    result = subprocess.run([\"docker\", \"info\", \"--format\", \"{{.NCPU}} {{.MemTotal}}\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        return SANDBOX_CPUS, SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB\n    ncpu, mem_bytes = result.stdout.split()\n    return min(SANDBOX_CPUS, int(ncpu)), min(SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB, int(mem_bytes) // 1024**3)\n\n\ndef baseline_identity(modeling: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Short content hash of the baseline's source, so changing it cannot reuse its cache.\"\"\"\n    return hashlib.sha256(modeling.read_bytes()).hexdigest()[:12]\n\n\ndef predictions_cache(\n    root: Path,\n    champion: str,\n    seed: int,\n    live_prompts: bool,\n    lead_in: bool,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    calendar_sha: str | None = None,\n) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where one champion's generated paths live, across runs.\n\n    Everything that decides WHICH prompts get generated is in the path. Two runs that disagree on\n    any of it answer the same window at different instants, and scoring matches the nearest\n    prediction within half an hour — so a shared tree would serve one run the other's predictions,\n    silently reproducing the behaviour the differing flag exists to measure.\n    \"\"\"\n    mode = \"live-prompts\" if live_prompts else \"cadence-grid\"\n    if not lead_in:\n        mode += \"-no-lead-in\"\n    if context_mode != \"ohlcv\":\n        mode += f\"-{context_mode}\"\n    if calendar_sha is not None:\n        mode += f\"-calendar-{calendar_sha[:12]}\"\n    return root / champion / f\"seed={seed}\" / mode\n\n\ndef sandbox(\n    workspace: Path,\n    data_root: Path,\n    home: Path,\n    inner: str,\n    network: str,\n    gpus: bool,\n    cpus: int = SANDBOX_CPUS,\n    memory_gb: int = SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB,\n    env: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n    predictions: Path | None = None,\n) -> list[str]:\n    return sandbox_cmd(\n        workspace=workspace,\n        snapshot=data_root,  # mounted read-only at /workspace/market_data\n        home=home,\n        image=SANDBOX_IMAGE,\n        memory_gb=memory_gb,\n        cpus=cpus,\n        network=network,\n        env=env or {},\n        inner_cmd=inner,\n        gpus=gpus,\n        predictions=predictions,\n    )\n\n\ndef clone_champion(bundle: Path, sha: str, dest: Path) -> None:\n    run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"-q\", str(bundle), str(dest)], f\"clone {bundle}\")\n    run([\"git\", \"-C\", str(dest), \"checkout\", \"-q\", sha], f\"checkout {sha}\")\n\n\ndef generate_all(\n    workspace: Path,\n    data_root: Path,\n    home: Path,\n    window: tuple[str, str],\n    gpus: bool,\n    limits: tuple[int, int],\n    seed: int,\n    lead_in: bool = True,\n    prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] | None = None,\n    cache: Path | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    calendar: Path | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"One --network none sandbox run per (competition, asset).\n\n    The sandbox inherits nothing from the host, so the seed, the prompt start_times and the calendar\n    have to be handed to it explicitly — the latter two as files in the workspace, since it has no\n    network. The calendar is the campaign's, frozen at its cutoff, not the one in the data root.\"\"\"\n    if not GENERATE_SCRIPT.exists():  # packaging regression: it must ship with the package\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"generation core missing at {GENERATE_SCRIPT}\")\n    shutil.copy(GENERATE_SCRIPT, workspace / \"generate_predictions.py\")\n    if prompt_starts is not None:\n        write_prompt_times(workspace, prompt_starts)\n    env = generation_env(seed)\n    if calendar is not None:\n        (workspace / CALENDAR_DIR).mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n        shutil.copy(calendar, workspace / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE)\n        env[CALENDAR_ENV] = f\"/workspace/{CALENDAR_DIR}/{VIEW_FILE}\"\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            inner = (\n                \"uv run python generate_predictions.py\"\n                \" --modeling agent/modeling.py\"\n                f\" --asset {asset}\"\n                f\" --window-start {generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)}\"\n                f\" --window-end {window[1]}\"\n                \" --data-root /workspace/market_data --out-dir predictions\"\n                f\" --cadence-minutes {CADENCE_MINUTES[comp.time_length]}\"\n                f\" --time-increment {comp.time_increment} --time-length {comp.time_length}\"\n            )\n            if prompt_starts is not None:\n                inner += f\" --prompt-times {PROMPT_TIMES_DIR}/{asset}_{comp.time_length}.json\"\n            if context_mode != \"ohlcv\":\n                inner += f\" --context {context_mode}\"\n            try:\n                run(\n                    sandbox(\n                        workspace,\n                        data_root,\n                        home,\n                        inner,\n                        network=\"none\",\n                        gpus=gpus,\n                        cpus=limits[0],\n                        memory_gb=limits[1],\n                        env=env,\n                        predictions=cache,\n                    ),\n                    f\"generate {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\",\n                )\n            except RuntimeError as exc:\n                # Per-asset fault isolation, mirroring evaluate_candidate: a dead asset (real\n                # case: SPYX — feed retired mid-July, no prices in any post-cutoff window) must\n                # not sink the leg. No predictions -> the asset lands in assets_failed at scoring.\n                print(f\"  SKIP {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {str(exc).splitlines()[-1]}\", flush=True)\n                continue\n            print(f\"  generated {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef reported_context_days(predictions: Path) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"The CONTEXT_DAYS every (competition, asset) run reported in its day indexes, None when there is\n    no index. An index written before the field reads as the default.\"\"\"\n    reported = {\n        json.loads(index.read_text()).get(\"context_days\", DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS)\n        for index in predictions.glob(\"*/*/date=*.json\")\n    }\n    if len(reported) > 1:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"the generation runs under {predictions} report different CONTEXT_DAYS: {sorted(reported)}\")\n    return reported.pop() if reported else None\n\n\ndef context_heads(predictions: Path, window: tuple[str, str], lead_in: bool) -> dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Per asset with a context of the window that did not start on a real close, the most minutes one\n    ran before its first, from the day indexes of the window's generation days. An index written\n    before the field reads as 0.\"\"\"\n    first = min(pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window[0], c.time_length, lead_in)) for c in COMPETITIONS)\n    end = pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\")\n    heads: dict[str, int] = {}\n    for index in predictions.glob(\"*/*/date=*.json\"):\n        day = pd.Timestamp(index.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\"), tz=\"UTC\")\n        if day < first.normalize() or day >= end:\n            continue\n        minutes = json.loads(index.read_text()).get(\"context_head_nan_minutes\", 0)\n        asset = index.parent.parent.name\n        if minutes:\n            heads[asset] = max(heads.get(asset, 0), minutes)\n    return dict(sorted(heads.items()))\n\n\ndef stores_starting_late(\n    data_root: Path, window_start: str, context_days: int, lead_in: bool\n) -> dict[str, tuple[date, date]]:\n    \"\"\"Per asset whose first partition in `data_root` is after the day its first context begins: that\n    day, and the first partition's.\"\"\"\n    begins: dict[str, date] = {}\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        start = pd.Timestamp(generation_start(window_start, comp.time_length, lead_in))\n        day = (start - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days)).date()\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            begins[asset] = min(begins.get(asset, day), day)\n    late = {}\n    for asset, day in begins.items():\n        stored = (data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\").glob(\"date=*.parquet\")\n        first = min((date.fromisoformat(p.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\")) for p in stored), default=None)\n        if first is not None and first > day:\n            late[asset] = (day, first)\n    return late\n\n\ndef generate_baseline(\n    modeling: Path,\n    data_root: Path,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    window: tuple[str, str],\n    seed: int,\n    lead_in: bool = True,\n    prompt_starts: dict[tuple[str, int], list[pd.Timestamp]] | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Host-side, trusted repo code. Known caveat: the subnet's default generator ignores\n    context_prices and anchors on a price it fetches ITSELF — for past prompts that anchor may be\n    wrong, so read the baseline's verdict with suspicion and drop it from the article if broken.\"\"\"\n    if prompt_starts is not None:\n        write_prompt_times(out_dir.parent, prompt_starts)\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for comp in COMPETITIONS:\n        for asset in comp.asset_list:\n            times = out_dir.parent / PROMPT_TIMES_DIR / f\"{asset}_{comp.time_length}.json\"\n            try:\n                run(\n                    [\n                        \"uv\",\n                        \"run\",\n                        \"python\",\n                        str(GENERATE_SCRIPT),\n                        *(\"--modeling\", str(modeling)),\n                        *(\"--asset\", asset),\n                        *(\"--window-start\", generation_start(window[0], comp.time_length, lead_in)),\n                        *(\"--window-end\", window[1]),\n                        *(\"--data-root\", str(data_root), \"--out-dir\", str(out_dir)),\n                        *(\"--cadence-minutes\", str(CADENCE_MINUTES[comp.time_length])),\n                        *(\"--time-increment\", str(comp.time_increment), \"--time-length\", str(comp.time_length)),\n                        *((\"--prompt-times\", str(times)) if prompt_starts is not None else ()),\n                    ],\n                    f\"baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\",\n                    env=generation_env(seed),\n                )\n            except RuntimeError as exc:\n                print(f\"  SKIP baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}: {str(exc).splitlines()[-1]}\", flush=True)\n                continue\n            print(f\"  baseline {asset} tl={comp.time_length}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef registration_span(window: tuple[str, str], simulate_registration: datetime | None) -> tuple[datetime, datetime]:\n    \"\"\"The span whose registrations can split the scored data: from one horizon before the window\n    (and a competition window earlier with a simulated registration) to the window's end.\"\"\"\n    start = pd.Timestamp(window[0], tz=\"UTC\") - pd.Timedelta(seconds=max(c.time_length for c in COMPETITIONS))\n    if simulate_registration is not None:\n        start -= pd.Timedelta(days=max(c.window_days for c in COMPETITIONS))\n    return start.to_pydatetime(), pd.Timestamp(window[1], tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime()\n\n\ndef registrations_record(span: tuple[datetime, datetime], rows: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The field's registrations over `span` (`get_registrations` rows), as kept beside a window's\n    bundle and in its verdicts.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"since\": span[0].isoformat(),\n        \"until\": span[1].isoformat(),\n        \"rows\": [\n            {\"miner_uid\": int(row.miner_uid), \"hotkey\": row.hotkey, \"created_at\": row.created_at.isoformat()}\n            for row in rows.itertuples()\n        ],\n    }\n\n\ndef registrations_from(record: dict) -> dict[int, list[datetime]]:\n    \"\"\"uid -> the registration times of its occupants in a `registrations_record`, ascending.\"\"\"\n    out: dict[int, list[datetime]] = {}\n    for row in record[\"rows\"]:\n        out.setdefault(int(row[\"miner_uid\"]), []).append(datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"created_at\"]))\n    return {uid: sorted(times) for uid, times in out.items()}\n\n\ndef _covers(record: dict, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> bool:\n    return (record.get(\"since\"), record.get(\"until\")) == (span[0].isoformat(), span[1].isoformat())\n\n\ndef recorded_registrations(campaign_dir: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict | None:\n    \"\"\"The registrations record any of the campaign's verdicts holds for `span`, or None.\"\"\"\n    for path in sorted(campaign_dir.glob(\"**/verdict*/verdict.json\")):\n        record = json.loads(path.read_text()).get(\"registrations\") or {}\n        if _covers(record, span):\n            return record\n    return None\n\n\ndef window_registrations(bundle: Path, campaign_dir: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The field's registrations record for `span`, from local files before the API: the window's\n    offline bundle, then the campaign's verdicts. Written into the bundle when it lacked it.\"\"\"\n    cached = bundle / REGISTRATIONS_FILE\n    if cached.exists() and _covers(record := json.loads(cached.read_text()), span):\n        return record\n    record = recorded_registrations(campaign_dir, span)\n    if record is None:\n        print(\"reading the field's uid registrations from the Synth API...\", flush=True)\n        record = registrations_record(span, get_registrations(*span))\n    cached.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return record\n\n\ndef window_save_order(bundle: Path, span: tuple[datetime, datetime]) -> dict[int, SaveOrder]:\n    \"\"\"time_length -> the validator's save order over `span` (`get_scores_save_order`), from the\n    window's offline bundle before the API. Written into the bundle when it lacked it.\"\"\"\n    cached = bundle / SAVE_ORDER_FILE\n    if cached.exists() and _covers(record := json.loads(cached.read_text()), span):\n        orders = record[\"orders\"]\n    else:\n        print(\"reading the validator's save order from the Synth API...\", flush=True)\n        orders = {\n            str(time_length): [\n                {\"scored_time\": t.isoformat(), \"assets\": assets}\n                for t, assets in get_scores_save_order(*span, time_length).items()\n            ]\n            for time_length in sorted({c.time_length for c in COMPETITIONS})\n        }\n        record = {\"since\": span[0].isoformat(), \"until\": span[1].isoformat(), \"orders\": orders}\n        cached.write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    return {int(tl): {pd.Timestamp(row[\"scored_time\"]): row[\"assets\"] for row in rows} for tl, rows in orders.items()}\n\n\ndef engine_rev() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"The synth-lib commit this host scores with, or None when it was not installed from git.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return workspace._host_synth_lib_rev()\n    except RuntimeError:\n        return None\n\n\ndef score(\n    name: str,\n    predictions: Path,\n    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n    window_days: int,\n    out_dir: Path,\n    simulate_registration: datetime | None = None,\n    registrations: Registrations | None = None,\n    save_order: Mapping[int, SaveOrder] | None = None,\n) -> dict:\n    result = evaluate_candidate(\n        name,\n        predictions,\n        window_end,\n        window_days,\n        out_dir,\n        simulate_registration,\n        registrations,\n        save_order,\n        match_tolerance_minutes=CADENCE_MINUTES,\n    )\n    mrt = result[\"mean_reward_vs_top\"]\n    result[\"score\"] = round(100 * mrt, 1) if mrt is not None else None\n    ranks = [c[\"rank\"] for c in result[\"per_competition\"].values() if c[\"rank\"] is not None]\n    # Crude by design (field sizes differ per competition) but requested for cross-window\n    # comparisons: the Score is softmax-top-weighted and near-zero for everyone off the podium,\n    # while the mean rank still moves in the mid-field.\n    result[\"mean_competition_rank\"] = round(sum(ranks) / len(ranks), 1) if ranks else None\n    return result\n\n\ndef verdict_payload(\n    result: dict,\n    sha: str | None,\n    window: tuple[str, str],\n    seed: int,\n    simulate_registration: datetime | None,\n    live_prompts: bool,\n    registrations: dict | None = None,\n    engine: str | None = None,\n    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n    calendar: dict | None = None,\n    context_days: int | None = None,\n    context_head_nan_minutes: dict[str, int] | None = None,\n) -> dict:\n    return {\n        \"score\": result[\"score\"],\n        \"mean_competition_rank\": result[\"mean_competition_rank\"],\n        \"score_definition\": \"100 x mean over competitions of min(1, candidate_total_reward /\"\n        \" top_other_miner_total_reward) (validator reward_weight summed over the window; bounded\"\n        \" 0-100: 0 = earned nothing, 100 = matched or beat the field's best in every competition;\"\n        \" per-competition beats_field flags when the cap binds)\",\n        \"mean_reward_vs_top\": result[\"mean_reward_vs_top\"],\n        \"mean_competition_percentile\": result[\"mean_competition_percentile\"],\n        \"per_competition\": result[\"per_competition\"],\n        \"window\": {\n            \"start\": window[0],\n            \"end\": window[1],\n            \"note\": \"pseudo-out-of-sample: after the \"\n            \"data cutoff, but agents had live field-API access during their runs\",\n        },\n        \"champion_sha\": sha,\n        \"sandbox_image\": image_identity(SANDBOX_IMAGE),\n        \"cadence_minutes\": CADENCE_MINUTES,\n        \"num_simulations\": 1000,\n        # What a stochastic champion was seeded with. Without it \"seeded\" is unverifiable and\n        # a re-score of this window cannot reproduce the number above.\n        \"seed\": seed,\n        # A Score with a simulated registration includes the onboarding backfill every real\n        # miner pays once. It answers a different question from the steady-state Score and the\n        # two must never be read as the same number.\n        \"simulate_registration\": simulate_registration.isoformat() if simulate_registration else None,\n        # False means the candidate answered a cadence grid and cadence_minutes describes it; True\n        # means it answered the validator's own scored start_times and the grid was not used.\n        \"live_prompts\": live_prompts,\n        # Field uids registered inside the scored span (registrations_record); a re-score of the\n        # same span reads them back instead of the API.\n        \"registrations\": registrations,\n        # The synth-lib commit that scored this verdict; None for an install not made from git.\n        \"engine_rev\": engine,\n        # What simulate() received as context_prices (generate_predictions.CONTEXT_MODES).\n        \"context_prices\": context_mode,\n        # How many days of it: the champion's CONTEXT_DAYS, as its generation runs reported it.\n        \"context_days\": context_days,\n        # Per asset whose contexts did not all start on a real close, the most minutes one ran before it.\n        \"context_head_nan_minutes\": context_head_nan_minutes,\n        # The event calendar the champion was handed: the one its campaign's agents saw, or None.\n        \"calendar\": calendar,\n    }\n\n\ndef main() -> None:  # noqa: C901 — a linear operator script; splitting it would obscure the order\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--campaign\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-start\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--window-end\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--results-dir\", type=Path, default=Path(\"campaign_results\"))\n    ap.add_argument(\"--data-root\", type=Path, default=Path(\"market_data\"))\n    ap.add_argument(\"--legs\", nargs=\"*\", default=None, help=\"default: every leg with a CHAMPION\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--tag\",\n        default=None,\n        help=\"write into verdict-<tag>/ instead of verdict/ — use for extra windows (in-sample \"\n        \"diagnostics) so they never overwrite the pre-registered window's canonical verdict\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"rescore legs whose verdict.json already exists\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--skip-baseline\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--no-lead-in\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"generate only inside the window, as before the lead-in fix: the first horizon of \"\n        \"scored prompts then has no prediction and the candidate is backfilled at the field's \"\n        \"worst score. For reproducing an old verdict, not for scoring a new one.\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--baseline-module\",\n        default=PACKAGED_BASELINE,\n        help=\"dotted module path or file path exposing simulate() (default: the packaged control)\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--simulate-registration\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"score the champion as a miner that registered on --window-start: the prompts issued \"\n        \"before that day are dropped, so its first score lands a horizon later and the validator's \"\n        \"moving average treats it as a late joiner, backfilling the preceding window at the field's \"\n        \"worst score. This is what a champion earns in its first days live, and it is NOT comparable \"\n        \"to a Score without it — give it its own --tag.\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--live-prompts\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"generate at the start_times the validator actually scored, instead of an even cadence \"\n        \"grid. Same number of prompts, different minutes: the kept request sits at an arbitrary \"\n        \"minute in its bucket, so without this the candidate answers up to half a cadence away from \"\n        \"the prompt the field answered and is scored against that prompt's realized path.\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--seed\",\n        type=int,\n        default=DEFAULT_SEED,\n        help=f\"value of {SEED_ENV} for generation, recorded in the verdict. Constitution rule 7 \"\n        \"has a stochastic champion seed every generator from it, so a re-score reproduces\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--predictions-cache\",\n        type=Path,\n        default=DEFAULT_PREDICTIONS_CACHE,\n        help=\"where generated paths are kept between runs, under <sha>/seed=<n>/<prompt mode>. A day already \"\n        \"covering every prompt of a re-score is reused instead of regenerated. Roughly 5 GB per \"\n        \"champion per 10-day window, so prune it rather than letting it grow\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--context\",\n        choices=CONTEXT_MODES,\n        default=\"ohlcv\",\n        help=\"what the champion's simulate() receives as context_prices: the minute OHLCV frame, or \"\n        \"'close', the Series of minute closes (NaN kept) of the contract before OHLCV, for a champion \"\n        \"written against it\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--no-gpu\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-work\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep clones + predictions for inspection\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    campaign_dir = args.results_dir / args.campaign\n    window = (args.window_start, args.window_end)\n    window_end = pd.Timestamp(args.window_end, tz=\"UTC\")\n    window_days = (date.fromisoformat(args.window_end) - date.fromisoformat(args.window_start)).days\n    data_root = args.data_root.resolve()\n\n    # The registration day is the window's first: the champion is deployed as the window opens.\n    sim_reg = pd.Timestamp(args.window_start, tz=\"UTC\").to_pydatetime() if args.simulate_registration else None\n    print(\"building the offline scores bundle for the scoring window (network, resumable)...\", flush=True)\n    bundle = prepare_offline_bundle(window_end, window_days, simulate_registration=sim_reg)\n    prompt_starts = None\n    if args.live_prompts:\n        print(\"reading the validator's scored prompt start_times from the bundle...\", flush=True)\n        prompt_starts = live_prompt_starts(window, lead_in=not args.no_lead_in)\n\n    span = registration_span(window, sim_reg)\n    record = window_registrations(bundle, campaign_dir, span)\n    registrations = registrations_from(record)\n    save_order = window_save_order(bundle, span)\n    print(f\"{len(record['rows'])} field registrations in {span[0]:%Y-%m-%d} -> {span[1]:%Y-%m-%d}\", flush=True)\n    engine = engine_rev()\n    calendar = campaign_dir / CALENDAR_DIR / VIEW_FILE\n    calendar_sha = sha256_file(calendar) if calendar.exists() else None\n    calendar_record = (\n        {\"sha256\": calendar_sha, \"events\": len(pd.read_parquet(calendar))} if calendar_sha is not None else None\n    )\n    if calendar_record is not None:\n        print(f\"calendar: {calendar_record['events']} events, sha256 {calendar_sha[:12]}\", flush=True)\n\n    legs = args.legs or sorted(p.name for p in campaign_dir.iterdir() if p.is_dir() and (p / \"CHAMPION\").exists())\n    work = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f\"verdict-{args.campaign}-\"))\n    limits = docker_limits()\n    if limits != (SANDBOX_CPUS, SANDBOX_MEMORY_GB):\n        print(f\"docker daemon smaller than the reference box: sandboxes capped at {limits[0]} cpus / {limits[1]} GB\")\n    print(f\"legs: {legs}; work dir: {work}\", flush=True)\n\n    verdict_name = f\"verdict-{args.tag}\" if args.tag else \"verdict\"\n    for leg in legs:\n        verdict_dir = campaign_dir / leg / verdict_name\n        out = verdict_dir / \"verdict.json\"\n        if out.exists() and not args.force:\n            print(f\"[{leg}] {out} already exists — SKIPPING (pass --force to rescore)\", flush=True)\n            continue\n        champion = parse_champion(campaign_dir / leg / \"CHAMPION\")\n        clone = work / leg\n        home = work / f\"{leg}-home\"\n        home.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        print(f\"[{leg}] clone @ {champion.sha}\", flush=True)\n        clone_champion(campaign_dir / leg / \"workspace.bundle\", champion.sha, clone)\n        print(f\"[{leg}] phase 1: uv sync (network)\", flush=True)\n        run(\n            sandbox(\n                clone, data_root, home, \"uv sync\", network=\"bridge\", gpus=False, cpus=limits[0], memory_gb=limits[1]\n            ),\n            f\"{leg} uv sync\",\n        )\n        print(f\"[{leg}] phase 2: generation (--network none)\", flush=True)\n        cache = predictions_cache(\n            args.predictions_cache,\n            champion.sha,\n            args.seed,\n            args.live_prompts,\n            not args.no_lead_in,\n            args.context,\n            calendar_sha,\n        )\n        generate_all(\n            clone,\n            data_root,\n            home,\n            window,\n            gpus=not args.no_gpu,\n            limits=limits,\n            seed=args.seed,\n            lead_in=not args.no_lead_in,\n            prompt_starts=prompt_starts,\n            cache=cache,\n            context_mode=args.context,\n            calendar=calendar if calendar_sha is not None else None,\n        )\n        context_days = reported_context_days(cache)\n        heads = context_heads(cache, window, not args.no_lead_in)\n        for asset, minutes in heads.items():\n            print(\n                f\"[{leg}] {asset}: contexts start with up to {minutes} NaN minutes ({minutes / 1440:.1f} days)\",\n                flush=True,\n            )\n        if context_days is not None:\n            late = stores_starting_late(data_root, args.window_start, context_days, not args.no_lead_in)\n            for asset, (begins, first) in late.items():\n                print(\n                    f\"[{leg}] WARNING: {asset}'s first partition in {data_root} is {first}, after {begins}, where \"\n                    f\"its first context begins. If the market traded before {first}, ingest those days and delete \"\n                    f\"{cache / asset}, whose day files keep the truncated contexts they were generated with.\",\n                    flush=True,\n                )\n        print(f\"[{leg}] scoring (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days})\", flush=True)\n        result = score(leg, cache, window_end, window_days, verdict_dir, sim_reg, registrations, save_order)\n        payload = verdict_payload(\n            result,\n            champion.sha,\n            window,\n            args.seed,\n            sim_reg,\n            args.live_prompts,\n            record,\n            engine,\n            args.context,\n            calendar_record,\n            context_days,\n            heads,\n        )\n        verdict_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        out.write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n        print(f\"[{leg}] score={result['score']} mean_rank={result['mean_competition_rank']} -> {out}\", flush=True)\n        if not args.keep_work:\n            shutil.rmtree(clone, ignore_errors=True)\n\n    baseline_dir = campaign_dir / \"baselines\" / \"synth_default\" / verdict_name\n    baseline_out = baseline_dir / \"verdict.json\"\n    if not args.skip_baseline and baseline_out.exists() and not args.force:\n        print(f\"[baseline] {baseline_out} already exists — SKIPPING (pass --force to rescore)\", flush=True)\n    elif not args.skip_baseline:\n        baseline_modeling = baseline_modeling_path(args.baseline_module)\n        predictions = predictions_cache(\n            args.predictions_cache, \"synth_default\", args.seed, args.live_prompts, not args.no_lead_in\n        )\n        print(\"[baseline] generating (host)\", flush=True)\n        generate_baseline(\n            baseline_modeling,\n            data_root,\n            predictions,\n            window,\n            seed=args.seed,\n            lead_in=not args.no_lead_in,\n            prompt_starts=prompt_starts,\n        )\n        result = score(\n            \"synth_default\", predictions, window_end, window_days, baseline_dir, sim_reg, registrations, save_order\n        )\n        payload = verdict_payload(\n            result,\n            None,\n            window,\n            args.seed,\n            sim_reg,\n            args.live_prompts,\n            record,\n            engine,\n            context_days=reported_context_days(predictions),\n            context_head_nan_minutes=context_heads(predictions, window, not args.no_lead_in),\n        )\n        baseline_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        baseline_out.write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n        print(\n            f\"[baseline] score={result['score']} mean_rank={result['mean_competition_rank']} -> {baseline_out}\",\n            flush=True,\n        )\n\n    if not args.keep_work:\n        shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","numLines":806,"startLine":1,"totalLines":806}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01U7TN9QYCM2KpBhfQ9493xq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
