{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011CgwD53CXKD9akxRRSK7SC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AhvBMn3Q71fQ6mFyNhPYiF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/agent/predict.py","content":"\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n\nUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\nAnswers, with agent/modeling.py, the prompts the validator scored in the --days before --eval-end,\nat the start times it actually used (read from the offline field bundle), then scores them with\nbacktest() (validator CRPS + rank vs the real field, from the same bundle). A prompt is scored one\nhorizon after it starts, so generation begins one horizon before the scored days.\n--cadence-minutes N answers an even grid over the same span instead; each scored prompt is then\nanswered by the grid point at or before it.\n\n--crps-only scores CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid (--cadence-minutes,\nby default every 60 minutes for 24h prompts and every 10 for 1h, on the round hour): no field, no\nrank, and any window of the snapshot, including before the bundle's span. Compare models on the same\ngrid with it; it is not an absolute calibration level. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula.\n\nWorks on every asset. A minute without a trade is a flat candle with trade_count 0. Prices load\nthrough the same lenient path the scored evaluation uses, so a NaN close (no price at all) reaches\nsimulate() rather than stopping the run — your model must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate).\nThe context spans the CONTEXT_DAYS your modeling.py sets (7 without it), and the days before an\nasset's first trade, or before the snapshot's first day, are NaN.\n\nWhen the snapshot carries an event calendar ($SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR), the summary is followed by\nyour gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type and\nover those that hold none: where an event costs you, that gap is wider.\n\n--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\ngeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\nfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n\nThe context a prompt gets ends BEFORE its start_time, and that is not an off-by-one. The store\nlabels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t closes at t+60s — and that close is\nthe first point the prompt is scored against. A prompt is also issued before the start_time it is\nscored from (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS). Ending the context at t would hand the model the answer to\nits own first step, and a model tuned that way is optimising a problem it will not be scored on.\n\n=== Campaign additions (the fast, parallel research loop) ===\n\n--assets A,B,C | all | crypto | comequ, --jobs N, --modeling PATH, --out FILE.parquet, --stride K,\n--offset-minutes M and --sweep switch to the PARALLEL mode. It is the same pipeline as above, split\ninto (asset, span-of-days) tasks that run in a process pool:\n\n  * generation goes through synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions.generate() — the function the\n    verdict runs — with the same context cut (context_slice) and the same float32 day layout;\n  * every CRPS comes from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration.score_crps(), i.e. the validator's\n    own calculate_crps_for_miner / calculate_total_score_for_miner. Nothing here reimplements the\n    metric.\n\nIn the parallel mode the default prompt set is still the validator's own scored start times; the\nfield is then JOINED from the bundle per prompt (best / median miner CRPS on the same prompt, and\nwhere our mean CRPS would sit among the miners' means). That join is a diagnostic, not the\nvalidator's moving-average rank: use the plain single-asset mode for that. With --crps-only the\nprompts are an even grid and nothing is joined.\n\nThe parallel mode prints one line per asset and a coefficient-weighted aggregate per competition\n(weights = synth.validator.moving_average.ASSET_COEFFICIENTS, the weights the validator's own\naggregation gives each asset's prompt scores).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor, as_completed\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES, competition_for, slug_for\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest, score_crps\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (\n    context_days_of,\n    context_slice,\n    load_minute_prices,\n    load_module,\n    nan_head_minutes,\n)\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import generate as generate_days\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns\n\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n\nDEFAULT_MODELING = AGENT_DIR / \"modeling.py\"\n# Each run writes its predictions to its own directory under this one.\nPREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\"\n# Must match synth_lib.backtester.config._OFFLINE_ENV_VAR.\nOFFLINE_ROOT_ENV = \"SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT\"\n# backtest()'s default miner_id: the rows of prompt_df that are yours.\nCANDIDATE_ID = 999\n# The --crps-only grid, by time_length. Must match synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict.CADENCE_MINUTES.\nCRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n# Parallel mode: how many days of prompts one task generates and scores.\nTASK_DAYS = {86_400: 4, 3_600: 2}\n\n\ndef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n\n    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n\n\ndef require_offline_bundle() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails unless backtest() reads the field from the offline bundle.\n\n    backtest() reads scores and rewards a day past --eval-end; from the live API that is data from\n    after your cutoff.\"\"\"\n    if not os.environ.get(OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV):\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"{OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV} is not set, so backtest() would read the field from the live API, past \"\n            f\"--eval-end. The harness points it at the bundle in your snapshot; restore it.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot (anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd).\"\"\"\n    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n\n\ndef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime, first_prompt: datetime) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n\n    The context's days before the asset's first partition are not missing: the context holds them\n    as NaN. The days from the first prompt on are never exempt.\n    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(asset)\n    first = min((p.name for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\")), default=\"\")\n    holes_from = min(first, f\"date={first_prompt.date().isoformat()}.parquet\")\n    missing = []\n    cursor = start.date()\n    while cursor <= end.date():\n        name = f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n        if name >= holes_from and not (root / name).exists():\n            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only): it ends at the campaign's data_cutoff, and DATA.md gives \"\n            f\"each asset's first and last day. Choose --eval-end / --days so that the window and its \"\n            f\"CONTEXT_DAYS stay on days {root} holds.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef prompt_times(\n    asset: str,\n    end: datetime,\n    days: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    time_increment: int,\n    cadence_minutes: int | None = None,\n    offset_minutes: int = 0,\n) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n    \"\"\"Start times of the prompts scored in the `days` before `end`: the validator's own, from the\n    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span (shifted by `offset_minutes`).\"\"\"\n    first = end - timedelta(days=days)\n    if cadence_minutes is not None:\n        horizon = timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n        shift = timedelta(minutes=offset_minutes)\n        grid = pd.date_range(\n            first - horizon + shift, end - horizon + shift, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"\n        )\n        return [t for t in grid if t + horizon <= end]\n    scores = get_miner_scores(first, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n    if scores.empty:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"the offline bundle has no scored {asset} prompt for --time-length {time_length} in \"\n            f\"{first.date()} → {end.date()} (DATA.md gives its span); --crps-only scores CRPS alone \"\n            f\"on any window of the snapshot.\"\n        )\n    return sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n\n\ndef generate(\n    modeling,\n    asset: str,\n    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n    out_dir: Path,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"One JSON per prompt (the layout backtest() has always read). Single-asset mode only.\"\"\"\n    context_days = context_days_of(modeling)\n    # The same loader the scored evaluation uses. NOT MinutePriceStore.load_range, which raises\n    # on a single NaN close. NaN reaches simulate() untouched, which is the contract — never\n    # interpolate it away.\n    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days), times[-1])\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    head = 0\n    for t in times:\n        # Never `prices.loc[:t]` — see the module docstring. Same cut the scored evaluation uses.\n        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, context_days)\n        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n        out = modeling.simulate(\n            asset=asset,\n            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n            context_prices=context,\n        )\n        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n        record = {\n            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n            \"asset\": asset,\n            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n            \"time_length\": time_length,\n            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n            \"paths\": paths,\n        }\n        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n        (out_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(record))\n    if head:\n        print(\n            f\"warning: {asset} contexts start with up to {head / 1440:.1f} days of NaN, before its first price \"\n            f\"in the snapshot\"\n        )\n    return len(times)\n\n\ndef print_event_split(prompts: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Your gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type\n    and over the prompts that hold none.\"\"\"\n    path = Path(os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV])\n    if not path.exists():\n        return\n    view = pd.read_parquet(path)\n    view = view[concerns(view, asset)]\n    scored = prompts[prompts[\"crps\"] > 0]  # -1 marks a prompt the backtester could not score\n    best = scored.groupby([\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])[\"crps\"].min().rename(\"best\")\n    ours = scored[scored[\"miner_id\"] == CANDIDATE_ID].join(best, on=[\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])\n    if ours.empty:\n        return\n    gap = ours[\"crps\"].to_numpy() / ours[\"best\"].to_numpy() - 1\n    starts = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"start_time\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy()\n    ends = starts + np.timedelta64(time_length, \"s\")\n    spans_any = np.zeros(len(ours), dtype=bool)\n    lines = []\n    for event, rows in view.groupby(\"event\"):\n        times = np.sort(pd.to_datetime(rows[\"time_utc\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy())\n        at = np.searchsorted(times, starts)\n        spans = (at < len(times)) & (times[np.minimum(at, len(times) - 1)] < ends)\n        spans_any |= spans\n        if spans.any():\n            lines.append(f\"  {event:<17} {spans.sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[spans].mean():+.2%}\")\n    if not spans_any.all():\n        lines.insert(0, f\"  {'no event':<17} {(~spans_any).sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[~spans_any].mean():+.2%}\")\n    print(\"event split (mean gap to each prompt's best miner):\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Parallel mode\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef assets_for(spec: str, time_length: int) -> list[str]:\n    from synth.validator.competition_config import ALL_COMPETITIONS, COM_EQU_24H, CRYPTO_24H\n\n    if spec == \"all\":\n        out: list[str] = []\n        for comp in ALL_COMPETITIONS:\n            if comp.time_length == time_length:\n                out += [a for a in comp.asset_list if a not in out]\n        return out\n    if spec == \"crypto\":\n        return list(CRYPTO_24H.asset_list)\n    if spec == \"comequ\":\n        if time_length != 86_400:\n            raise SystemExit(\"comequ assets have no 1h competition\")\n        return list(COM_EQU_24H.asset_list)\n    return [a.strip() for a in spec.split(\",\") if a.strip()]\n\n\ndef _chunks(times: list[pd.Timestamp], time_length: int) -> list[list[pd.Timestamp]]:\n    \"\"\"Split one asset's prompts into spans of whole days: one task each.\"\"\"\n    span = TASK_DAYS[time_length]\n    by_key: dict[int, list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n    day0 = times[0].normalize()\n    for t in times:\n        by_key.setdefault(int((t.normalize() - day0).days) // span, []).append(t)\n    return [by_key[k] for k in sorted(by_key)]\n\n\ndef _run_task(task: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Generate one (asset, span) with the verdict's generator and score it with score_crps().\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n    for key, value in task[\"env\"].items():\n        os.environ[key] = value\n    module = load_module(Path(task[\"modeling\"]))\n    context_days = context_days_of(module)\n    times = task[\"times\"]\n    asset, time_length, time_increment = task[\"asset\"], task[\"time_length\"], task[\"time_increment\"]\n    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f\"task-{asset}-{time_length}-\", dir=task[\"root\"]))\n    try:\n        prices = load_minute_prices(\n            WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days), times[-1]\n        )\n        generate_days(\n            module.simulate,\n            asset,\n            times[0],\n            times[-1] + pd.Timedelta(seconds=1),\n            prices,\n            out_dir,\n            cadence_minutes=1,\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=task[\"num_simulations\"],\n            prompt_times=times,\n            context_days=context_days,\n        )\n        result = score_crps(\n            miner_name=\"campaign\",\n            asset=asset,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            latest_formula=task[\"latest_formula\"],\n        )\n        frame = result.prompt_df[[\"asset\", \"start_time\", \"scored_time\", \"crps\", \"time_length\"]].copy()\n        if task.get(\"keep_dir\"):\n            keep = Path(task[\"keep_dir\"])\n            keep.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            for src in out_dir.rglob(\"date=*\"):\n                dst = keep / src.relative_to(out_dir)\n                dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n                shutil.copy(src, dst)\n        return frame\n    finally:\n        shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n\n\ndef field_join(ours: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int, time_increment: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Per prompt: the field's best, 5th-percentile and median CRPS on the same prompt (bundle).\"\"\"\n    start = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"scored_time\"], utc=True).min().to_pydatetime()\n    end = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"scored_time\"], utc=True).max().to_pydatetime() + timedelta(seconds=1)\n    field = get_miner_scores(start, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n    field = field[field[\"crps\"] > 0]\n    stats = field.groupby(\"start_time\")[\"crps\"].agg(\n        field_min=\"min\", field_p05=lambda s: s.quantile(0.05), field_med=\"median\", field_n=\"size\"\n    )\n    return ours.join(stats, on=\"start_time\"), field\n\n\ndef miner_mean_rank(ours: pd.DataFrame, field: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[int, int, float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Where our mean CRPS sits among the miners' mean CRPS on the same prompts.\n\n    Only miners that answered at least 98% of those prompts are ranked, each on its own answered\n    prompts against ours on the same ones. Returns (rank, miners, best miner mean, median miner mean)\n    with the two means taken on the common prompt set of all ranked miners.\"\"\"\n    mine = ours.set_index(\"start_time\")[\"crps\"]\n    piv = field[field[\"start_time\"].isin(mine.index)].pivot_table(index=\"start_time\", columns=\"miner_uid\", values=\"crps\")\n    full = piv.loc[:, piv.notna().mean() >= 0.98]\n    if full.empty:\n        return 0, 0, float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\")\n    means = full.mean()\n    mine_on = pd.Series({uid: mine.reindex(full.index)[full[uid].notna()].mean() for uid in full.columns})\n    rank = int((means < mine_on).sum()) + 1\n    return rank, full.shape[1], float(means.min()), float(means.median())\n\n\ndef run_parallel(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\n    from synth.validator.moving_average import ASSET_COEFFICIENTS\n\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    modeling_path = Path(args.modeling).resolve()\n    module = load_module(modeling_path)\n    context_days = context_days_of(module)\n    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    assets = assets_for(args.assets or args.asset, args.time_length)\n    cadence = args.cadence_minutes\n    if args.crps_only:\n        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]\n    else:\n        require_offline_bundle()\n    # With the field joined, score each prompt with the formula the field was scored with, unless\n    # --latest-formula; a bare CRPS always uses the latest (score_crps' default).\n    latest = True if args.crps_only else bool(args.latest_formula)\n\n    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"par-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))\n    env = {k: os.environ[k] for k in (CALENDAR_ENV, OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV, \"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\") if k in os.environ}\n    tasks = []\n    for asset in assets:\n        times = prompt_times(\n            asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence, args.offset_minutes\n        )\n        if args.stride > 1:\n            times = times[:: args.stride]\n        check_snapshot_coverage(asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=context_days), end, times[0])\n        for chunk in _chunks(times, args.time_length):\n            tasks.append(\n                {\n                    \"modeling\": str(modeling_path),\n                    \"asset\": asset,\n                    \"times\": chunk,\n                    \"time_length\": args.time_length,\n                    \"time_increment\": args.time_increment,\n                    \"num_simulations\": args.num_simulations,\n                    \"latest_formula\": latest,\n                    \"root\": str(root),\n                    \"env\": env,\n                    \"keep_dir\": args.keep_dir,\n                }\n            )\n    began = time.monotonic()\n    frames = []\n    try:\n        if args.jobs <= 1:\n            frames = [_run_task(t) for t in tasks]\n        else:\n            with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.jobs) as pool:\n                futures = [pool.submit(_run_task, t) for t in tasks]\n                for future in as_completed(futures):\n                    frames.append(future.result())\n    finally:\n        shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)\n    ours = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True).sort_values([\"asset\", \"start_time\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n    failed = int((ours[\"crps\"] == -1).sum())\n    ours = ours[ours[\"crps\"] != -1]\n    n = len(ours)\n    print(\n        f\"[{modeling_path.name}] CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}, {n} prompts scored ({failed} failed) in \"\n        f\"{time.monotonic() - began:.0f}s, {args.num_simulations} paths, window {args.days}d → {args.eval_end}, \"\n        f\"{'grid ' + str(cadence) + 'min+' + str(args.offset_minutes) if cadence else 'validator prompts'}\"\n        f\"{' stride ' + str(args.stride) if args.stride > 1 else ''}\"\n    )\n    rows = []\n    joined = []\n    for asset in assets:\n        mine = ours[ours[\"asset\"] == asset]\n        if mine.empty:\n            continue\n        row = {\"asset\": asset, \"n\": len(mine), \"crps\": mine[\"crps\"].mean()}\n        if not args.crps_only:\n            mine, field = field_join(mine, asset, args.time_length, args.time_increment)\n            rank, miners, best, med = miner_mean_rank(mine, field)\n            row.update(\n                {\n                    \"field_best_miner\": best,\n                    \"field_med_miner\": med,\n                    \"vs_best%\": 100 * (row[\"crps\"] / best - 1),\n                    \"vs_med%\": 100 * (row[\"crps\"] / med - 1),\n                    \"rank\": f\"{rank}/{miners}\",\n                    \"prompt_min\": mine[\"field_min\"].mean(),\n                }\n            )\n        joined.append(mine)\n        rows.append(row)\n    table = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    with pd.option_context(\"display.width\", 250, \"display.float_format\", lambda v: f\"{v:.2f}\"):\n        print(table.to_string(index=False))\n    # Coefficient-weighted aggregate per competition: what the validator's per-miner average weights.\n    for comp_assets, label in _competitions(assets, args.time_length):\n        sub = table[table[\"asset\"].isin(comp_assets)]\n        if sub.empty:\n            continue\n        w = sub[\"asset\"].map(ASSET_COEFFICIENTS) * sub[\"n\"]\n        agg = float((sub[\"crps\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())\n        line = f\"AGG {label}: weighted mean CRPS {agg:.3f}\"\n        if not args.crps_only:\n            best = float((sub[\"field_best_miner\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())\n            med = float((sub[\"field_med_miner\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())\n            line += f\" | field best-per-asset {best:.3f} ({100 * (agg / best - 1):+.2f}%) median {med:.3f} ({100 * (agg / med - 1):+.2f}%)\"\n        print(line)\n    if args.out:\n        out = pd.concat(joined, ignore_index=True)\n        Path(args.out).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        out.to_parquet(args.out, index=False)\n        print(f\"per-prompt rows -> {args.out}\")\n\n\ndef _competitions(assets: list[str], time_length: int) -> list[tuple[list[str], str]]:\n    out = []\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    for asset in assets:\n        comp = competition_for(asset, time_length)\n        slug = slug_for(comp)\n        if slug not in seen:\n            seen.add(slug)\n            out.append((list(comp.asset_list), slug))\n    return out\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, at most the snapshot's last day\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=None, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--num-simulations\",\n        type=int,\n        default=1000,\n        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--cadence-minutes\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"answer an even grid every N minutes instead of the validator's own start times (with \"\n        \"--crps-only, 60 for 24h prompts and 10 for 1h by default). A cadence that divides an hour \"\n        \"puts every prompt on the round hour\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--latest-formula\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"score every crypto-1h prompt with the volatility term, as prompts are scored now, \"\n        \"including those scored before it went live. Field ranks before that day then compare \"\n        \"two formulas; CRPS does not\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--crps-only\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid: no field and no rank, \"\n        \"on any window of the snapshot. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-predictions\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep this run's prediction files\")\n    # --- parallel mode ---\n    ap.add_argument(\"--assets\", default=None, help=\"comma list, or all | crypto | comequ: parallel mode\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--jobs\", type=int, default=0, help=\"worker processes (parallel mode)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--modeling\", default=str(DEFAULT_MODELING), help=\"model file to evaluate\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", default=None, help=\"write the per-prompt rows to this parquet (parallel mode)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--stride\", type=int, default=1, help=\"keep every K-th prompt (parallel mode)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--offset-minutes\", type=int, default=0, help=\"shift an even grid off the round hour\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-dir\", default=None, help=\"copy the generated day files here (parallel mode)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    if args.time_increment is None:\n        args.time_increment = 60 if args.time_length == 3_600 else 300\n\n    parallel = bool(args.assets or args.jobs or args.out or args.stride > 1 or args.offset_minutes or args.keep_dir)\n    if parallel:\n        args.jobs = args.jobs or 1\n        run_parallel(args)\n        return\n\n    modeling = load_module(Path(args.modeling))\n    context_days = context_days_of(modeling)\n    if not args.crps_only:\n        require_offline_bundle()\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    cadence = args.cadence_minutes\n    if args.crps_only:\n        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]\n    times = prompt_times(args.asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence_minutes=cadence)\n    # the context reaches back CONTEXT_DAYS before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=context_days), end, times[0])\n    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"run-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))\n    try:\n        n = generate(\n            modeling,\n            args.asset,\n            times,\n            out_dir,\n            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n            time_length=args.time_length,\n            num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n        )\n        print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n        if args.crps_only:\n            result = score_crps(\n                miner_name=\"campaign\",\n                asset=args.asset,\n                time_length=args.time_length,\n                time_increment=args.time_increment,\n                predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            )\n            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}):\", result.summary)\n            return\n        result = backtest(\n            miner_name=\"campaign\",\n            asset=args.asset,\n            time_length=args.time_length,\n            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n            n_backtest_days=args.days,\n            predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            eval_end=end,\n            latest_formula=args.latest_formula,\n            match_tolerance_minutes=args.cadence_minutes or PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES,\n        )\n        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}):\", result.summary)\n        if os.environ.get(CALENDAR_ENV):\n            print_event_split(result.prompt_df, args.asset, args.time_length)\n    finally:\n        if args.keep_predictions:\n            print(f\"predictions kept in {out_dir}\")\n        else:\n            shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2730,"cache_read_input_tokens":201041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2730,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"0596b5c3-ae02-44b5-bec2-de60da548ca0","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:21:52.354Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AhvBMn3Q71fQ6mFyNhPYiF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/agent/predict.py has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"98ca5cd5-441e-4978-adf8-d40ed57d919e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:21:52.399Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/workspace/agent/predict.py","content":"\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n\nUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\nAnswers, with agent/modeling.py, the prompts the validator scored in the --days before --eval-end,\nat the start times it actually used (read from the offline field bundle), then scores them with\nbacktest() (validator CRPS + rank vs the real field, from the same bundle). A prompt is scored one\nhorizon after it starts, so generation begins one horizon before the scored days.\n--cadence-minutes N answers an even grid over the same span instead; each scored prompt is then\nanswered by the grid point at or before it.\n\n--crps-only scores CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid (--cadence-minutes,\nby default every 60 minutes for 24h prompts and every 10 for 1h, on the round hour): no field, no\nrank, and any window of the snapshot, including before the bundle's span. Compare models on the same\ngrid with it; it is not an absolute calibration level. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula.\n\nWorks on every asset. A minute without a trade is a flat candle with trade_count 0. Prices load\nthrough the same lenient path the scored evaluation uses, so a NaN close (no price at all) reaches\nsimulate() rather than stopping the run — your model must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate).\nThe context spans the CONTEXT_DAYS your modeling.py sets (7 without it), and the days before an\nasset's first trade, or before the snapshot's first day, are NaN.\n\nWhen the snapshot carries an event calendar ($SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR), the summary is followed by\nyour gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type and\nover those that hold none: where an event costs you, that gap is wider.\n\n--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\ngeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\nfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n\nThe context a prompt gets ends BEFORE its start_time, and that is not an off-by-one. The store\nlabels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t closes at t+60s — and that close is\nthe first point the prompt is scored against. A prompt is also issued before the start_time it is\nscored from (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS). Ending the context at t would hand the model the answer to\nits own first step, and a model tuned that way is optimising a problem it will not be scored on.\n\n=== Campaign additions (the fast, parallel research loop) ===\n\n--assets A,B,C | all | crypto | comequ, --jobs N, --modeling PATH, --out FILE.parquet, --stride K,\n--offset-minutes M and --sweep switch to the PARALLEL mode. It is the same pipeline as above, split\ninto (asset, span-of-days) tasks that run in a process pool:\n\n  * generation goes through synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions.generate() — the function the\n    verdict runs — with the same context cut (context_slice) and the same float32 day layout;\n  * every CRPS comes from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration.score_crps(), i.e. the validator's\n    own calculate_crps_for_miner / calculate_total_score_for_miner. Nothing here reimplements the\n    metric.\n\nIn the parallel mode the default prompt set is still the validator's own scored start times; the\nfield is then JOINED from the bundle per prompt (best / median miner CRPS on the same prompt, and\nwhere our mean CRPS would sit among the miners' means). That join is a diagnostic, not the\nvalidator's moving-average rank: use the plain single-asset mode for that. With --crps-only the\nprompts are an even grid and nothing is joined.\n\nThe parallel mode prints one line per asset and a coefficient-weighted aggregate per competition\n(weights = synth.validator.moving_average.ASSET_COEFFICIENTS, the weights the validator's own\naggregation gives each asset's prompt scores).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor, as_completed\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES, competition_for, slug_for\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest, score_crps\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (\n    context_days_of,\n    context_slice,\n    load_minute_prices,\n    load_module,\n    nan_head_minutes,\n)\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import generate as generate_days\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns\n\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n\nDEFAULT_MODELING = AGENT_DIR / \"modeling.py\"\n# Each run writes its predictions to its own directory under this one.\nPREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\"\n# Must match synth_lib.backtester.config._OFFLINE_ENV_VAR.\nOFFLINE_ROOT_ENV = \"SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT\"\n# backtest()'s default miner_id: the rows of prompt_df that are yours.\nCANDIDATE_ID = 999\n# The --crps-only grid, by time_length. Must match synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict.CADENCE_MINUTES.\nCRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n# Parallel mode: how many days of prompts one task generates and scores.\nTASK_DAYS = {86_400: 4, 3_600: 2}\n\n\ndef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n\n    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n\n\ndef require_offline_bundle() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails unless backtest() reads the field from the offline bundle.\n\n    backtest() reads scores and rewards a day past --eval-end; from the live API that is data from\n    after your cutoff.\"\"\"\n    if not os.environ.get(OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV):\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"{OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV} is not set, so backtest() would read the field from the live API, past \"\n            f\"--eval-end. The harness points it at the bundle in your snapshot; restore it.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot (anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd).\"\"\"\n    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n\n\ndef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime, first_prompt: datetime) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n\n    The context's days before the asset's first partition are not missing: the context holds them\n    as NaN. The days from the first prompt on are never exempt.\n    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(asset)\n    first = min((p.name for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\")), default=\"\")\n    holes_from = min(first, f\"date={first_prompt.date().isoformat()}.parquet\")\n    missing = []\n    cursor = start.date()\n    while cursor <= end.date():\n        name = f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n        if name >= holes_from and not (root / name).exists():\n            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only): it ends at the campaign's data_cutoff, and DATA.md gives \"\n            f\"each asset's first and last day. Choose --eval-end / --days so that the window and its \"\n            f\"CONTEXT_DAYS stay on days {root} holds.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef prompt_times(\n    asset: str,\n    end: datetime,\n    days: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    time_increment: int,\n    cadence_minutes: int | None = None,\n    offset_minutes: int = 0,\n) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n    \"\"\"Start times of the prompts scored in the `days` before `end`: the validator's own, from the\n    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span (shifted by `offset_minutes`).\"\"\"\n    first = end - timedelta(days=days)\n    if cadence_minutes is not None:\n        horizon = timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n        shift = timedelta(minutes=offset_minutes)\n        grid = pd.date_range(\n            first - horizon + shift, end - horizon + shift, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"\n        )\n        return [t for t in grid if t + horizon <= end]\n    scores = get_miner_scores(first, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n    if scores.empty:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"the offline bundle has no scored {asset} prompt for --time-length {time_length} in \"\n            f\"{first.date()} → {end.date()} (DATA.md gives its span); --crps-only scores CRPS alone \"\n            f\"on any window of the snapshot.\"\n        )\n    return sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n\n\ndef generate(\n    modeling,\n    asset: str,\n    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n    out_dir: Path,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"One JSON per prompt (the layout backtest() has always read). Single-asset mode only.\"\"\"\n    context_days = context_days_of(modeling)\n    # The same loader the scored evaluation uses. NOT MinutePriceStore.load_range, which raises\n    # on a single NaN close. NaN reaches simulate() untouched, which is the contract — never\n    # interpolate it away.\n    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days), times[-1])\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    head = 0\n    for t in times:\n        # Never `prices.loc[:t]` — see the module docstring. Same cut the scored evaluation uses.\n        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, context_days)\n        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n        out = modeling.simulate(\n            asset=asset,\n            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n            context_prices=context,\n        )\n        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n        record = {\n            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n            \"asset\": asset,\n            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n            \"time_length\": time_length,\n            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n            \"paths\": paths,\n        }\n        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n        (out_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(record))\n    if head:\n        print(\n            f\"warning: {asset} contexts start with up to {head / 1440:.1f} days of NaN, before its first price \"\n            f\"in the snapshot\"\n        )\n    return len(times)\n\n\ndef print_event_split(prompts: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Your gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type\n    and over the prompts that hold none.\"\"\"\n    path = Path(os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV])\n    if not path.exists():\n        return\n    view = pd.read_parquet(path)\n    view = view[concerns(view, asset)]\n    scored = prompts[prompts[\"crps\"] > 0]  # -1 marks a prompt the backtester could not score\n    best = scored.groupby([\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])[\"crps\"].min().rename(\"best\")\n    ours = scored[scored[\"miner_id\"] == CANDIDATE_ID].join(best, on=[\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])\n    if ours.empty:\n        return\n    gap = ours[\"crps\"].to_numpy() / ours[\"best\"].to_numpy() - 1\n    starts = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"start_time\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy()\n    ends = starts + np.timedelta64(time_length, \"s\")\n    spans_any = np.zeros(len(ours), dtype=bool)\n    lines = []\n    for event, rows in view.groupby(\"event\"):\n        times = np.sort(pd.to_datetime(rows[\"time_utc\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy())\n        at = np.searchsorted(times, starts)\n        spans = (at < len(times)) & (times[np.minimum(at, len(times) - 1)] < ends)\n        spans_any |= spans\n        if spans.any():\n            lines.append(f\"  {event:<17} {spans.sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[spans].mean():+.2%}\")\n    if not spans_any.all():\n        lines.insert(0, f\"  {'no event':<17} {(~spans_any).sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[~spans_any].mean():+.2%}\")\n    print(\"event split (mean gap to each prompt's best miner):\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Parallel mode\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef assets_for(spec: str, time_length: int) -> list[str]:\n    from synth.validator.competition_config import ALL_COMPETITIONS, COM_EQU_24H, CRYPTO_24H\n\n    if spec == \"all\":\n        out: list[str] = []\n        for comp in ALL_COMPETITIONS:\n            if comp.time_length == time_length:\n                out += [a for a in comp.asset_list if a not in out]\n        return out\n    if spec == \"crypto\":\n        return list(CRYPTO_24H.asset_list)\n    if spec == \"comequ\":\n        if time_length != 86_400:\n            raise SystemExit(\"comequ assets have no 1h competition\")\n        return list(COM_EQU_24H.asset_list)\n    return [a.strip() for a in spec.split(\",\") if a.strip()]\n\n\ndef _chunks(times: list[pd.Timestamp], time_length: int) -> list[list[pd.Timestamp]]:\n    \"\"\"Split one asset's prompts into spans of whole days: one task each.\"\"\"\n    span = TASK_DAYS[time_length]\n    by_key: dict[int, list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}\n    day0 = times[0].normalize()\n    for t in times:\n        by_key.setdefault(int((t.normalize() - day0).days) // span, []).append(t)\n    return [by_key[k] for k in sorted(by_key)]\n\n\ndef _run_task(task: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Generate one (asset, span) with the verdict's generator and score it with score_crps().\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n    for key, value in task[\"env\"].items():\n        os.environ[key] = value\n    module = load_module(Path(task[\"modeling\"]))\n    context_days = context_days_of(module)\n    times = task[\"times\"]\n    asset, time_length, time_increment = task[\"asset\"], task[\"time_length\"], task[\"time_increment\"]\n    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f\"task-{asset}-{time_length}-\", dir=task[\"root\"]))\n    try:\n        prices = load_minute_prices(\n            WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days), times[-1]\n        )\n        generate_days(\n            module.simulate,\n            asset,\n            times[0],\n            times[-1] + pd.Timedelta(seconds=1),\n            prices,\n            out_dir,\n            cadence_minutes=1,\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=task[\"num_simulations\"],\n            prompt_times=times,\n            context_days=context_days,\n        )\n        result = score_crps(\n            miner_name=\"campaign\",\n            asset=asset,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            latest_formula=task[\"latest_formula\"],\n        )\n        frame = result.prompt_df[[\"asset\", \"start_time\", \"scored_time\", \"crps\", \"time_length\"]].copy()\n        if task.get(\"keep_dir\"):\n            keep = Path(task[\"keep_dir\"])\n            keep.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            for src in out_dir.rglob(\"date=*\"):\n                dst = keep / src.relative_to(out_dir)\n                dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n                shutil.copy(src, dst)\n        return frame\n    finally:\n        shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n\n\ndef field_join(ours: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int, time_increment: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Per prompt: the field's best, 5th-percentile and median CRPS on the same prompt (bundle).\"\"\"\n    start = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"scored_time\"], utc=True).min().to_pydatetime()\n    end = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"scored_time\"], utc=True).max().to_pydatetime() + timedelta(seconds=1)\n    field = get_miner_scores(start, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n    field = field[field[\"crps\"] > 0]\n    stats = field.groupby(\"start_time\")[\"crps\"].agg(\n        field_min=\"min\", field_p05=lambda s: s.quantile(0.05), field_med=\"median\", field_n=\"size\"\n    )\n    return ours.join(stats, on=\"start_time\"), field\n\n\ndef miner_mean_rank(ours: pd.DataFrame, field: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[int, int, float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Where our mean CRPS sits among the miners' mean CRPS on the same prompts.\n\n    Only miners that answered at least 98% of those prompts are ranked, each on its own answered\n    prompts against ours on the same ones. Returns (rank, miners, best miner mean, median miner mean)\n    with the two means taken on the common prompt set of all ranked miners.\"\"\"\n    mine = ours.set_index(\"start_time\")[\"crps\"]\n    piv = field[field[\"start_time\"].isin(mine.index)].pivot_table(index=\"start_time\", columns=\"miner_uid\", values=\"crps\")\n    full = piv.loc[:, piv.notna().mean() >= 0.98]\n    if full.empty:\n        return 0, 0, float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\")\n    means = full.mean()\n    mine_on = pd.Series({uid: mine.reindex(full.index)[full[uid].notna()].mean() for uid in full.columns})\n    rank = int((means < mine_on).sum()) + 1\n    return rank, full.shape[1], float(means.min()), float(means.median())\n\n\ndef run_parallel(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\n    from synth.validator.moving_average import ASSET_COEFFICIENTS\n\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    modeling_path = Path(args.modeling).resolve()\n    module = load_module(modeling_path)\n    context_days = context_days_of(module)\n    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    assets = assets_for(args.assets or args.asset, args.time_length)\n    cadence = args.cadence_minutes\n    if args.crps_only:\n        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]\n    else:\n        require_offline_bundle()\n    # With the field joined, score each prompt with the formula the field was scored with, unless\n    # --latest-formula; a bare CRPS always uses the latest (score_crps' default).\n    latest = True if args.crps_only else bool(args.latest_formula)\n\n    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"par-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))\n    env = {k: os.environ[k] for k in (CALENDAR_ENV, OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV, \"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\") if k in os.environ}\n    tasks = []\n    for asset in assets:\n        times = prompt_times(\n            asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence, args.offset_minutes\n        )\n        if args.stride > 1:\n            times = times[:: args.stride]\n        check_snapshot_coverage(asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=context_days), end, times[0])\n        for chunk in _chunks(times, args.time_length):\n            tasks.append(\n                {\n                    \"modeling\": str(modeling_path),\n                    \"asset\": asset,\n                    \"times\": chunk,\n                    \"time_length\": args.time_length,\n                    \"time_increment\": args.time_increment,\n                    \"num_simulations\": args.num_simulations,\n                    \"latest_formula\": latest,\n                    \"root\": str(root),\n                    \"env\": env,\n                    \"keep_dir\": args.keep_dir,\n                }\n            )\n    began = time.monotonic()\n    frames = []\n    try:\n        if args.jobs <= 1:\n            frames = [_run_task(t) for t in tasks]\n        else:\n            with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.jobs) as pool:\n                futures = [pool.submit(_run_task, t) for t in tasks]\n                for future in as_completed(futures):\n                    frames.append(future.result())\n    finally:\n        shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)\n    ours = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True).sort_values([\"asset\", \"start_time\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n    failed = int((ours[\"crps\"] == -1).sum())\n    ours = ours[ours[\"crps\"] != -1]\n    n = len(ours)\n    print(\n        f\"[{modeling_path.name}] CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}, {n} prompts scored ({failed} failed) in \"\n        f\"{time.monotonic() - began:.0f}s, {args.num_simulations} paths, window {args.days}d → {args.eval_end}, \"\n        f\"{'grid ' + str(cadence) + 'min+' + str(args.offset_minutes) if cadence else 'validator prompts'}\"\n        f\"{' stride ' + str(args.stride) if args.stride > 1 else ''}\"\n    )\n    rows = []\n    joined = []\n    for asset in assets:\n        mine = ours[ours[\"asset\"] == asset]\n        if mine.empty:\n            continue\n        row = {\"asset\": asset, \"n\": len(mine), \"crps\": mine[\"crps\"].mean()}\n        if not args.crps_only:\n            mine, field = field_join(mine, asset, args.time_length, args.time_increment)\n            rank, miners, best, med = miner_mean_rank(mine, field)\n            row.update(\n                {\n                    \"field_best_miner\": best,\n                    \"field_med_miner\": med,\n                    \"vs_best%\": 100 * (row[\"crps\"] / best - 1),\n                    \"vs_med%\": 100 * (row[\"crps\"] / med - 1),\n                    \"rank\": f\"{rank}/{miners}\",\n                    \"prompt_min\": mine[\"field_min\"].mean(),\n                }\n            )\n        joined.append(mine)\n        rows.append(row)\n    table = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    with pd.option_context(\"display.width\", 250, \"display.float_format\", lambda v: f\"{v:.2f}\"):\n        print(table.to_string(index=False))\n    # Coefficient-weighted aggregate per competition: what the validator's per-miner average weights.\n    for comp_assets, label in _competitions(assets, args.time_length):\n        sub = table[table[\"asset\"].isin(comp_assets)]\n        if sub.empty:\n            continue\n        w = sub[\"asset\"].map(ASSET_COEFFICIENTS) * sub[\"n\"]\n        agg = float((sub[\"crps\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())\n        line = f\"AGG {label}: weighted mean CRPS {agg:.3f}\"\n        if not args.crps_only:\n            best = float((sub[\"field_best_miner\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())\n            med = float((sub[\"field_med_miner\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())\n            line += f\" | field best-per-asset {best:.3f} ({100 * (agg / best - 1):+.2f}%) median {med:.3f} ({100 * (agg / med - 1):+.2f}%)\"\n        print(line)\n    if args.out:\n        out = pd.concat(joined, ignore_index=True)\n        Path(args.out).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        out.to_parquet(args.out, index=False)\n        print(f\"per-prompt rows -> {args.out}\")\n\n\ndef _competitions(assets: list[str], time_length: int) -> list[tuple[list[str], str]]:\n    out = []\n    seen: set[str] = set()\n    for asset in assets:\n        comp = competition_for(asset, time_length)\n        slug = slug_for(comp)\n        if slug not in seen:\n            seen.add(slug)\n            out.append((list(comp.asset_list), slug))\n    return out\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, at most the snapshot's last day\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=None, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--num-simulations\",\n        type=int,\n        default=1000,\n        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--cadence-minutes\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"answer an even grid every N minutes instead of the validator's own start times (with \"\n        \"--crps-only, 60 for 24h prompts and 10 for 1h by default). A cadence that divides an hour \"\n        \"puts every prompt on the round hour\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--latest-formula\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"score every crypto-1h prompt with the volatility term, as prompts are scored now, \"\n        \"including those scored before it went live. Field ranks before that day then compare \"\n        \"two formulas; CRPS does not\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--crps-only\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid: no field and no rank, \"\n        \"on any window of the snapshot. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-predictions\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep this run's prediction files\")\n    # --- parallel mode ---\n    ap.add_argument(\"--assets\", default=None, help=\"comma list, or all | crypto | comequ: parallel mode\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--jobs\", type=int, default=0, help=\"worker processes (parallel mode)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--modeling\", default=str(DEFAULT_MODELING), help=\"model file to evaluate\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", default=None, help=\"write the per-prompt rows to this parquet (parallel mode)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--stride\", type=int, default=1, help=\"keep every K-th prompt (parallel mode)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--offset-minutes\", type=int, default=0, help=\"shift an even grid off the round hour\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-dir\", default=None, help=\"copy the generated day files here (parallel mode)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    if args.time_increment is None:\n        args.time_increment = 60 if args.time_length == 3_600 else 300\n\n    parallel = bool(args.assets or args.jobs or args.out or args.stride > 1 or args.offset_minutes or args.keep_dir)\n    if parallel:\n        args.jobs = args.jobs or 1\n        run_parallel(args)\n        return\n\n    modeling = load_module(Path(args.modeling))\n    context_days = context_days_of(modeling)\n    if not args.crps_only:\n        require_offline_bundle()\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    cadence = args.cadence_minutes\n    if args.crps_only:\n        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]\n    times = prompt_times(args.asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence_minutes=cadence)\n    # the context reaches back CONTEXT_DAYS before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=context_days), end, times[0])\n    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"run-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))\n    try:\n        n = generate(\n            modeling,\n            args.asset,\n            times,\n            out_dir,\n            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n            time_length=args.time_length,\n            num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n        )\n        print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n        if args.crps_only:\n            result = score_crps(\n                miner_name=\"campaign\",\n                asset=args.asset,\n                time_length=args.time_length,\n                time_increment=args.time_increment,\n                predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            )\n            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}):\", result.summary)\n            return\n        result = backtest(\n            miner_name=\"campaign\",\n            asset=args.asset,\n            time_length=args.time_length,\n            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n            n_backtest_days=args.days,\n            predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            eval_end=end,\n            latest_formula=args.latest_formula,\n            match_tolerance_minutes=args.cadence_minutes or PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES,\n        )\n        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}):\", result.summary)\n        if os.environ.get(CALENDAR_ENV):\n            print_event_split(result.prompt_df, args.asset, args.time_length)\n    finally:\n        if args.keep_predictions:\n            print(f\"predictions kept in {out_dir}\")\n        else:\n            shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":6,"newStart":33,"newLines":28,"lines":[" the first point the prompt is scored against. A prompt is also issued before the start_time it is"," scored from (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS). Ending the context at t would hand the model the answer to"," its own first step, and a model tuned that way is optimising a problem it will not be scored on.","+","+=== Campaign additions (the fast, parallel research loop) ===","+","+--assets A,B,C | all | crypto | comequ, --jobs N, --modeling PATH, --out FILE.parquet, --stride K,","+--offset-minutes M and --sweep switch to the PARALLEL mode. It is the same pipeline as above, split","+into (asset, span-of-days) tasks that run in a process pool:","+","+  * generation goes through synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions.generate() — the function the","+    verdict runs — with the same context cut (context_slice) and the same float32 day layout;","+  * every CRPS comes from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration.score_crps(), i.e. the validator's","+    own calculate_crps_for_miner / calculate_total_score_for_miner. Nothing here reimplements the","+    metric.","+","+In the parallel mode the default prompt set is still the validator's own scored start times; the","+field is then JOINED from the bundle per prompt (best / median miner CRPS on the same prompt, and","+where our mean CRPS would sit among the miners' means). That join is a diagnostic, not the","+validator's moving-average rank: use the plain single-asset mode for that. With --crps-only the","+prompts are an even grid and nothing is joined.","+","+The parallel mode prints one line per asset and a coefficient-weighted aggregate per competition","+(weights = synth.validator.moving_average.ASSET_COEFFICIENTS, the weights the validator's own","+aggregation gives each asset's prompt scores)."," \"\"\""," "," from __future__ import annotations"]},{"oldStart":43,"oldLines":21,"newStart":65,"newLines":25,"lines":[" import shutil"," import sys"," import tempfile","+import time","+from concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor, as_completed"," from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone"," from pathlib import Path"," "," import numpy as np"," import pandas as pd"," ","-from synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES","+from synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES, competition_for, slug_for"," from synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores"," from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest, score_crps"," from synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (","     context_days_of,","     context_slice,","     load_minute_prices,","+    load_module,","     nan_head_minutes,"," )","+from synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import generate as generate_days"," from synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR"," from synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns"," "]},{"oldStart":68,"oldLines":10,"newStart":94,"newLines":7,"lines":[" WORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent"," sys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))"," ","-import modeling  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)","-","-# Your modeling.py's CONTEXT_DAYS, read as the verdict and the live miner read it.","-CONTEXT_DAYS = context_days_of(modeling)","+DEFAULT_MODELING = AGENT_DIR / \"modeling.py\""," # Each run writes its predictions to its own directory under this one."," PREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\""," # Must match synth_lib.backtester.config._OFFLINE_ENV_VAR."]},{"oldStart":80,"oldLines":6,"newStart":103,"newLines":8,"lines":[" CANDIDATE_ID = 999"," # The --crps-only grid, by time_length. Must match synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict.CADENCE_MINUTES."," CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}","+# Parallel mode: how many days of prompts one task generates and scores.","+TASK_DAYS = {86_400: 4, 3_600: 2}"," "," "," def ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:"]},{"oldStart":106,"oldLines":12,"newStart":131,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," "," def store_root(asset: str) -> Path:","-    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.","-","-    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,","-    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do","-    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the","-    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"","+    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot (anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd).\"\"\"","     return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\""," "," "]},{"oldStart":149,"oldLines":13,"newStart":169,"newLines":18,"lines":["     time_length: int,","     time_increment: int,","     cadence_minutes: int | None = None,","+    offset_minutes: int = 0,"," ) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:","     \"\"\"Start times of the prompts scored in the `days` before `end`: the validator's own, from the","-    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span.\"\"\"","+    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span (shifted by `offset_minutes`).\"\"\"","     first = end - timedelta(days=days)","     if cadence_minutes is not None:","         horizon = timedelta(seconds=time_length)","-        return list(pd.date_range(first - horizon, end - horizon, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"))","+        shift = timedelta(minutes=offset_minutes)","+        grid = pd.date_range(","+            first - horizon + shift, end - horizon + shift, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"","+        )","+        return [t for t in grid if t + horizon <= end]","     scores = get_miner_scores(first, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)","     if scores.empty:","         raise SystemExit("]},{"oldStart":167,"oldLines":6,"newStart":192,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," "," def generate(","+    modeling,","     asset: str,","     times: list[pd.Timestamp],","     out_dir: Path,"]},{"oldStart":174,"oldLines":15,"newStart":200,"newLines":17,"lines":["     time_length: int = 86_400,","     num_simulations: int = 1000,"," ) -> int:","+    \"\"\"One JSON per prompt (the layout backtest() has always read). Single-asset mode only.\"\"\"","+    context_days = context_days_of(modeling)","     # The same loader the scored evaluation uses. NOT MinutePriceStore.load_range, which raises","     # on a single NaN close. NaN reaches simulate() untouched, which is the contract — never","     # interpolate it away.","-    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), times[-1])","+    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days), times[-1])","     out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","     head = 0","     for t in times:","         # Never `prices.loc[:t]` — see the module docstring. Same cut the scored evaluation uses.","-        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, CONTEXT_DAYS)","+        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, context_days)","         head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))","         out = modeling.simulate(","             asset=asset,"]},{"oldStart":243,"oldLines":12,"newStart":271,"newLines":246,"lines":["     print(\"\\n\".join(lines))"," "," ","+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------","+# Parallel mode","+# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------","+","+","+def assets_for(spec: str, time_length: int) -> list[str]:","+    from synth.validator.competition_config import ALL_COMPETITIONS, COM_EQU_24H, CRYPTO_24H","+","+    if spec == \"all\":","+        out: list[str] = []","+        for comp in ALL_COMPETITIONS:","+            if comp.time_length == time_length:","+                out += [a for a in comp.asset_list if a not in out]","+        return out","+    if spec == \"crypto\":","+        return list(CRYPTO_24H.asset_list)","+    if spec == \"comequ\":","+        if time_length != 86_400:","+            raise SystemExit(\"comequ assets have no 1h competition\")","+        return list(COM_EQU_24H.asset_list)","+    return [a.strip() for a in spec.split(\",\") if a.strip()]","+","+","+def _chunks(times: list[pd.Timestamp], time_length: int) -> list[list[pd.Timestamp]]:","+    \"\"\"Split one asset's prompts into spans of whole days: one task each.\"\"\"","+    span = TASK_DAYS[time_length]","+    by_key: dict[int, list[pd.Timestamp]] = {}","+    day0 = times[0].normalize()","+    for t in times:","+        by_key.setdefault(int((t.normalize() - day0).days) // span, []).append(t)","+    return [by_key[k] for k in sorted(by_key)]","+","+","+def _run_task(task: dict) -> pd.DataFrame:","+    \"\"\"Generate one (asset, span) with the verdict's generator and score it with score_crps().\"\"\"","+    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)","+    for key, value in task[\"env\"].items():","+        os.environ[key] = value","+    module = load_module(Path(task[\"modeling\"]))","+    context_days = context_days_of(module)","+    times = task[\"times\"]","+    asset, time_length, time_increment = task[\"asset\"], task[\"time_length\"], task[\"time_increment\"]","+    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=f\"task-{asset}-{time_length}-\", dir=task[\"root\"]))","+    try:","+        prices = load_minute_prices(","+            WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days), times[-1]","+        )","+        generate_days(","+            module.simulate,","+            asset,","+            times[0],","+            times[-1] + pd.Timedelta(seconds=1),","+            prices,","+            out_dir,","+            cadence_minutes=1,","+            time_increment=time_increment,","+            time_length=time_length,","+            num_simulations=task[\"num_simulations\"],","+            prompt_times=times,","+            context_days=context_days,","+        )","+        result = score_crps(","+            miner_name=\"campaign\",","+            asset=asset,","+            time_length=time_length,","+            time_increment=time_increment,","+            predictions_dir=out_dir,","+            latest_formula=task[\"latest_formula\"],","+        )","+        frame = result.prompt_df[[\"asset\", \"start_time\", \"scored_time\", \"crps\", \"time_length\"]].copy()","+        if task.get(\"keep_dir\"):","+            keep = Path(task[\"keep_dir\"])","+            keep.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","+            for src in out_dir.rglob(\"date=*\"):","+                dst = keep / src.relative_to(out_dir)","+                dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","+                shutil.copy(src, dst)","+        return frame","+    finally:","+        shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)","+","+","+def field_join(ours: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int, time_increment: int) -> pd.DataFrame:","+    \"\"\"Per prompt: the field's best, 5th-percentile and median CRPS on the same prompt (bundle).\"\"\"","+    start = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"scored_time\"], utc=True).min().to_pydatetime()","+    end = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"scored_time\"], utc=True).max().to_pydatetime() + timedelta(seconds=1)","+    field = get_miner_scores(start, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)","+    field = field[field[\"crps\"] > 0]","+    stats = field.groupby(\"start_time\")[\"crps\"].agg(","+        field_min=\"min\", field_p05=lambda s: s.quantile(0.05), field_med=\"median\", field_n=\"size\"","+    )","+    return ours.join(stats, on=\"start_time\"), field","+","+","+def miner_mean_rank(ours: pd.DataFrame, field: pd.DataFrame) -> tuple[int, int, float, float]:","+    \"\"\"Where our mean CRPS sits among the miners' mean CRPS on the same prompts.","+","+    Only miners that answered at least 98% of those prompts are ranked, each on its own answered","+    prompts against ours on the same ones. Returns (rank, miners, best miner mean, median miner mean)","+    with the two means taken on the common prompt set of all ranked miners.\"\"\"","+    mine = ours.set_index(\"start_time\")[\"crps\"]","+    piv = field[field[\"start_time\"].isin(mine.index)].pivot_table(index=\"start_time\", columns=\"miner_uid\", values=\"crps\")","+    full = piv.loc[:, piv.notna().mean() >= 0.98]","+    if full.empty:","+        return 0, 0, float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\")","+    means = full.mean()","+    mine_on = pd.Series({uid: mine.reindex(full.index)[full[uid].notna()].mean() for uid in full.columns})","+    rank = int((means < mine_on).sum()) + 1","+    return rank, full.shape[1], float(means.min()), float(means.median())","+","+","+def run_parallel(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:","+    from synth.validator.moving_average import ASSET_COEFFICIENTS","+","+    ensure_workspace_cwd()","+    modeling_path = Path(args.modeling).resolve()","+    module = load_module(modeling_path)","+    context_days = context_days_of(module)","+    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)","+    assets = assets_for(args.assets or args.asset, args.time_length)","+    cadence = args.cadence_minutes","+    if args.crps_only:","+        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]","+    else:","+        require_offline_bundle()","+    # With the field joined, score each prompt with the formula the field was scored with, unless","+    # --latest-formula; a bare CRPS always uses the latest (score_crps' default).","+    latest = True if args.crps_only else bool(args.latest_formula)","+","+    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","+    root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"par-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))","+    env = {k: os.environ[k] for k in (CALENDAR_ENV, OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV, \"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\") if k in os.environ}","+    tasks = []","+    for asset in assets:","+        times = prompt_times(","+            asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence, args.offset_minutes","+        )","+        if args.stride > 1:","+            times = times[:: args.stride]","+        check_snapshot_coverage(asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=context_days), end, times[0])","+        for chunk in _chunks(times, args.time_length):","+            tasks.append(","+                {","+                    \"modeling\": str(modeling_path),","+                    \"asset\": asset,","+                    \"times\": chunk,","+                    \"time_length\": args.time_length,","+                    \"time_increment\": args.time_increment,","+                    \"num_simulations\": args.num_simulations,","+                    \"latest_formula\": latest,","+                    \"root\": str(root),","+                    \"env\": env,","+                    \"keep_dir\": args.keep_dir,","+                }","+            )","+    began = time.monotonic()","+    frames = []","+    try:","+        if args.jobs <= 1:","+            frames = [_run_task(t) for t in tasks]","+        else:","+            with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.jobs) as pool:","+                futures = [pool.submit(_run_task, t) for t in tasks]","+                for future in as_completed(futures):","+                    frames.append(future.result())","+    finally:","+        shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)","+    ours = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True).sort_values([\"asset\", \"start_time\"]).reset_index(drop=True)","+    failed = int((ours[\"crps\"] == -1).sum())","+    ours = ours[ours[\"crps\"] != -1]","+    n = len(ours)","+    print(","+        f\"[{modeling_path.name}] CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}, {n} prompts scored ({failed} failed) in \"","+        f\"{time.monotonic() - began:.0f}s, {args.num_simulations} paths, window {args.days}d → {args.eval_end}, \"","+        f\"{'grid ' + str(cadence) + 'min+' + str(args.offset_minutes) if cadence else 'validator prompts'}\"","+        f\"{' stride ' + str(args.stride) if args.stride > 1 else ''}\"","+    )","+    rows = []","+    joined = []","+    for asset in assets:","+        mine = ours[ours[\"asset\"] == asset]","+        if mine.empty:","+            continue","+        row = {\"asset\": asset, \"n\": len(mine), \"crps\": mine[\"crps\"].mean()}","+        if not args.crps_only:","+            mine, field = field_join(mine, asset, args.time_length, args.time_increment)","+            rank, miners, best, med = miner_mean_rank(mine, field)","+            row.update(","+                {","+                    \"field_best_miner\": best,","+                    \"field_med_miner\": med,","+                    \"vs_best%\": 100 * (row[\"crps\"] / best - 1),","+                    \"vs_med%\": 100 * (row[\"crps\"] / med - 1),","+                    \"rank\": f\"{rank}/{miners}\",","+                    \"prompt_min\": mine[\"field_min\"].mean(),","+                }","+            )","+        joined.append(mine)","+        rows.append(row)","+    table = pd.DataFrame(rows)","+    with pd.option_context(\"display.width\", 250, \"display.float_format\", lambda v: f\"{v:.2f}\"):","+        print(table.to_string(index=False))","+    # Coefficient-weighted aggregate per competition: what the validator's per-miner average weights.","+    for comp_assets, label in _competitions(assets, args.time_length):","+        sub = table[table[\"asset\"].isin(comp_assets)]","+        if sub.empty:","+            continue","+        w = sub[\"asset\"].map(ASSET_COEFFICIENTS) * sub[\"n\"]","+        agg = float((sub[\"crps\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())","+        line = f\"AGG {label}: weighted mean CRPS {agg:.3f}\"","+        if not args.crps_only:","+            best = float((sub[\"field_best_miner\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())","+            med = float((sub[\"field_med_miner\"] * w).sum() / w.sum())","+            line += f\" | field best-per-asset {best:.3f} ({100 * (agg / best - 1):+.2f}%) median {med:.3f} ({100 * (agg / med - 1):+.2f}%)\"","+        print(line)","+    if args.out:","+        out = pd.concat(joined, ignore_index=True)","+        Path(args.out).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","+        out.to_parquet(args.out, index=False)","+        print(f\"per-prompt rows -> {args.out}\")","+","+","+def _competitions(assets: list[str], time_length: int) -> list[tuple[list[str], str]]:","+    out = []","+    seen: set[str] = set()","+    for asset in assets:","+        comp = competition_for(asset, time_length)","+        slug = slug_for(comp)","+        if slug not in seen:","+            seen.add(slug)","+            out.append((list(comp.asset_list), slug))","+    return out","+","+"," def main() -> None:","     ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()","     ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")","     ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)","     ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, at most the snapshot's last day\")","-    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=None, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")","     ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")","     ap.add_argument(","         \"--num-simulations\","]},{"oldStart":280,"oldLines":7,"newStart":542,"newLines":26,"lines":["         \"on any window of the snapshot. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula\",","     )","     ap.add_argument(\"--keep-predictions\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep this run's prediction files\")","+    # --- parallel mode ---","+    ap.add_argument(\"--assets\", default=None, help=\"comma list, or all | crypto | comequ: parallel mode\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--jobs\", type=int, default=0, help=\"worker processes (parallel mode)\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--modeling\", default=str(DEFAULT_MODELING), help=\"model file to evaluate\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", default=None, help=\"write the per-prompt rows to this parquet (parallel mode)\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--stride\", type=int, default=1, help=\"keep every K-th prompt (parallel mode)\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--offset-minutes\", type=int, default=0, help=\"shift an even grid off the round hour\")","+    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-dir\", default=None, help=\"copy the generated day files here (parallel mode)\")","     args = ap.parse_args()","+    if args.time_increment is None:","+        args.time_increment = 60 if args.time_length == 3_600 else 300","+","+    parallel = bool(args.assets or args.jobs or args.out or args.stride > 1 or args.offset_minutes or args.keep_dir)","+    if parallel:","+        args.jobs = args.jobs or 1","+        run_parallel(args)","+        return","+","+    modeling = load_module(Path(args.modeling))","+    context_days = context_days_of(modeling)","     if not args.crps_only:","         require_offline_bundle()","     ensure_workspace_cwd()"]},{"oldStart":290,"oldLines":11,"newStart":571,"newLines":12,"lines":["         cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]","     times = prompt_times(args.asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence_minutes=cadence)","     # the context reaches back CONTEXT_DAYS before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far","-    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), end, times[0])","+    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=context_days), end, times[0])","     PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)","     out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"run-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))","     try:","         n = generate(","+            modeling,","             args.asset,","             times,","             out_dir,"]},{"oldStart":311,"oldLines":7,"newStart":593,"newLines":7,"lines":["                 time_increment=args.time_increment,","                 predictions_dir=out_dir,","             )","-            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)","+            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}):\", result.summary)","             return","         result = backtest(","             miner_name=\"campaign\","]},{"oldStart":324,"oldLines":7,"newStart":606,"newLines":7,"lines":["             latest_formula=args.latest_formula,","             match_tolerance_minutes=args.cadence_minutes or PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES,","         )","-        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)","+        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {context_days}):\", result.summary)","         if os.environ.get(CALENDAR_ENV):","             print_event_split(result.prompt_df, args.asset, args.time_length)","     finally:"]}],"originalFile":"\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n\nUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\nAnswers, with agent/modeling.py, the prompts the validator scored in the --days before --eval-end,\nat the start times it actually used (read from the offline field bundle), then scores them with\nbacktest() (validator CRPS + rank vs the real field, from the same bundle). A prompt is scored one\nhorizon after it starts, so generation begins one horizon before the scored days.\n--cadence-minutes N answers an even grid over the same span instead; each scored prompt is then\nanswered by the grid point at or before it.\n\n--crps-only scores CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid (--cadence-minutes,\nby default every 60 minutes for 24h prompts and every 10 for 1h, on the round hour): no field, no\nrank, and any window of the snapshot, including before the bundle's span. Compare models on the same\ngrid with it; it is not an absolute calibration level. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula.\n\nWorks on every asset. A minute without a trade is a flat candle with trade_count 0. Prices load\nthrough the same lenient path the scored evaluation uses, so a NaN close (no price at all) reaches\nsimulate() rather than stopping the run — your model must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate).\nThe context spans the CONTEXT_DAYS your modeling.py sets (7 without it), and the days before an\nasset's first trade, or before the snapshot's first day, are NaN.\n\nWhen the snapshot carries an event calendar ($SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR), the summary is followed by\nyour gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type and\nover those that hold none: where an event costs you, that gap is wider.\n\n--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\ngeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\nfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n\nThe context a prompt gets ends BEFORE its start_time, and that is not an off-by-one. The store\nlabels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t closes at t+60s — and that close is\nthe first point the prompt is scored against. A prompt is also issued before the start_time it is\nscored from (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS). Ending the context at t would hand the model the answer to\nits own first step, and a model tuned that way is optimising a problem it will not be scored on.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest, score_crps\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (\n    context_days_of,\n    context_slice,\n    load_minute_prices,\n    nan_head_minutes,\n)\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns\n\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n\nimport modeling  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\n\n# Your modeling.py's CONTEXT_DAYS, read as the verdict and the live miner read it.\nCONTEXT_DAYS = context_days_of(modeling)\n# Each run writes its predictions to its own directory under this one.\nPREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\"\n# Must match synth_lib.backtester.config._OFFLINE_ENV_VAR.\nOFFLINE_ROOT_ENV = \"SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT\"\n# backtest()'s default miner_id: the rows of prompt_df that are yours.\nCANDIDATE_ID = 999\n# The --crps-only grid, by time_length. Must match synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict.CADENCE_MINUTES.\nCRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n\n\ndef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n\n    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n\n\ndef require_offline_bundle() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails unless backtest() reads the field from the offline bundle.\n\n    backtest() reads scores and rewards a day past --eval-end; from the live API that is data from\n    after your cutoff.\"\"\"\n    if not os.environ.get(OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV):\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"{OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV} is not set, so backtest() would read the field from the live API, past \"\n            f\"--eval-end. The harness points it at the bundle in your snapshot; restore it.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.\n\n    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,\n    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do\n    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the\n    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"\n    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n\n\ndef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime, first_prompt: datetime) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n\n    The context's days before the asset's first partition are not missing: the context holds them\n    as NaN. The days from the first prompt on are never exempt.\n    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(asset)\n    first = min((p.name for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\")), default=\"\")\n    holes_from = min(first, f\"date={first_prompt.date().isoformat()}.parquet\")\n    missing = []\n    cursor = start.date()\n    while cursor <= end.date():\n        name = f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n        if name >= holes_from and not (root / name).exists():\n            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only): it ends at the campaign's data_cutoff, and DATA.md gives \"\n            f\"each asset's first and last day. Choose --eval-end / --days so that the window and its \"\n            f\"CONTEXT_DAYS stay on days {root} holds.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef prompt_times(\n    asset: str,\n    end: datetime,\n    days: int,\n    time_length: int,\n    time_increment: int,\n    cadence_minutes: int | None = None,\n) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n    \"\"\"Start times of the prompts scored in the `days` before `end`: the validator's own, from the\n    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span.\"\"\"\n    first = end - timedelta(days=days)\n    if cadence_minutes is not None:\n        horizon = timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n        return list(pd.date_range(first - horizon, end - horizon, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"))\n    scores = get_miner_scores(first, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n    if scores.empty:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"the offline bundle has no scored {asset} prompt for --time-length {time_length} in \"\n            f\"{first.date()} → {end.date()} (DATA.md gives its span); --crps-only scores CRPS alone \"\n            f\"on any window of the snapshot.\"\n        )\n    return sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n\n\ndef generate(\n    asset: str,\n    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n    out_dir: Path,\n    time_increment: int = 300,\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n) -> int:\n    # The same loader the scored evaluation uses. NOT MinutePriceStore.load_range, which raises\n    # on a single NaN close. NaN reaches simulate() untouched, which is the contract — never\n    # interpolate it away.\n    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), times[-1])\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    head = 0\n    for t in times:\n        # Never `prices.loc[:t]` — see the module docstring. Same cut the scored evaluation uses.\n        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, CONTEXT_DAYS)\n        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n        out = modeling.simulate(\n            asset=asset,\n            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n            time_increment=time_increment,\n            time_length=time_length,\n            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n            context_prices=context,\n        )\n        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n        record = {\n            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n            \"asset\": asset,\n            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n            \"time_length\": time_length,\n            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n            \"paths\": paths,\n        }\n        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n        (out_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(record))\n    if head:\n        print(\n            f\"warning: {asset} contexts start with up to {head / 1440:.1f} days of NaN, before its first price \"\n            f\"in the snapshot\"\n        )\n    return len(times)\n\n\ndef print_event_split(prompts: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Your gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type\n    and over the prompts that hold none.\"\"\"\n    path = Path(os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV])\n    if not path.exists():\n        return\n    view = pd.read_parquet(path)\n    view = view[concerns(view, asset)]\n    scored = prompts[prompts[\"crps\"] > 0]  # -1 marks a prompt the backtester could not score\n    best = scored.groupby([\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])[\"crps\"].min().rename(\"best\")\n    ours = scored[scored[\"miner_id\"] == CANDIDATE_ID].join(best, on=[\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])\n    if ours.empty:\n        return\n    gap = ours[\"crps\"].to_numpy() / ours[\"best\"].to_numpy() - 1\n    starts = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"start_time\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy()\n    ends = starts + np.timedelta64(time_length, \"s\")\n    spans_any = np.zeros(len(ours), dtype=bool)\n    lines = []\n    for event, rows in view.groupby(\"event\"):\n        times = np.sort(pd.to_datetime(rows[\"time_utc\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy())\n        at = np.searchsorted(times, starts)\n        spans = (at < len(times)) & (times[np.minimum(at, len(times) - 1)] < ends)\n        spans_any |= spans\n        if spans.any():\n            lines.append(f\"  {event:<17} {spans.sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[spans].mean():+.2%}\")\n    if not spans_any.all():\n        lines.insert(0, f\"  {'no event':<17} {(~spans_any).sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[~spans_any].mean():+.2%}\")\n    print(\"event split (mean gap to each prompt's best miner):\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, at most the snapshot's last day\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--num-simulations\",\n        type=int,\n        default=1000,\n        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--cadence-minutes\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"answer an even grid every N minutes instead of the validator's own start times (with \"\n        \"--crps-only, 60 for 24h prompts and 10 for 1h by default). A cadence that divides an hour \"\n        \"puts every prompt on the round hour\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--latest-formula\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"score every crypto-1h prompt with the volatility term, as prompts are scored now, \"\n        \"including those scored before it went live. Field ranks before that day then compare \"\n        \"two formulas; CRPS does not\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\n        \"--crps-only\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid: no field and no rank, \"\n        \"on any window of the snapshot. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula\",\n    )\n    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-predictions\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep this run's prediction files\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    if not args.crps_only:\n        require_offline_bundle()\n    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    cadence = args.cadence_minutes\n    if args.crps_only:\n        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]\n    times = prompt_times(args.asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence_minutes=cadence)\n    # the context reaches back CONTEXT_DAYS before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), end, times[0])\n    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"run-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))\n    try:\n        n = generate(\n            args.asset,\n            times,\n            out_dir,\n            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n            time_length=args.time_length,\n            num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n        )\n        print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n        if args.crps_only:\n            result = score_crps(\n                miner_name=\"campaign\",\n                asset=args.asset,\n                time_length=args.time_length,\n                time_increment=args.time_increment,\n                predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            )\n            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)\n            return\n        result = backtest(\n            miner_name=\"campaign\",\n            asset=args.asset,\n            time_length=args.time_length,\n            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n            n_backtest_days=args.days,\n            predictions_dir=out_dir,\n            eval_end=end,\n            latest_formula=args.latest_formula,\n            match_tolerance_minutes=args.cadence_minutes or PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES,\n        )\n        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)\n        if os.environ.get(CALENDAR_ENV):\n            print_event_split(result.prompt_df, args.asset, args.time_length)\n    finally:\n        if args.keep_predictions:\n            print(f\"predictions kept in {out_dir}\")\n        else:\n            shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AhvBMn3Q71fQ6mFyNhPYiF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
