{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-2","id":"msg_011CgwXjVHZguobaHsNJsKWv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The champion is nominated and committed, and the harness interface check passes. I stopped when the landing order arrived at 90 % of credits, with about 14 of the 18 hours unused.\n\n## Champion\n\n`agent/CHAMPION` points to commit `6e3fc56`. A clean export of that commit passes the nomination probe and loads the 31 fitted parameter files; a call takes about 0.5 s (24h) and 0.1 s (1h).\n\nThe model is a seasonal, session-aware stochastic-volatility simulator with every parameter fitted directly on the validator's CRPS. It serves stratified paths, matched to a larger reference sample and snapped to the venue's tick grid.\n\n## Measured results\n\nOfficial scorer, 1000 paths, validator prompts scored 2026-10-08 → 2026-11-07. The served parameters were fitted on data before 2026-10-01, so this window is out of sample for them.\n\n| Configuration | Starter | Champion | Change | vs best miner | vs median miner |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CRYPTO_24H | 3785.58 | 3663.19 | −3.23 % | −0.02 % | −0.26 % |\n| COM_EQU_24H | 1988.95 | 1799.38 | −9.53 % | −0.01 % | −0.72 % |\n| CRYPTO_1H | 833.37 | 791.12 | −5.07 % | −0.06 % | −0.33 % |\n\nThe last two columns compare mean CRPS with each miner on the prompts both answered. Over the slightly longer 36-day run (2026-10-02 → 2026-11-07, quantile matching off) the model ranks first on BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, XAU, NVDAX, TSLAX and SP500 at 24h, and on BTC, ETH, SOL and XRP at 1h.\n\n## What is weak or unverified\n\n- **Margins over the best miner are a few hundredths of a percent.** On the last 12 days alone, against the five miners that turned out best there, the model is 0.2–0.3 % behind on crypto.\n- **WTIOIL and HYPE are weak.** WTIOIL ranks 191/231 and loses about 0.5 % to the median miner on ordinary prompts, unexplained. HYPE is mid-field (85/231 at 24h, 31/223 at 1h).\n- **The served parameters are five weeks older than the cutoff.** A refit through 2026-11-08 was training when the landing order came; I stopped it rather than serve something unvalidated. An earlier comparison suggests the refit would help SPCX, SP500, XAU and WTIOIL.\n- **Some planned work never ran:** two of the four component ablations, a learned network for the volatility level, and volume features.\n\n## Housekeeping\n\n- **Budget:** ten-minute sleeps let the prompt cache expire, so the later turns cost several times more than the early ones.\n- **`BUDGET.md`:** a broad `git add` of mine committed a snapshot of the harness-owned file once; I removed it from tracking (the file itself is untouched) and noted it in `suggestions.md`.\n\nDeliverables are in `agent/`: `CHAMPION`, `report.md`, `journal.md`, `suggestions.md`, with the model in `modeling.py`, `core.py` and `params/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2099,"cache_read_input_tokens":512475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2099,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":841,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"9931998f-6841-443b-80b9-97ad6a036cef","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:25:10.353Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[The agent may stop only in one of three cases. (1) A LANDING ORDER has arrived, printed from agent/BUDGET.md or sent by the harness, and the agent's command output shows it carried out: agent/journal.md finalized, agent/report.md written, agent/CHAMPION written, `git cat-file -t` on its sha printing `commit`, and `git status --short` printing nothing after the last commit. (2) The same deliverables, committed and verified the same way, alongside journal entries whose measured CRPS shows that further iteration would not improve the champion. (3) `background_tasks` in the arguments lists a running workflow or subagent: the session waits for that work, and its result starts the next turn. A plan, a claim, or a CHAMPION file alone is not enough.]: Case 1 applies in part: the landing order was printed from agent/BUDGET.md (\"## LANDING ORDER — NON-NEGOTIABLE\"), and the journal, report and CHAMPION were written and committed (\"1b92cb7 Stop tracking the harness-owned BUDGET.md; correct the note about it\"). Two required verifications are missing from the command output. First, `git cat-file -t` was never run on the CHAMPION sha 6e3fc56c96fde4abf279d4b25acb9c0e3ef4f4a5; only `git rev-parse`, `git ls-tree` and `git archive` were used, so nothing prints `commit`. Second, the last `git status --short` after the final commit printed \"?? agent/BUDGET.md\" rather than nothing. Case 2 needs the same verification, and the journal says a refit \"would help SPCX, SP500, XAU and WTIOIL\", so it does not show further iteration is futile. Case 3 fails because background_tasks is []."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5de06de-0f9b-444f-a451-a2a51a4613ad","uuid":"74149667-aacb-4fb8-b18c-e898057da7d1","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:25:29.008Z","isSynthetic":true}
